`attachCommand('sk-doc', <single sk-create-skill route>, prompt)` imported from `lib/command-attach.ts`, with five prompts that ask for a skill called invoice-parser and end in a no-edit request.\n182:- What should happen: all five match and attach nothing. `scorer/text.ts:148` holds a third copy of the same wording (`isReadOnlyExplainer`), so it misses the same four.\n184:- Test: in `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, each of the four wordings returns `/create:skill` today and `undefined` after. `isReadOnlyExplainer` gets the same four cases.\n227:- **SA2-P2-001** `:120` asks for mode `sk-create-benchmark` with the `INJECTED` table, which has no row for it. So the call returns `undefined` at the table lookup, before any gate (probe: `undefined` for a plain and an effort prompt). `:121` already proves that a hub other than deep-loop answers with its command. The lineage's fix, adding the mode to `INJECTED`, would turn `:120` red. Test: none can fail, because the defect is a misleading assertion.\n228:- **SA2-P2-003** The case at `:493` stores no prompt text, then asserts that status shows none. Status carries aggregates only (`advisor-status.ts:501-510`), so the assertion cannot fail. ADJUSTED because no leak path exists today. The guard only lacks a target. Test: persist a debug record holding a marker and assert the marker is absent. It passes today and would catch a future leak.\n229:- **SA2-P2-004** `CommandRow` (`command-attach.ts:48-53`) carries `mutating`, which the renderer reads. The README sentence at `:50` names the command, its policy and the owning skill only. Test: a doc check that the README names every `CommandRow` field fails today.\n230:- **SA2-P2-005** `tsString` (`:957-959`) escapes the backslash and the single quote only. A value holding a line break would emit an unterminated literal. It is latent: 0 of the 1683 strings in `command-bridges.generated.json` hold U+000A, U+000D, U+2028 or U+2029. Test: export `tsString` beside the exports at `:1396` and assert that the literal it emits for a value with each break holds no raw break. It fails today.\n236:- **iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report** The header (`:5-8`) promises the `COMMAND:` lines, the reads and writes in order and the init check. The CLI prints per-arm counts and verdicts, not an ordered list. Test: none, the fix is a comment.\n259:| scorer-attach | 5 | 5 | 0 | scorer-attach-2. Rerun here: `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` 14 passed and `command-attach.vitest.ts` 10 passed, both exit 0 |\n260:| render-hooks-plugin | 12 | 12 | 0 | render-hooks-plugin-2. Its report says eleven of twelve hold and counts the refuted pass-one finding as the twelfth, under the wrong id `R3-P2-002--16e5737e0e56`. This synthesis counts twelve fixable items plus that refuted one. Rerun here: `subprocess-output-cap.vitest.ts` 2 passed, exit 0 |\n265:Two fixes hold for the case pass one named but carry a related new defect. DR2-P2-007 is the A10 count beside the pass-one fix for DR3-P2-001. DR2-P2-006 is the setup text beside the pass-one fix for Q3.\n273:1. **WG1 Attach-path no-edit guard and bridge text (safety lane).** SA2-P2-002, SA2-P2-003, SA2-P2-001, SA2-P2-004 and SA2-P2-005. Files: `command-attach.ts`, `scorer/text.ts`, `command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `command-attach.vitest.ts`, `handlers/advisor-status.vitest.ts`, `derive-command-bridges.cjs`, `command-bridges/README.md` and a new `derive-command-bridges-strings.vitest.ts`. `scorer/text.ts` imports `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` from the import-free `command-attach.ts`, as `fusion.ts:20` already does. `fusion.ts` itself is not edited. Run the deriver's check mode after, which must print `\"changed\": []`.\n276:4. **WG4 Routing-accuracy README and transcript scorer.** iter4-P2-row-id-session-mode and iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report. Files: `routing-accuracy/README.md`, `score-command-transcripts.mjs` and `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts`. This group also writes the README lines for WG2 and WG3: `untrusted_checkout` in the backfill refusal list near `:75-77`, the `fixture` field, the g2 arm rule with `mixed_row_arms` and the cost script clearing `AI_SESSION_CHILD` near `:95-97`.\n308:5. Phase 016 interplay, read from its draft at the time of this synthesis: it writes `scorer/fusion.ts` and `AGENTS.md` line 65, which no group here writes. Its boundary task T015 requires `_routes.yaml` unchanged against HEAD, so WG8 is committed before T015 runs or is built after phase 016. Its doctor gate runs every doctor test, so WG8 and WG9 must leave `fail 0`.\n319:| `spec_code` | partial | Thirteen findings are docs, comments or contracts that disagree with code: SA2-P2-004, iter4-P2-row-id-session-mode, iter5-P2-scorer-header-ordered-report, iter4-P2-playbook-inventory-note, iter4-P2-playbook-persistence-path, iter4-P2-tests-readme-description, iter2-P2-inert-bounded-summary-option, iter4-P2-advisor-recommend-stale-line-refs, DR2-P2-004, DR2-P2-006, DR2-P2-008, iter2-P2-capture-env-not-restored (its header promise) and SA2-P2-001 (its comment). The lineages scored this row pass in three areas and partial in scorer-attach. |\n328:| `agent_cross_runtime` | partial | render-hooks-plugin-2 and doctor-install-2 scored pass. scorer-attach-2 and accuracy-runner-2 scored partial, because live per-runtime proof belongs to phase 007's final arm after the merge. accuracy-runner-2 records `live_turn_execution_evidence` as blocked. |\n329:| `feature_catalog_code` | partial | `advisor-recommend.md` matches the code in substance but six line citations are stale. scorer-attach-2 found `command-meaning-matching.md` matching on every checked claim. |\n339:- **`run` commands that write (pass one).** `/doctor:deep-loop` and `/doctor:speckit` are `run` with class `add-only`. Whether that is intended is still a decision, not a fix. scorer-attach-2 lists it the same way.\n343:- **Third no-edit pattern (pass one).** `scorer/text.ts:148` is now part of SA2-P2-002's fix in WG1.\n364:| scorer-attach-2 | 0 | 0 | 0