{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794669605922,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"id":"prt_1daa4f422001ftvbFXecM45WVu","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1daa4e677001Z1fS9JyKQdiCIf","type":"step-start","snapshot":"316b21fa9a16aa551645f4b6ba92d169b60ee0b6"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669609057,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa5001d001ckNQKlfFQ2SQ6i","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1daa4e677001Z1fS9JyKQdiCIf","type":"tool","id":"call_01_8x3fu0z4a0de2pflxuiuom4o","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"typo\\|small edit\\|correction\\|refus\\|question\\|mention\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md | head -40"},"output":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:36:A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandMeaningEligible` asks the question that floor asks of a phrase match. A prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, such as \"no edits\", \"do not change\", \"just show\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only explainer prompt admits only a command marked `readOnly`, because running it is the answer. `readOnlyRouteAllowed` reads the same pattern, so the two gates cannot drift apart.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:44:`capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --real-embedding` scores the command corpus against this machine's skill graph and live embedder. It first checks that the embedder serves `nomic-embed-text` and that a `vec_cmd_*` table holds vectors, and it refuses `--write`. The committed baseline still comes from the fixture run, which has no real cosine.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:65:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Vitest | 17 cases: cosine bar, margin, stand-in refusal, eligibility and ranking rule |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:31:A doctor bridge passes on its own wording, an explicit-author match on one of its manifest phrases or its runnable string. With the local embedder running it can also pass on meaning, as [command-meaning-matching.md](./command-meaning-matching.md) describes. When none passes and none was typed, the scorer asks `/doctor:helper`'s ranker whether the prompt describes a doctor problem, and if it does the command the ranker puts first passes by name when its policy is `run`, and `/doctor:helper` passes instead when that command asks first or has no bridge. A prompt that asks for a `repair path` or says `I have a problem`, with no ranked command and no passing skill, gets `/doctor:helper`. `stopped converging` counts as a wrong state beside a passing skill. Beside a passing skill this needs a wrong state or health check in the prompt, so ordinary requests that share doctor words get no doctor line. A `/doctor:` command counts as typed when the prompt starts with `/doctor:` or when it directly follows `run`, `execute`, `start`, `launch`, `use` or `kick off` outside quotes and backticks. A quoted command or a bare mid-sentence mention does not count. A typed command puts its own passing bridge first. For other prompts, a passing skill stays first and passing doctor bridges sit right after the second passing skill or the only passing skill. This keeps a doctor line within the CLI's three shown results. Doctor bridges never change skill scores. The scorer computes skill ambiguity and abstention as if no doctor bridge existed. The Python native wrapper keeps the same order. A read-only question, such as a list or show prompt, holds every candidate under the read-only confidence floor, unless the prompt names the skill, a command bridge marked `readOnly` matches one of its own phrases, or a skill-specific rule lifts it. A prompt with a no-write phrase, such as `no edits` or `just list`, gets none of these lifts. Mutating bridges stay gated.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:36:A meaning pass lifts a command past the read-only confidence floor, so `commandMeaningEligible` asks the question that floor asks of a phrase match. A prompt matching `NO_EDIT_REQUEST`, such as \"no edits\", \"do not change\", \"just show\" or \"just list\", rules out every command on meaning. A read-only explainer prompt admits only a command marked `readOnly`, because running it is the answer. `readOnlyRouteAllowed` reads the same pattern, so the two gates cannot drift apart.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:44:`capture-command-routing-baseline.mjs --real-embedding` scores the command corpus against this machine's skill graph and live embedder. It first checks that the embedder serves `nomic-embed-text` and that a `vec_cmd_*` table holds vectors, and it refuses `--write`. The committed baseline still comes from the fixture run, which has no real cosine.\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:65:| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Vitest | 17 cases: cosine bar, margin, stand-in refusal, eligibility and ranking rule |\n.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md:31:A doctor bridge passes on its own wording, an explicit-author match on one of its manifest phrases or its runnable string. With the local embedder running it can also pass on meaning, as [command-meaning-matching.md](./command-meaning-matching.md) describes. When none passes and none was typed, the scorer asks `/doctor:helper`'s ranker whether the prompt describes a doctor problem, and if it does the command the ranker puts first passes by name when its policy is `run`, and `/doctor:helper` passes instead when that command asks first or has no bridge. A prompt that asks for a `repair path` or says `I have a problem`, with no ranked command and no passing skill, gets `/doctor:helper`. `stopped converging` counts as a wrong state beside a passing skill. Beside a passing skill this needs a wrong state or health check in the prompt, so ordinary requests that share doctor words get no doctor line. A `/doctor:` command counts as typed when the prompt starts with `/doctor:` or when it directly follows `run`, `execute`, `start`, `launch`, `use` or `kick off` outside quotes and backticks. A quoted command or a bare mid-sentence mention does not count. A typed command puts its own passing bridge first. For other prompts, a passing skill stays first and passing doctor bridges sit right after the second passing skill or the only passing skill. This keeps a doctor line within the CLI's three shown results. Doctor bridges never change skill scores. The scorer computes skill ambiguity and abstention as if no doctor bridge existed. The Python native wrapper keeps the same order. A read-only question, such as a list or show prompt, holds every candidate under the read-only confidence floor, unless the prompt names the skill, a command bridge marked `readOnly` matches one of its own phrases, or a skill-specific rule lifts it. A prompt with a no-write phrase, such as `no edits` or `just list`, gets none of these lifts. Mutating bridges stay gated.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"grep -rn \\\"typo\\\\|small edit\\\\|correction\\\\|refus\\\\|question\\\\|mention\\\" .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669608989,"end":1794669609057}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669609072,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa50006001THgmzjEAe2ImZW","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1daa4e677001Z1fS9JyKQdiCIf","type":"tool","id":"call_00_g9bsto6tyud3s9jczn6ira81","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -rn \"typo\\|small edit\\|correction\\|refus\\|question\\|mention\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/*.md | head -60"},"output":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:22:    open_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:23:    answered_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:41:| Q005 | Run the Fable reviewer through the Claude Code CLI after the subagent hook refused it. | Not stated. | None | 007 research/synthesis-review.md |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:56:| Q020 | Close phase 003 with its holdout plain-recall miss accepted on the terms phase 004 recorded. | Asked on the wrong premise that the holdout row was the only unmet one. The corrected question followed the same day. | None | 003-plain-chat-command-reach decision-record.md ADR-016, AC-007 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:80:| Q044 | No design was chosen: the operator asked whether commands were already symlinked across the CLIs, which led to the next question. | Not stated. | None | 016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default lane A |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:83:| Q047 | No design was chosen: the operator pointed at the file name skill.md and proposed sk-skill, which led to the rename question. | Not stated. | None | 016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default lane A |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:84:| Q048 | No option was chosen: the operator asked to check that the name is correct, that Skilled commands use it and whether Claude Code has a bug, which the next question answered. | Not stated. | None | 016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default lane A |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:100:| Q064 | Before choosing the arm size, the operator asked for the token usage per CLI. It was measured from the 144 stored sessions of the last arm and put in the Q063 question. | Not stated. | None | goal.md log |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:559:Correction first: I told you phase 003 (plain-chat command reach) was open only because of its holdout row. That was wrong. It has eight more unmet criteria, and I re-measured them today. Three are still fixable: one typed command (/create:agent) still ties with its own skill, four old spec-kit ids still sit in the Python compatibility list, and the prompt 'show me which packets mention the token cap' still reaches no command. Three are doctor rows whose phrases were reverted, where phase 004 now reaches 3 of 17 tune and 2 of 17 held-out doctor prompts with real embeddings. One is a one-time measurement-order miss. One asks you to judge that the doctor-only phrase gate was widened to every command. I recorded your holdout waiver and left the phase In Progress. How should phase 003 close?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:619:Phase 005, question 2 of 4. When the advisor daemon is down, the hook falls back to a simpler Python scorer (the degraded path). What may the brief show about commands in that state?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:639:Phase 005, question 3 of 4. /doctor:update has six actions with different risk (check runs, others ask or start). When the advisor surfaces /doctor:update without naming an action, which policy word should the brief print?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:678:Phase 006, question 2 of 4. A dispatched worker session (a child, such as a DeepSeek worker through Pi) also gets an advisor brief. How should a child see a surfaced command? A child that starts /speckit:plan on its own would act outside its brief.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:698:Phase 006, question 4 of 4. The advisor's runtime list still contains 'copilot', which Skilled no longer supports. Stored metrics records and tool input are validated against that list.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:738:Phase 007, question 2 of 4. The 'before' measurement must describe behaviour without the new brief and Gate 2 rule. When should it run? It has to happen before phase 005's code lands, or in a checkout of the older code.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:758:Phase 007, question 3 of 4. To measure what a real chat user gets, the test sessions must start like a normal session and not as a marked child session. Two dispatch rules stand in the way: the OpenCode contract wants the child marker set, and the Claude Code contract forbids starting Claude Code from inside Claude Code. May the behaviour runs start each CLI like a chat user?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:777:Phase 007, question 4 of 4. The research proposed a wording check on doctor lead phrases that would remove the phrase 'disable comment hygiene gate', which today leads with /doctor:git hooks. A pinned doctor test expects that command first. What should happen?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:817:Phase 008, question 2 of 4. After the user says yes, may Skilled's doctor route itself start the Ollama server and pull the model, or should it only print the commands?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:837:Phase 008, question 3 of 4. Today the advisor says nothing when meaning matching is off. Where should the user see it?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:857:Phase 008, question 4 of 4. How long may the advisor wait for the embedding of a prompt before it gives up and matches on phrases only? Today the adapter waits up to 5000 ms while the hook gives up at 2500 ms, so a hung server costs the whole brief. A cold model load took about 275 ms here.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:877:One routing miss surfaced when I rebased onto main. The prompt 'fix the typo in the heading of the setup guide' should go to sk-doc. It ties three skills at the same score and sk-doc is not among the winners: before the rebase sk-code came first, now system-skilled-doctor does. No command is offered and no metric moved, so I re-captured the baseline to keep the suite green. It was a miss before this work too. What should happen with it?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1361:| P010 | A run on an ask row that asked and wrote nothing counts in the new `followedRate` and never in `loadRate`. | The ask policy tells the model to offer the command in one question and wait, so asking is the policy's own step. A reader who disagrees still has the unchanged load rate. | Yes | 022 spec, Open Questions |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1366:| P015 | The OpenCode plugin sends `compiledRouteTopOnly`, the request option every hook already sends. This reverses the 021 line that left the plugin's request shape out of scope. | The head-row fix does not reach the partner of an ambiguous head: four probe prompts printed a partner with a command on OpenCode and none on Claude, or the reverse. One option that already exists makes both paths ask the same question. | Yes | 021 tasks T014, 021 goal D1 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1368:| P017 | The small-edit gate covers correction wording only. An edit that names no correction word, an app problem that scores above the doctor bar and a no-change wording the no-edit pattern does not hold are named as classes and not planned. | Each reproduced by a probe. Telling an edit from a request to write a document, or a foreign project from the toolkit, needs the matching change the operator logged for a follow-up, and widening a word list to move the probes would be tuning on them. | Yes | 020 spec, Out of Scope |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1371:| P020 | Phase 020 recaptures `command-routing-baseline.json`, a committed baseline its scope boundary left out. Taken by the coordinator at the phase gate. | The slice test failed only on rows sv-09, sv-11 and sv-12, each a question about a command, which this phase stops offering a command on by design. The full suite cannot reach 0 failed without the recapture, and no other row moved. | Yes | 020 `scratch/after.txt`, `implementation-summary.md` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1373:| P022 | The mention reader ends a sentence only at `.`, `!` or a line break. `quick question? is /speckit:resume safe to run twice` and `ok, is /speckit:plan enough here` read as requests. Taken by the coordinator. | Both follow the sentence-end set the task named, and the Opus check found no case the change broke. Adding `?` and `,` would be a new rule with no reproduction from real use. | Yes, with a real prompt that reproduces it | 020 `tasks.md` T028 evidence |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1375:| P024 | A question mark ends a sentence in the mention reader, so a bare ask word that follows one opens a question about the command. This supersedes P022 for the question mark. A comma stays out of the sentence-start set. Taken by the dispatched planner that wrote phases 024 and 025 after the Fable 5.2 review of 2026-11-14, as are P025 to P031. | The review reproduced it: `quick question? is /speckit:resume safe to run twice` returned `/speckit:resume` (start), and the planning probe printed `shipped=false` for it. A question mark ends a sentence in any grammar, so the edit is no tuning, and the guard `is this right? run /speckit:plan` stays a request. P022's own condition was a prompt that reproduces it. A comma ends a clause, and no prompt reproduced the comma form. | Yes | 024 tasks T008, 024 `scratch/planning/probe-mention-reader.before.txt` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1377:| P026 | Rows sv-09, sv-11 and sv-12 keep their `expected_command`. No build task relabels them. The routing-accuracy README states the three designed withholds, and the relabel waits on the operator with options and a recommendation. | The capture counts a slash-variant row with no expected command as a row that must stay silent, so a relabel moves the false-offer floor from 0 of 35 to 0 of 38, and completion criterion 2 quotes 35. That criterion is the operator's. A relabel would also file a full command name under partial mentions, a different class, while phase 023 counts questions about a command on sealed `decline` rows. Consumers checked: the capture and its committed baseline, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`, the transcript scorer's row labels, the behaviour runner, `measure-brief-cost.mjs` and two handler and scorer tests. | Waits on the operator | 024 spec, Open Questions and mechanism table |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1380:| P029 | The Codex reader keeps the body of a custom tool call as `arguments.input` and the transcript scorer reads the shell commands out of it. One `exec` call stays one shell step whose command holds its `cmd` strings one per line. | The reader is shared with the history lookup, four hooks and one plugin, whose contract calls tool arguments opaque, so the record keeps its shape and gains one key. What counts as a command is the scorer's question. One step per call keeps the change to one helper and one call, at the cost that a body holding a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step, which the README states. | Yes | 024 tasks T009 and T011, 024 plan, affected surfaces |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:25:    open_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:26:    answered_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:155:| Operator chat instruction, 2026-11-13 04:30Z | Recorded here | 'In rease parallelism' (verbatim, typo is the operator's): run file-disjoint work side by side, several workers per wave. It has no sweep key, because it answered no question, so the save path cannot write it to a decision record |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:167:| Phase 015 health default and brief refinements | Complete, committed (see git log) | Builds segment three ranks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 9 and 11. 20 planned tasks verified 20 of 20 PASS by three Opus verifiers, five follow-ups checked by the coordinator. Suite 183 files 1755 passed 0 failed, floors unchanged, strict PASSED. Open: live brief cost not measured, the script refused with degraded_brief |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:170:| Operator amendment to D1, 2026-11-13 | Operator-made | 'use ask question tool for any decisions needed': decisions that are the operator's are now asked through the question tool, no longer taken alone |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:171:| Operator answers, 2026-11-13 (question tool) | Decided by the operator | Rank 7: build the Claude-only create skill and managed .claude/skills tree. Rank 12: keep typed only on the degraded brief (Q026 stands), declined. Rank 13: offer /doctor:helper on an ambiguous doctor prompt. R4-P2-003: yes, edit the AGENTS.md Gate 2 direct-call example to the stdin form. The three builds become phase 016 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:177:| Operator answers, 2026-11-13 third round (question tool) | Decided by the operator | Codex: approve the hooks for one arena and run one Codex-only arm, which reverses no more arms for Codex alone. Gate 2 clause for a skill-only brief: declined, Gate 2 stays as approved. Write discipline on Devin and OpenCode: tracked for a separate packet. Holdout row suppressed-codex-abstain: retire it in this packet, as a new phase 018 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:178:| Operator answers, 2026-11-13 fourth round (question tool) | Decided by the operator | Phase 018 retires only suppressed-codex-abstain. The two short sealed rows that hit data files (P1-ABSTAIN-001, P1-PHRASE-001) and the six sealed rows that hit hand-written scorer rules only are an advisory for a separate decision. The final hand-over of this branch reaches main through a pull request, not a direct push |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:181:| Operator instruction, 2026-11-13 17:00Z | Operator-made, amends D4 | Verbatim: Use fable 5.2 medium through claude 2 for critical thinking / hard questions but dont ket it implement or use subagents. claude2 is the operator zsh function for the second Claude account. It is used read-only for judgment questions, never to edit and never with subagents |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:184:| Phase 009 research | Complete, decided without the operato... | Segment one ranks 7 and 11 and three guards of rank 14 declined with reasons in 009 tasks.md, rank 8 reason restated on Q053 and Q057, question 4 carried to the Codex-only arm. Each reason was checked read-only by Fable 5.2 medium on the second Claude account, which corrected three of them. Strict PASSED, 0 errors, 1 SOURCE_TAGS warning on lineage files |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:189:| WAITING ON OPERATOR: Codex-only behaviour arm | Waiting | Approved by the operator (Q052) and needs the operator to open Codex in a prepared arena, run /hooks and approve each entry. Phase 007 closes without it, decided without the operator (D1): the summary already prints codex 0 of 12 before and after with no brief delivered. Research question 4 is carried to this arm |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:191:| Conflict named: D1 against the logged amendment | Resolved toward the session goal | The goal the operator set for this session on 2026-11-13 states D1 as ask the operator nothing. The log row of the same day amends D1 to ask through the question tool. This session followed the goal as set and took each decision itself, recording it as decided without the operator, so each one stays open for the operator to overturn |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:202:| Outcome measure for the core need | Proposed, waits on the operator | The packet counts offers and starts. It has no number for how often a model followed a real workflow, the command's or the skill's own, against improvising. Recorded as an open question in the parent spec. Building it and setting a target is the operator's decision |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:207:| Peer session question on the routing corpus pin, 2026-11-13 | Answered not yet | The archive subtrack session will fix the Routing Registry Drift Guard on main. This branch removes one holdout row (phase 018) that reaches main only with the pull request, so a pin recaptured before the merge goes red again. Who recaptures the pin is the operator's call |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:210:| Routing corpus pin recapture, operator-confirmed 2026-11-13 (question tool) | Done, commit 0238274ed8, not pushed | The operator chose this branch to recapture routing-baseline.json in system-deep-loop 013-drift-guard-repairs. All three corpus hashes repinned, four captures retaken, the workflow's pin check prints corpus matches the pinned baseline hashes and the scoring gate passes at its floors in the CI regime (accuracy 0.5795, TT 110, FT 3, FF 1). The peer session that asked could not be told: its socket... |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:215:| Operator answers, 2026-11-13 fifth round (question tool) | Decided by the operator | Release note: amend v4.0.2.1 on the branch, no new version. Outcome measure for the core need: build now as phase 019 from the stored final-arm sessions. Typed /create:skill: the advisor points it at /create:sk-skill. Cleanup: delete the nested repository and the 34 GB behaviour arenas, the arenas after the measure is scored |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:221:| Merge of origin/main 4f57ea6ac8 and of worktrees/372-hub-vocabulary-drift | Done, commits 8390d86ca9 and 2276ba13... | Operator approved the 372 merge through the question tool on 2026-11-14 after the peer session asked. Tag pre-merge-352b marks 3a91e4ab61. Only the trigger index and its three fixtures conflicted, rebuilt by generate-trigger-index.mjs with --check exit 0. The commit gate raised sk-doc ROUTER.md to 2.4.8.0 and re-minted both hub manifests. Skill graph freshness strict exit 0, bridges fresh, 0 be... |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:224:| Fable 5.2 alignment reviews, 2026-11-14 | Done, verdicts DRIFTING and not ready... | Operator asked for two fresh Fable 5.2 medium reviews on the second Claude account, read-only, no subagents. Code lens: 5 P1, 7 P2. Purpose lens: DRIFTING, 4 P1, 7 P2. Both found the phase 019 share drops runs that wrote nothing: 9 of Claude's 10 such final-arm runs ran shell steps without a load. Reproduced by the coordinator: refusal and question prompts get a start command, app problems get... |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:242:| Phase 020 command offer fit guards closed | Done, not committed yet | Probe offers 26 to 8, suite 1919 passed 0 failed, five floors and eval equal. Real sealed plain 5 to 4 of 44, cause the uncertainty bar (P021). Slice baseline recaptured for three question rows (P020). Two doctor cases out of scope, scores 10.009 and 9.761. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:245:| Phase 020 test-first check rerun | Holds, no correction | Parsing the shell tool events of each worker log shows a failing vitest run before the passing one for each of T003 to T010 and T017, for example T003 24 failed then 62 passed, T007 1 failed then 20 passed. The earlier finding that only T007 had one came from a grep over the whole log, which matched quoted task text |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:252:| Remediation plan for the 11:40 review, 2026-11-14 | Planning, Fable 5.2 medium on claude2 | Phase 024 review remediation (Codex shell text in the session reader, refusal wording, question mark as a sentence end superseding P022, offeredAs read by the scorer, the rest of the shell-read rule, sv-09 to sv-12 labels, the two skillLabel fallbacks) and phase 025 release notes and doc sync. Brief and report in review/fable-review-2026-11-14-1140/ |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:253:| Phases 024 and 025 planned, 2026-11-14 | Planned, not built | 024: 23 tasks, lanes A and R first, lane S after phases 022 and 023 close. 025: 18 tasks, after 019 to 024 close. Probes in 024 scratch/planning: Codex shell events with no command text 58 of 58, mention reader 40 of 46 shipped and 46 of 46 planned, shell-read edits 18 of 18. Both validate strict. Decisions P024 to P031 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:22:    open_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:23:    answered_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:139:| 20 | 020-command-offer-fit-guards/ | Keep the model's free choice where no command fits: a command the prompt only mentions, refuses or asks about is not offered, a no-edit request and a correction inside an existing document carry no writing command and a weak doctor cue needs the stronger bar, each reproduced by a probe that printed 26 command heads on 26 such prompts (alignment reviews of 2026-11-14, findings A-4, A-5, A-6, A-8, B-3 and B-9) | Complete |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:143:| 24 | 024-fable-review-remediation/ | The fixes for the Fable 5.2 review of 2026-11-14: the Codex session reader keeps the body of a custom tool call and the transcript scorer reads its shell commands, so a Codex run can show a load, the mention reader reads `no need to run` and `stop using` as refusals, keeps the command on `why not use` and on a later `run it` and ends a sentence at a question mark, a search and a heredoc line are no load, a `cd` inside one command is followed and a command on the partner side is not counted as offered, with both stored arms rescored and the Codex start rate restated. The relabel of three slash-variant rows waits on the operator and three carry items are declined on their probes (findings 1, 4, 5, 6 and 7, decision P024) | Complete |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:168:| 015-health-default-and-brief-refinements | 016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default | Phase 015 is committed, every pinned floor holds and the operator has answered the rename, doctor cue and changelog questions | `git log -1 --format=%h -- 015-health-default-and-brief-refinements` prints `3b48f0e5f1` or later and phase 016 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:171:| 018-holdout-row-retirement | 019-workflow-outcome-measure | Phase 018 is committed, every pinned floor holds on the tree merged with `origin/main` and the operator has chosen to build the measure now (question tool, 2026-11-13) | The transcript scorer tests report 0 failed, the two summary runs write a per-runtime share for the before arm and the final arm, and phase 019 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:182:<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:195:- Rows sv-09, sv-11 and sv-12 of the command corpus name a command inside a question and still carry `expected_command`, so the committed baseline records three designed withholds as misses. A relabel to no command moves them into the false-offer tally, and the floor in completion criterion 2 would read 0 of 38 where it says 0 of 35. The relabel waits on the operator. The options and a recommendation are in the phase 024 spec (P026).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:198:<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:22:    open_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:23:    answered_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:41:| Q005 | Run the Fable reviewer through the Claude Code CLI after the subagent hook refused it. | Not stated. | None | 007 research/synthesis-review.md |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:56:| Q020 | Close phase 003 with its holdout plain-recall miss accepted on the terms phase 004 recorded. | Asked on the wrong premise that the holdout row was the only unmet one. The corrected question followed the same day. | None | 003-plain-chat-command-reach decision-record.md ADR-016, AC-007 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:80:| Q044 | No design was chosen: the operator asked whether commands were already symlinked across the CLIs, which led to the next question. | Not stated. | None | 016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default lane A |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:83:| Q047 | No design was chosen: the operator pointed at the file name skill.md and proposed sk-skill, which led to the rename question. | Not stated. | None | 016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default lane A |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:84:| Q048 | No option was chosen: the operator asked to check that the name is correct, that Skilled commands use it and whether Claude Code has a bug, which the next question answered. | Not stated. | None | 016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default lane A |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:100:| Q064 | Before choosing the arm size, the operator asked for the token usage per CLI. It was measured from the 144 stored sessions of the last arm and put in the Q063 question. | Not stated. | None | goal.md log |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:559:Correction first: I told you phase 003 (plain-chat command reach) was open only because of its holdout row. That was wrong. It has eight more unmet criteria, and I re-measured them today. Three are still fixable: one typed command (/create:agent) still ties with its own skill, four old spec-kit ids still sit in the Python compatibility list, and the prompt 'show me which packets mention the token cap' still reaches no command. Three are doctor rows whose phrases were reverted, where phase 004 now reaches 3 of 17 tune and 2 of 17 held-out doctor prompts with real embeddings. One is a one-time measurement-order miss. One asks you to judge that the doctor-only phrase gate was widened to every command. I recorded your holdout waiver and left the phase In Progress. How should phase 003 close?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:619:Phase 005, question 2 of 4. When the advisor daemon is down, the hook falls back to a simpler Python scorer (the degraded path). What may the brief show about commands in that state?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:639:Phase 005, question 3 of 4. /doctor:update has six actions with different risk (check runs, others ask or start). When the advisor surfaces /doctor:update without naming an action, which policy word should the brief print?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:678:Phase 006, question 2 of 4. A dispatched worker session (a child, such as a DeepSeek worker through Pi) also gets an advisor brief. How should a child see a surfaced command? A child that starts /speckit:plan on its own would act outside its brief.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:698:Phase 006, question 4 of 4. The advisor's runtime list still contains 'copilot', which Skilled no longer supports. Stored metrics records and tool input are validated against that list.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:738:Phase 007, question 2 of 4. The 'before' measurement must describe behaviour without the new brief and Gate 2 rule. When should it run? It has to happen before phase 005's code lands, or in a checkout of the older code.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:758:Phase 007, question 3 of 4. To measure what a real chat user gets, the test sessions must start like a normal session and not as a marked child session. Two dispatch rules stand in the way: the OpenCode contract wants the child marker set, and the Claude Code contract forbids starting Claude Code from inside Claude Code. May the behaviour runs start each CLI like a chat user?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:777:Phase 007, question 4 of 4. The research proposed a wording check on doctor lead phrases that would remove the phrase 'disable comment hygiene gate', which today leads with /doctor:git hooks. A pinned doctor test expects that command first. What should happen?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:817:Phase 008, question 2 of 4. After the user says yes, may Skilled's doctor route itself start the Ollama server and pull the model, or should it only print the commands?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:837:Phase 008, question 3 of 4. Today the advisor says nothing when meaning matching is off. Where should the user see it?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:857:Phase 008, question 4 of 4. How long may the advisor wait for the embedding of a prompt before it gives up and matches on phrases only? Today the adapter waits up to 5000 ms while the hook gives up at 2500 ms, so a hung server costs the whole brief. A cold model load took about 275 ms here.\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:877:One routing miss surfaced when I rebased onto main. The prompt 'fix the typo in the heading of the setup guide' should go to sk-doc. It ties three skills at the same score and sk-doc is not among the winners: before the rebase sk-code came first, now system-skilled-doctor does. No command is offered and no metric moved, so I re-captured the baseline to keep the suite green. It was a miss before this work too. What should happen with it?\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1361:| P010 | A run on an ask row that asked and wrote nothing counts in the new `followedRate` and never in `loadRate`. | The ask policy tells the model to offer the command in one question and wait, so asking is the policy's own step. A reader who disagrees still has the unchanged load rate. | Yes | 022 spec, Open Questions |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1366:| P015 | The OpenCode plugin sends `compiledRouteTopOnly`, the request option every hook already sends. This reverses the 021 line that left the plugin's request shape out of scope. | The head-row fix does not reach the partner of an ambiguous head: four probe prompts printed a partner with a command on OpenCode and none on Claude, or the reverse. One option that already exists makes both paths ask the same question. | Yes | 021 tasks T014, 021 goal D1 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1368:| P017 | The small-edit gate covers correction wording only. An edit that names no correction word, an app problem that scores above the doctor bar and a no-change wording the no-edit pattern does not hold are named as classes and not planned. | Each reproduced by a probe. Telling an edit from a request to write a document, or a foreign project from the toolkit, needs the matching change the operator logged for a follow-up, and widening a word list to move the probes would be tuning on them. | Yes | 020 spec, Out of Scope |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1371:| P020 | Phase 020 recaptures `command-routing-baseline.json`, a committed baseline its scope boundary left out. Taken by the coordinator at the phase gate. | The slice test failed only on rows sv-09, sv-11 and sv-12, each a question about a command, which this phase stops offering a command on by design. The full suite cannot reach 0 failed without the recapture, and no other row moved. | Yes | 020 `scratch/after.txt`, `implementation-summary.md` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1373:| P022 | The mention reader ends a sentence only at `.`, `!` or a line break. `quick question? is /speckit:resume safe to run twice` and `ok, is /speckit:plan enough here` read as requests. Taken by the coordinator. | Both follow the sentence-end set the task named, and the Opus check found no case the change broke. Adding `?` and `,` would be a new rule with no reproduction from real use. | Yes, with a real prompt that reproduces it | 020 `tasks.md` T028 evidence |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1375:| P024 | A question mark ends a sentence in the mention reader, so a bare ask word that follows one opens a question about the command. This supersedes P022 for the question mark. A comma stays out of the sentence-start set. Taken by the dispatched planner that wrote phases 024 and 025 after the Fable 5.2 review of 2026-11-14, as are P025 to P031. | The review reproduced it: `quick question? is /speckit:resume safe to run twice` returned `/speckit:resume` (start), and the planning probe printed `shipped=false` for it. A question mark ends a sentence in any grammar, so the edit is no tuning, and the guard `is this right? run /speckit:plan` stays a request. P022's own condition was a prompt that reproduces it. A comma ends a clause, and no prompt reproduced the comma form. | Yes | 024 tasks T008, 024 `scratch/planning/probe-mention-reader.before.txt` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1377:| P026 | Rows sv-09, sv-11 and sv-12 keep their `expected_command`. No build task relabels them. The routing-accuracy README states the three designed withholds, and the relabel waits on the operator with options and a recommendation. | The capture counts a slash-variant row with no expected command as a row that must stay silent, so a relabel moves the false-offer floor from 0 of 35 to 0 of 38, and completion criterion 2 quotes 35. That criterion is the operator's. A relabel would also file a full command name under partial mentions, a different class, while phase 023 counts questions about a command on sealed `decline` rows. Consumers checked: the capture and its committed baseline, `command-routing-slice.vitest.ts`, the transcript scorer's row labels, the behaviour runner, `measure-brief-cost.mjs` and two handler and scorer tests. | Waits on the operator | 024 spec, Open Questions and mechanism table |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/decision-record.md:1380:| P029 | The Codex reader keeps the body of a custom tool call as `arguments.input` and the transcript scorer reads the shell commands out of it. One `exec` call stays one shell step whose command holds its `cmd` strings one per line. | The reader is shared with the history lookup, four hooks and one plugin, whose contract calls tool arguments opaque, so the record keeps its shape and gains one key. What counts as a command is the scorer's question. One step per call keeps the change to one helper and one call, at the cost that a body holding a gate lookup and a task command reads as a gate step, which the README states. | Yes | 024 tasks T009 and T011, 024 plan, affected surfaces |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:25:    open_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:26:    answered_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:155:| Operator chat instruction, 2026-11-13 04:30Z | Recorded here | 'In rease parallelism' (verbatim, typo is the operator's): run file-disjoint work side by side, several workers per wave. It has no sweep key, because it answered no question, so the save path cannot write it to a decision record |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:167:| Phase 015 health default and brief refinements | Complete, committed (see git log) | Builds segment three ranks 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 9 and 11. 20 planned tasks verified 20 of 20 PASS by three Opus verifiers, five follow-ups checked by the coordinator. Suite 183 files 1755 passed 0 failed, floors unchanged, strict PASSED. Open: live brief cost not measured, the script refused with degraded_brief |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:170:| Operator amendment to D1, 2026-11-13 | Operator-made | 'use ask question tool for any decisions needed': decisions that are the operator's are now asked through the question tool, no longer taken alone |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:171:| Operator answers, 2026-11-13 (question tool) | Decided by the operator | Rank 7: build the Claude-only create skill and managed .claude/skills tree. Rank 12: keep typed only on the degraded brief (Q026 stands), declined. Rank 13: offer /doctor:helper on an ambiguous doctor prompt. R4-P2-003: yes, edit the AGENTS.md Gate 2 direct-call example to the stdin form. The three builds become phase 016 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:177:| Operator answers, 2026-11-13 third round (question tool) | Decided by the operator | Codex: approve the hooks for one arena and run one Codex-only arm, which reverses no more arms for Codex alone. Gate 2 clause for a skill-only brief: declined, Gate 2 stays as approved. Write discipline on Devin and OpenCode: tracked for a separate packet. Holdout row suppressed-codex-abstain: retire it in this packet, as a new phase 018 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:178:| Operator answers, 2026-11-13 fourth round (question tool) | Decided by the operator | Phase 018 retires only suppressed-codex-abstain. The two short sealed rows that hit data files (P1-ABSTAIN-001, P1-PHRASE-001) and the six sealed rows that hit hand-written scorer rules only are an advisory for a separate decision. The final hand-over of this branch reaches main through a pull request, not a direct push |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:181:| Operator instruction, 2026-11-13 17:00Z | Operator-made, amends D4 | Verbatim: Use fable 5.2 medium through claude 2 for critical thinking / hard questions but dont ket it implement or use subagents. claude2 is the operator zsh function for the second Claude account. It is used read-only for judgment questions, never to edit and never with subagents |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:184:| Phase 009 research | Complete, decided without the operato... | Segment one ranks 7 and 11 and three guards of rank 14 declined with reasons in 009 tasks.md, rank 8 reason restated on Q053 and Q057, question 4 carried to the Codex-only arm. Each reason was checked read-only by Fable 5.2 medium on the second Claude account, which corrected three of them. Strict PASSED, 0 errors, 1 SOURCE_TAGS warning on lineage files |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:189:| WAITING ON OPERATOR: Codex-only behaviour arm | Waiting | Approved by the operator (Q052) and needs the operator to open Codex in a prepared arena, run /hooks and approve each entry. Phase 007 closes without it, decided without the operator (D1): the summary already prints codex 0 of 12 before and after with no brief delivered. Research question 4 is carried to this arm |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:191:| Conflict named: D1 against the logged amendment | Resolved toward the session goal | The goal the operator set for this session on 2026-11-13 states D1 as ask the operator nothing. The log row of the same day amends D1 to ask through the question tool. This session followed the goal as set and took each decision itself, recording it as decided without the operator, so each one stays open for the operator to overturn |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:202:| Outcome measure for the core need | Proposed, waits on the operator | The packet counts offers and starts. It has no number for how often a model followed a real workflow, the command's or the skill's own, against improvising. Recorded as an open question in the parent spec. Building it and setting a target is the operator's decision |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:207:| Peer session question on the routing corpus pin, 2026-11-13 | Answered not yet | The archive subtrack session will fix the Routing Registry Drift Guard on main. This branch removes one holdout row (phase 018) that reaches main only with the pull request, so a pin recaptured before the merge goes red again. Who recaptures the pin is the operator's call |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:210:| Routing corpus pin recapture, operator-confirmed 2026-11-13 (question tool) | Done, commit 0238274ed8, not pushed | The operator chose this branch to recapture routing-baseline.json in system-deep-loop 013-drift-guard-repairs. All three corpus hashes repinned, four captures retaken, the workflow's pin check prints corpus matches the pinned baseline hashes and the scoring gate passes at its floors in the CI regime (accuracy 0.5795, TT 110, FT 3, FF 1). The peer session that asked could not be told: its socket... |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:215:| Operator answers, 2026-11-13 fifth round (question tool) | Decided by the operator | Release note: amend v4.0.2.1 on the branch, no new version. Outcome measure for the core need: build now as phase 019 from the stored final-arm sessions. Typed /create:skill: the advisor points it at /create:sk-skill. Cleanup: delete the nested repository and the 34 GB behaviour arenas, the arenas after the measure is scored |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:221:| Merge of origin/main 4f57ea6ac8 and of worktrees/372-hub-vocabulary-drift | Done, commits 8390d86ca9 and 2276ba13... | Operator approved the 372 merge through the question tool on 2026-11-14 after the peer session asked. Tag pre-merge-352b marks 3a91e4ab61. Only the trigger index and its three fixtures conflicted, rebuilt by generate-trigger-index.mjs with --check exit 0. The commit gate raised sk-doc ROUTER.md to 2.4.8.0 and re-minted both hub manifests. Skill graph freshness strict exit 0, bridges fresh, 0 be... |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:224:| Fable 5.2 alignment reviews, 2026-11-14 | Done, verdicts DRIFTING and not ready... | Operator asked for two fresh Fable 5.2 medium reviews on the second Claude account, read-only, no subagents. Code lens: 5 P1, 7 P2. Purpose lens: DRIFTING, 4 P1, 7 P2. Both found the phase 019 share drops runs that wrote nothing: 9 of Claude's 10 such final-arm runs ran shell steps without a load. Reproduced by the coordinator: refusal and question prompts get a start command, app problems get... |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:242:| Phase 020 command offer fit guards closed | Done, not committed yet | Probe offers 26 to 8, suite 1919 passed 0 failed, five floors and eval equal. Real sealed plain 5 to 4 of 44, cause the uncertainty bar (P021). Slice baseline recaptured for three question rows (P020). Two doctor cases out of scope, scores 10.009 and 9.761. |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:245:| Phase 020 test-first check rerun | Holds, no correction | Parsing the shell tool events of each worker log shows a failing vitest run before the passing one for each of T003 to T010 and T017, for example T003 24 failed then 62 passed, T007 1 failed then 20 passed. The earlier finding that only T007 had one came from a grep over the whole log, which matched quoted task text |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:252:| Remediation plan for the 11:40 review, 2026-11-14 | Planning, Fable 5.2 medium on claude2 | Phase 024 review remediation (Codex shell text in the session reader, refusal wording, question mark as a sentence end superseding P022, offeredAs read by the scorer, the rest of the shell-read rule, sv-09 to sv-12 labels, the two skillLabel fallbacks) and phase 025 release notes and doc sync. Brief and report in review/fable-review-2026-11-14-1140/ |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/goal.md:253:| Phases 024 and 025 planned, 2026-11-14 | Planned, not built | 024: 23 tasks, lanes A and R first, lane S after phases 022 and 023 close. 025: 18 tasks, after 019 to 024 close. Probes in 024 scratch/planning: Codex shell events with no command text 58 of 58, mention reader 40 of 46 shipped and 46 of 46 planned, shell-read edits 18 of 18. Both validate strict. Decisions P024 to P031 |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:22:    open_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:23:    answered_questions: []\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:139:| 20 | 020-command-offer-fit-guards/ | Keep the model's free choice where no command fits: a command the prompt only mentions, refuses or asks about is not offered, a no-edit request and a correction inside an existing document carry no writing command and a weak doctor cue needs the stronger bar, each reproduced by a probe that printed 26 command heads on 26 such prompts (alignment reviews of 2026-11-14, findings A-4, A-5, A-6, A-8, B-3 and B-9) | Complete |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:143:| 24 | 024-fable-review-remediation/ | The fixes for the Fable 5.2 review of 2026-11-14: the Codex session reader keeps the body of a custom tool call and the transcript scorer reads its shell commands, so a Codex run can show a load, the mention reader reads `no need to run` and `stop using` as refusals, keeps the command on `why not use` and on a later `run it` and ends a sentence at a question mark, a search and a heredoc line are no load, a `cd` inside one command is followed and a command on the partner side is not counted as offered, with both stored arms rescored and the Codex start rate restated. The relabel of three slash-variant rows waits on the operator and three carry items are declined on their probes (findings 1, 4, 5, 6 and 7, decision P024) | Complete |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:168:| 015-health-default-and-brief-refinements | 016-claude-create-reach-and-doctor-default | Phase 015 is committed, every pinned floor holds and the operator has answered the rename, doctor cue and changelog questions | `git log -1 --format=%h -- 015-health-default-and-brief-refinements` prints `3b48f0e5f1` or later and phase 016 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:171:| 018-holdout-row-retirement | 019-workflow-outcome-measure | Phase 018 is committed, every pinned floor holds on the tree merged with `origin/main` and the operator has chosen to build the measure now (question tool, 2026-11-13) | The transcript scorer tests report 0 failed, the two summary runs write a per-runtime share for the before arm and the final arm, and phase 019 validates under `validate.sh --strict` |\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:182:<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:195:- Rows sv-09, sv-11 and sv-12 of the command corpus name a command inside a question and still carry `expected_command`, so the committed baseline records three designed withholds as misses. A relabel to no command moves them into the false-offer tally, and the floor in completion criterion 2 would read 0 of 38 where it says 0 of 35. The relabel waits on the operator. The options and a recommendation are in the phase 024 spec (P026).\nspecs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/spec.md:198:<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"grep -rn \\\"typo\\\\|small edit\\\\|correction\\\\|refus\\\\|question\\\\|mention\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/*.md | head -60\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669608966,"end":1794669609072}}}}
