{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669629771,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa5511e001RTCo1ithZjzwvz","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1daa544ae001ARyniuWy4zDWII","type":"tool","id":"call_00_m3hss3m15w41h9wzue1muiwf","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"sed -n '1,220p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md"},"output":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Phase 20: command-offer-fit-guards\"\ndescription: \"The advisor hands a command to prompts where no command fits. A command the reader only refuses or asks about still arrives with a start policy, a typo fix gets a creation workflow, an app problem that shares doctor words gets a doctor command, a no-edit request gets a command that writes and a meaning match the hooks drop still counts as passing. This phase withholds the command in each case and keeps the skill.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"command offer fit guards\"\n  - \"phase 20 command offer fit guards\"\n  - \"withhold a command where none fits\"\n  - \"command only mentioned\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Phase 20: command-offer-fit-guards\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n<!-- FILL: Fill every row: level, priority, status, date and branch. Use the real branch name. GOOD: Priority P1. Status Draft. Branch `feat/rotate-logs-keep`. WEAK: Priority TBD. Status maybe. -->\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 2 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Complete |\n| **Created** | 2026-11-14 |\n| **Branch** | `worktrees/352-command-surfacing-research` |\n| **Parent Spec** | ../spec.md |\n| **Phase** | 20 of 23 |\n| **Predecessor** | 019-workflow-outcome-measure |\n| **Successor** | 021-brief-head-parity |\n| **Handoff Criteria** | Every task in `tasks.md` is `[x]`, the advisor suite reports 0 failed, every floor line equals its line in `scratch/before.txt`, `scratch/repro-after.txt` holds the after counts T014 names and strict validation prints `RESULT: PASSED` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n## Phase Context\n\nThis is **Phase 20** of the build that makes the skill advisor surface every tracked slash command with a run, start or ask policy on every supported CLI (`../spec.md`). The operator's core need is that an AI working through skills stays free to choose and lands on the best correct workflow more often. A command offered where none fits pulls the model off the skill path, which works against that need. Two read-only alignment reviews of 2026-11-14 (`../review/fable-alignment-2026-11-14/`) found five such cases. This phase fixes the ones a probe reproduced.\n\n**Scope Boundary**: three source files (`lib/command-attach.ts`, `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`) and three existing test files in the advisor runtime. No renderer, handler, plugin, corpus row, committed baseline, hook, `AGENTS.md` wording or model run.\n\n**Dependencies**:\n- The advisor suite is green on the start commit and the five floor lines are recorded, the sealed plain count among them (T001).\n- The two planning probes in `scratch/planning/` still print the lines T002 names.\n- Phase 021 edits the renderer, the recommend handler and the OpenCode plugin. The two phases share no file, so they may be built side by side.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- `commandOnlyMentioned` in `lib/command-attach.ts`, read by the typed path, the hub attach path and the scorer.\n- A small-edit gate on `/create:*` commands in `attachCommand`.\n- Three scorer gates in `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`: a meaning pass that holds the uncertainty bar, a no-edit gate on every command that writes and a weak problem cue that no longer lowers the hand-off bar.\n- Test cases written first for each, and `scratch/repro-after.txt` with the probe counts after the change.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n<!-- FILL: State the problem in two sentences: what breaks, and for whom. GOOD: The rotate-logs script never deletes old archives, so a host that copies `logs/archive` fills its disk. WEAK: The script has issues with output. -->\n\n### Problem Statement\nThe advisor attaches a command whenever a prompt names one or a hub route picks its mode, without asking whether the reader wants that command. A reader who writes `do not run /speckit:complete yet, just explain what it does` gets `/speckit:complete` with a `start` policy, and `update the README typo in line 3` gets the README creation workflow. The doctor hand-off also reads the bare words `missing`, `broken` and `stale` as a toolkit problem, so `the environment variable for the database url is missing in production` gets `/doctor:env list` as its only recommendation. Each of these is a command where the skill path, or no path, was the best correct answer.\n\n### Purpose\nA prompt that refuses a command, asks about it, wants a small in-place edit, describes an ordinary app problem with a weak cue or rules out a change gets its skill and no unfit command, while every typed and plain request that gets its command today keeps it.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\n<!-- FILL: Run the command this change affects and paste the command and its verbatim output. Quote every number the spec states about current behavior from this block. Write `N/A:` and a reason when no command applies. GOOD: `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh` with 10 archives, then `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 10. WEAK: The script deletes old logs. -->\n```text\n# node scratch/planning/probe-offers.mjs, 2026-11-14, commit 16c9757ac0, advisor daemon live.\n# Full output: scratch/planning/probe-offers.before.txt (26 prompts, 26 lines that hold command=/).\nPROMPT: do not run /speckit:complete yet, just explain what it does\n  row 0: command-speckit-complete 0.8225/0.16 command=/speckit:complete policy=start owner=system-spec-kit ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: I never want to use /create:agent again, delete the agent file\n  row 0: create:agent 0.82/0.16 command=/create:agent policy=start owner=sk-doc ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: someone ran /speckit:save by accident, how do I undo what it wrote\n  row 0: command-speckit-save 0.8709/0.16 command=/speckit:save policy=start owner=system-spec-kit ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: please do not start /deep:research, I only want a two line summary of the readme\n  row 0: system-deep-loop 0.8575/0.16 command=/deep:research policy=ask owner=system-deep-loop ambiguous=true\nPROMPT: what does /create:readme do?\n  row 0: sk-doc 0.95/0.12 command=/create:readme policy=start owner=sk-doc ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: update the README typo in line 3\n  row 0: sk-doc 0.927/0.12 command=/create:readme policy=start owner=- ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: do not run it, just tell me what /doctor:update would change\n  row 0: system-skilled-doctor 0.82/0.26 command=/doctor:update policy=ask owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=true\n  row 2: command-doctor-update 0.82/0.2 command=/doctor:update policy=ask owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=true\nPROMPT: the environment variable for the database url is missing in production\n  row 0: command-doctor-env 0.8/0.34 command=/doctor:env list policy=run owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: the install step in our dockerfile is broken, the overlay filesystem is stale\n  row 0: command-doctor-overlay-status 0.8/0.34 command=/doctor:overlay status policy=run owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: the trigger index lookup returns nothing for my packet, do not change anything\n  row 2: command-doctor-speckit 0.82/0.22 command=/doctor:speckit policy=run owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: my deep research loop never converges, dont touch anything just tell me why\n  row 1: command-doctor-deep-loop 0.8/0.34 command=/doctor:deep-loop policy=run owner=system-deep-loop ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: document the new skill and create a feature catalog for it\n  row 0: command-doctor-sk-skill-convert 0.8/0.42 command=/doctor:sk-skill convert policy=ask owner=sk-doc ambiguous=false\n  row 1: sk-doc 0.95/0.12 command=- policy=- owner=- ambiguous=false\n\n# node --import <tsx loader> scratch/planning/probe-doctor-cue.mts. Full output: scratch/planning/probe-doctor-cue.before.txt\ncue=weak first=/doctor:env list score=8.361 noEdit=false :: the environment variable for the database url is missing in production\ncue=weak first=/doctor:overlay status score=6.529 noEdit=false :: the install step in our dockerfile is broken, the overlay filesystem is stale\ncue=weak first=/doctor:mcp debug score=10.009 noEdit=false :: the mcp tool call fails with a wrong argument error in my weather server code\ncue=strong first=/doctor:git hooks score=9.761 noEdit=false :: turn off the dark mode toggle in the settings page\ncue=weak first=/doctor:runtime-mirrors score=14.255 noEdit=false :: the runtime mirrors are out of sync with .skilled\ncue=weak first=/doctor:agents-md check score=15.398 noEdit=false :: AGENTS.md is missing the shipped sections\ncue=weak first=/doctor:symlink link score=11.428 noEdit=false :: the symlink to the skilled checkout is broken\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n\n### Mechanism per Finding\n\n| Finding | Where it comes from | Fix |\n|---------|---------------------|-----|\n| A-8, B-9 first half, B-3 question case | `typedCommandForTop` and `attachCommand` attach any command the prompt names, and the command's own scorer row passes on the typed string | `commandOnlyMentioned` reads a refusal or a question about the command, and all three paths withhold it (T003 to T005, T008, T017, T018) |\n| B-3 edit case | A hub route that picks the README mode attaches `/create:readme` whatever the size of the edit | `attachCommand` withholds a `/create:*` command when the prompt names a correction, such as a typo, a spelling or a broken link (T006). An edit that names no correction word is not gated |\n| A-4 | `requireCommandPhraseAnchor` lifts a meaning match to the confidence bar and keeps its uncertainty of 0.42, above the 0.35 the hooks use | The meaning pass holds the uncertainty bar, so the scorer and the hooks agree (T007) |\n| A-6 | `/doctor:speckit` and `/doctor:deep-loop` are `run` commands of class `add-only`, and neither the phrase path nor the hand-off checks the no-edit request | Every command row that is not `read-only` stops passing on a no-edit request (T009) |\n| A-5, the two prompts with only a doctor row | A weak cue with no passing skill needs only the ranker score 6 | A weak cue needs the score 10 that a prompt with no cue needs (T010, T011) |\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n<!-- FILL: List three to five things this change does, each starting with a verb. Before you list a new file, module, option, layer or dependency, name what fails today without it, or drop it. GOOD: Add a `--keep <n>` option that deletes all but the newest n archives in `logs/archive/`. WEAK: Update the script and docs. -->\n\n### In Scope\n- Add `commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)` to `lib/command-attach.ts`. Without it nothing can tell `run /speckit:complete` from `do not run /speckit:complete`.\n- Withhold a typed command the prompt refuses or asks about, on the typed path, the hub attach path and the command's own scorer row.\n- Withhold a `/create:*` command from a prompt that asks for a small in-place edit.\n- Hold a meaning-passed command to the uncertainty bar the hooks already apply.\n- Stop a command that writes from passing on a no-edit request, and stop a weak problem cue from lowering the doctor hand-off bar.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- `/doctor:mcp debug` on `the mcp tool call fails ... in my weather server code` and `/doctor:helper` beside `sk-code` on `turn off the dark mode toggle` - the ranker scores both at 10.009 and 9.761, inside the range real toolkit problems score (7.491 to 23.471). Telling them apart needs the ranker to know the subject is foreign, which is the matching change the operator logged for a follow-up packet on 2026-11-13. Raising a bar to move two probes would be tuning on the probes.\n- A plain request that clearly fits a command and gets no brief (B-11) - the same matching change, and it waits on the operator (parent goal log).\n- The `run` policy of an `add-only` doctor command on a prompt that allows a change - the policy is derived from the risk class the inventory phase fixed, and this phase does not reopen it.\n- An in-place edit that names no correction word - `change the title of the README in the hooks folder` and `add a troubleshooting section to the existing README` still return `sk-doc` with `/create:readme (start)` (`scratch/planning/verify-fix-probe.before.txt`). The small-edit gate reads correction wording only. Telling an edit of an existing document from a request to write one needs the route to know the document exists, which no word list can state, so the class is left to the head-wording decision that waits on the operator.\n- A problem in the user's own project that shares a doctor target's words and scores above the bar - a class, not two prompts. Beside the two prompts above, `the symlink in my node_modules folder is broken after npm install` returns only `/doctor:symlink check (run)`. The weak-cue bar removes the low scores and leaves this class to the matching follow-up.\n- A no-change wording `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` does not hold - T009 reads `isNoEditRequest` as it is, so `the trigger index lookup returns nothing for my packet, leave every file as it is` still returns `/doctor:speckit (run)`. Widening that pattern changes the existing attach gate and the read-only routes that share it, so it is not folded into this phase.\n- A refusal word with no comma before a real request - `dont guess run /speckit:plan`, `not sure use /create:readme`, `i can't wait to run /speckit:save`, `why not run /speckit:plan now`, `not only run /speckit:plan but also write tests` and `don't just run /speckit:plan, also update the docs` read as a mention and lose the command. The user typed the command, so it stays in the prompt, and the lead lists are exported data a later change can narrow.\n- The brief wording, the `Also:` line and the OpenCode head - phase 021.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`.\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | `commandOnlyMentioned`, two lead lists, the small-edit list, and the two gates in `typedCommandForTop` and `attachCommand` |\n| `ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | Modify | The uncertainty bar in `requireCommandPhraseAnchor`, `withholdMentionedCommands`, `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit`, the weak-cue line in `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` and their three calls in `scoreAdvisorPrompt` |\n| `ADV/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts` | Modify | The header comment that states the cue rule |\n| `ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cases for the mention reader, the typed gate, the attach gate and the small-edit gate |\n| `ADV/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cases for the uncertainty bar and the two scorer gates |\n| `ADV/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cases for the weak cue |\n| `ADV/tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` | Modify | One case: a refused typed command does not pull its owner first |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n<!-- FILL: Write one testable requirement per row. Name the exact command or output. GOOD: With 10 archives, `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh --keep 3` exits 0 and `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3. WEAK: The option should work well. -->\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | The five floor lines and the eval line equal their lines in `scratch/before.txt`: typed recall at least 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, typed delivery 44 of 44, the plain tune count unchanged and the sealed plain count under the fixture regime unchanged. A lower sealed plain count under the real embedding is recorded with the task that caused it. |\n| REQ-002 | `commandOnlyMentioned` returns `true` for the eight refusal and question prompts in the Measured Behavior block and for the two yes or no questions T003 names, and `false` for the six request prompts and the five controls T003 names, in which a refusal word or a question word sits near a real request. A lead gap holds letters and apostrophes only, so no lead crosses a comma. |\n| REQ-003 | The advisor CLI returns no row that carries the command for the seven prompts that refuse or ask about a command, and `run /speckit:complete for the rate limiter` and `/create:agent security-reviewer` still lead with their command. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-004 | `update the README typo in line 3` and `fix the typo in the README` return `sk-doc` with no command, and `write a readme for the doctor scripts folder` still returns `sk-doc` with `/create:readme`. The gate covers correction wording only: an edit that names no correction word keeps its command and is listed under Out of Scope. |\n| REQ-005 | A meaning-passed command row whose uncertainty is above the threshold does not pass, so `document the new skill and create a feature catalog for it` leads with `sk-doc`. |\n| REQ-006 | On a no-edit request no command row of class `add-only` or `mutates` passes, and a `read-only` command row still passes. |\n| REQ-007 | A weak problem cue with no passing skill hands off only at ranker score 10 or more, so the two app-problem prompts return no recommendation and the three weak-cue toolkit prompts in the probe keep their doctor command. |\n| REQ-008 | No code comment added by this phase names a spec path, a phase, a task, a finding or a requirement id. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n<!-- FILL: Write one measurable outcome per line. A command can prove it. GOOD: With 10 archives in `logs/archive`, `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh --keep 3` leaves 3. WEAK: The feature is successful. -->\n\n- **SC-001**: `node scratch/planning/probe-offers.mjs` prints 8 lines that hold `command=/` where it printed 26 before: `/speckit:complete` 1, `/create:readme` 2, `/create:agent` 2, `/create:manual-testing-playbook` 1 and `/doctor:` 2.\n- **SC-002**: The advisor suite reports 0 failed with more passed tests than `scratch/before.txt`, and the five floor lines and the eval line are unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Name one dependency and one risk. Give each a concrete mitigation. GOOD: A script that reads `--keep` with no value could delete every archive. Mitigation: reject a missing value with exit 2 and test it. WEAK: There may be some risk. -->\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | The advisor daemon and its embedder answer the CLI probe | The after counts cannot be read | T014 marks itself `[B]` with the CLI error. The unit tests prove each gate without the daemon |\n| Risk | A lead list reads a real request as a refusal and a typed row loses its command | High: typed delivery is a pinned floor | Six request prompts are tested first, `don't forget to run` is excluded by name and T013 fails when typed delivery leaves 44 of 44 |\n| Risk | The weak-cue bar drops a tune row whose ranker score is between 6 and 10 | Med: the plain tune count is a floor | T013 compares the count. On a drop the task is `[B]` and no pattern is tuned to restore it |\n| Risk | The lists are tuned to the review's own probes | Med: that is the failure the reviews named | Each list holds general wording, the tests hold counter-examples and phase 023 scores sealed rows nobody saw |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:nfr -->\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Phase 20: command-offer-fit-guards\"\ndescription: \"The advisor hands a command to prompts where no command fits. A command the reader only refuses or asks about still arrives with a start policy, a typo fix gets a creation workflow, an app problem that shares doctor words gets a doctor command, a no-edit request gets a command that writes and a meaning match the hooks drop still counts as passing. This phase withholds the command in each case and keeps the skill.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"command offer fit guards\"\n  - \"phase 20 command offer fit guards\"\n  - \"withhold a command where none fits\"\n  - \"command only mentioned\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Phase 20: command-offer-fit-guards\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n<!-- FILL: Fill every row: level, priority, status, date and branch. Use the real branch name. GOOD: Priority P1. Status Draft. Branch `feat/rotate-logs-keep`. WEAK: Priority TBD. Status maybe. -->\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 2 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Complete |\n| **Created** | 2026-11-14 |\n| **Branch** | `worktrees/352-command-surfacing-research` |\n| **Parent Spec** | ../spec.md |\n| **Phase** | 20 of 23 |\n| **Predecessor** | 019-workflow-outcome-measure |\n| **Successor** | 021-brief-head-parity |\n| **Handoff Criteria** | Every task in `tasks.md` is `[x]`, the advisor suite reports 0 failed, every floor line equals its line in `scratch/before.txt`, `scratch/repro-after.txt` holds the after counts T014 names and strict validation prints `RESULT: PASSED` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n## Phase Context\n\nThis is **Phase 20** of the build that makes the skill advisor surface every tracked slash command with a run, start or ask policy on every supported CLI (`../spec.md`). The operator's core need is that an AI working through skills stays free to choose and lands on the best correct workflow more often. A command offered where none fits pulls the model off the skill path, which works against that need. Two read-only alignment reviews of 2026-11-14 (`../review/fable-alignment-2026-11-14/`) found five such cases. This phase fixes the ones a probe reproduced.\n\n**Scope Boundary**: three source files (`lib/command-attach.ts`, `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`) and three existing test files in the advisor runtime. No renderer, handler, plugin, corpus row, committed baseline, hook, `AGENTS.md` wording or model run.\n\n**Dependencies**:\n- The advisor suite is green on the start commit and the five floor lines are recorded, the sealed plain count among them (T001).\n- The two planning probes in `scratch/planning/` still print the lines T002 names.\n- Phase 021 edits the renderer, the recommend handler and the OpenCode plugin. The two phases share no file, so they may be built side by side.\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- `commandOnlyMentioned` in `lib/command-attach.ts`, read by the typed path, the hub attach path and the scorer.\n- A small-edit gate on `/create:*` commands in `attachCommand`.\n- Three scorer gates in `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`: a meaning pass that holds the uncertainty bar, a no-edit gate on every command that writes and a weak problem cue that no longer lowers the hand-off bar.\n- Test cases written first for each, and `scratch/repro-after.txt` with the probe counts after the change.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n<!-- FILL: State the problem in two sentences: what breaks, and for whom. GOOD: The rotate-logs script never deletes old archives, so a host that copies `logs/archive` fills its disk. WEAK: The script has issues with output. -->\n\n### Problem Statement\nThe advisor attaches a command whenever a prompt names one or a hub route picks its mode, without asking whether the reader wants that command. A reader who writes `do not run /speckit:complete yet, just explain what it does` gets `/speckit:complete` with a `start` policy, and `update the README typo in line 3` gets the README creation workflow. The doctor hand-off also reads the bare words `missing`, `broken` and `stale` as a toolkit problem, so `the environment variable for the database url is missing in production` gets `/doctor:env list` as its only recommendation. Each of these is a command where the skill path, or no path, was the best correct answer.\n\n### Purpose\nA prompt that refuses a command, asks about it, wants a small in-place edit, describes an ordinary app problem with a weak cue or rules out a change gets its skill and no unfit command, while every typed and plain request that gets its command today keeps it.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\n<!-- FILL: Run the command this change affects and paste the command and its verbatim output. Quote every number the spec states about current behavior from this block. Write `N/A:` and a reason when no command applies. GOOD: `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh` with 10 archives, then `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 10. WEAK: The script deletes old logs. -->\n```text\n# node scratch/planning/probe-offers.mjs, 2026-11-14, commit 16c9757ac0, advisor daemon live.\n# Full output: scratch/planning/probe-offers.before.txt (26 prompts, 26 lines that hold command=/).\nPROMPT: do not run /speckit:complete yet, just explain what it does\n  row 0: command-speckit-complete 0.8225/0.16 command=/speckit:complete policy=start owner=system-spec-kit ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: I never want to use /create:agent again, delete the agent file\n  row 0: create:agent 0.82/0.16 command=/create:agent policy=start owner=sk-doc ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: someone ran /speckit:save by accident, how do I undo what it wrote\n  row 0: command-speckit-save 0.8709/0.16 command=/speckit:save policy=start owner=system-spec-kit ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: please do not start /deep:research, I only want a two line summary of the readme\n  row 0: system-deep-loop 0.8575/0.16 command=/deep:research policy=ask owner=system-deep-loop ambiguous=true\nPROMPT: what does /create:readme do?\n  row 0: sk-doc 0.95/0.12 command=/create:readme policy=start owner=sk-doc ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: update the README typo in line 3\n  row 0: sk-doc 0.927/0.12 command=/create:readme policy=start owner=- ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: do not run it, just tell me what /doctor:update would change\n  row 0: system-skilled-doctor 0.82/0.26 command=/doctor:update policy=ask owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=true\n  row 2: command-doctor-update 0.82/0.2 command=/doctor:update policy=ask owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=true\nPROMPT: the environment variable for the database url is missing in production\n  row 0: command-doctor-env 0.8/0.34 command=/doctor:env list policy=run owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: the install step in our dockerfile is broken, the overlay filesystem is stale\n  row 0: command-doctor-overlay-status 0.8/0.34 command=/doctor:overlay status policy=run owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: the trigger index lookup returns nothing for my packet, do not change anything\n  row 2: command-doctor-speckit 0.82/0.22 command=/doctor:speckit policy=run owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: my deep research loop never converges, dont touch anything just tell me why\n  row 1: command-doctor-deep-loop 0.8/0.34 command=/doctor:deep-loop policy=run owner=system-deep-loop ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: document the new skill and create a feature catalog for it\n  row 0: command-doctor-sk-skill-convert 0.8/0.42 command=/doctor:sk-skill convert policy=ask owner=sk-doc ambiguous=false\n  row 1: sk-doc 0.95/0.12 command=- policy=- owner=- ambiguous=false\n\n# node --import <tsx loader> scratch/planning/probe-doctor-cue.mts. Full output: scratch/planning/probe-doctor-cue.before.txt\ncue=weak first=/doctor:env list score=8.361 noEdit=false :: the environment variable for the database url is missing in production\ncue=weak first=/doctor:overlay status score=6.529 noEdit=false :: the install step in our dockerfile is broken, the overlay filesystem is stale\ncue=weak first=/doctor:mcp debug score=10.009 noEdit=false :: the mcp tool call fails with a wrong argument error in my weather server code\ncue=strong first=/doctor:git hooks score=9.761 noEdit=false :: turn off the dark mode toggle in the settings page\ncue=weak first=/doctor:runtime-mirrors score=14.255 noEdit=false :: the runtime mirrors are out of sync with .skilled\ncue=weak first=/doctor:agents-md check score=15.398 noEdit=false :: AGENTS.md is missing the shipped sections\ncue=weak first=/doctor:symlink link score=11.428 noEdit=false :: the symlink to the skilled checkout is broken\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n\n### Mechanism per Finding\n\n| Finding | Where it comes from | Fix |\n|---------|---------------------|-----|\n| A-8, B-9 first half, B-3 question case | `typedCommandForTop` and `attachCommand` attach any command the prompt names, and the command's own scorer row passes on the typed string | `commandOnlyMentioned` reads a refusal or a question about the command, and all three paths withhold it (T003 to T005, T008, T017, T018) |\n| B-3 edit case | A hub route that picks the README mode attaches `/create:readme` whatever the size of the edit | `attachCommand` withholds a `/create:*` command when the prompt names a correction, such as a typo, a spelling or a broken link (T006). An edit that names no correction word is not gated |\n| A-4 | `requireCommandPhraseAnchor` lifts a meaning match to the confidence bar and keeps its uncertainty of 0.42, above the 0.35 the hooks use | The meaning pass holds the uncertainty bar, so the scorer and the hooks agree (T007) |\n| A-6 | `/doctor:speckit` and `/doctor:deep-loop` are `run` commands of class `add-only`, and neither the phrase path nor the hand-off checks the no-edit request | Every command row that is not `read-only` stops passing on a no-edit request (T009) |\n| A-5, the two prompts with only a doctor row | A weak cue with no passing skill needs only the ranker score 6 | A weak cue needs the score 10 that a prompt with no cue needs (T010, T011) |\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n<!-- FILL: List three to five things this change does, each starting with a verb. Before you list a new file, module, option, layer or dependency, name what fails today without it, or drop it. GOOD: Add a `--keep <n>` option that deletes all but the newest n archives in `logs/archive/`. WEAK: Update the script and docs. -->\n\n### In Scope\n- Add `commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)` to `lib/command-attach.ts`. Without it nothing can tell `run /speckit:complete` from `do not run /speckit:complete`.\n- Withhold a typed command the prompt refuses or asks about, on the typed path, the hub attach path and the command's own scorer row.\n- Withhold a `/create:*` command from a prompt that asks for a small in-place edit.\n- Hold a meaning-passed command to the uncertainty bar the hooks already apply.\n- Stop a command that writes from passing on a no-edit request, and stop a weak problem cue from lowering the doctor hand-off bar.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- `/doctor:mcp debug` on `the mcp tool call fails ... in my weather server code` and `/doctor:helper` beside `sk-code` on `turn off the dark mode toggle` - the ranker scores both at 10.009 and 9.761, inside the range real toolkit problems score (7.491 to 23.471). Telling them apart needs the ranker to know the subject is foreign, which is the matching change the operator logged for a follow-up packet on 2026-11-13. Raising a bar to move two probes would be tuning on the probes.\n- A plain request that clearly fits a command and gets no brief (B-11) - the same matching change, and it waits on the operator (parent goal log).\n- The `run` policy of an `add-only` doctor command on a prompt that allows a change - the policy is derived from the risk class the inventory phase fixed, and this phase does not reopen it.\n- An in-place edit that names no correction word - `change the title of the README in the hooks folder` and `add a troubleshooting section to the existing README` still return `sk-doc` with `/create:readme (start)` (`scratch/planning/verify-fix-probe.before.txt`). The small-edit gate reads correction wording only. Telling an edit of an existing document from a request to write one needs the route to know the document exists, which no word list can state, so the class is left to the head-wording decision that waits on the operator.\n- A problem in the user's own project that shares a doctor target's words and scores above the bar - a class, not two prompts. Beside the two prompts above, `the symlink in my node_modules folder is broken after npm install` returns only `/doctor:symlink check (run)`. The weak-cue bar removes the low scores and leaves this class to the matching follow-up.\n- A no-change wording `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` does not hold - T009 reads `isNoEditRequest` as it is, so `the trigger index lookup returns nothing for my packet, leave every file as it is` still returns `/doctor:speckit (run)`. Widening that pattern changes the existing attach gate and the read-only routes that share it, so it is not folded into this phase.\n- A refusal word with no comma before a real request - `dont guess run /speckit:plan`, `not sure use /create:readme`, `i can't wait to run /speckit:save`, `why not run /speckit:plan now`, `not only run /speckit:plan but also write tests` and `don't just run /speckit:plan, also update the docs` read as a mention and lose the command. The user typed the command, so it stays in the prompt, and the lead lists are exported data a later change can narrow.\n- The brief wording, the `Also:` line and the OpenCode head - phase 021.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n`ADV` is `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime`.\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `ADV/lib/command-attach.ts` | Modify | `commandOnlyMentioned`, two lead lists, the small-edit list, and the two gates in `typedCommandForTop` and `attachCommand` |\n| `ADV/lib/scorer/fusion.ts` | Modify | The uncertainty bar in `requireCommandPhraseAnchor`, `withholdMentionedCommands`, `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit`, the weak-cue line in `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` and their three calls in `scoreAdvisorPrompt` |\n| `ADV/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts` | Modify | The header comment that states the cue rule |\n| `ADV/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cases for the mention reader, the typed gate, the attach gate and the small-edit gate |\n| `ADV/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cases for the uncertainty bar and the two scorer gates |\n| `ADV/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cases for the weak cue |\n| `ADV/tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` | Modify | One case: a refused typed command does not pull its owner first |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n<!-- FILL: Write one testable requirement per row. Name the exact command or output. GOOD: With 10 archives, `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh --keep 3` exits 0 and `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3. WEAK: The option should work well. -->\nREQ ids run in one sequence across the P0 and P1 tables. A new requirement takes the highest REQ id plus one. validate.sh does not link ids between files.\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-001 | The five floor lines and the eval line equal their lines in `scratch/before.txt`: typed recall at least 24 of 44, false offers 0 of 35, typed delivery 44 of 44, the plain tune count unchanged and the sealed plain count under the fixture regime unchanged. A lower sealed plain count under the real embedding is recorded with the task that caused it. |\n| REQ-002 | `commandOnlyMentioned` returns `true` for the eight refusal and question prompts in the Measured Behavior block and for the two yes or no questions T003 names, and `false` for the six request prompts and the five controls T003 names, in which a refusal word or a question word sits near a real request. A lead gap holds letters and apostrophes only, so no lead crosses a comma. |\n| REQ-003 | The advisor CLI returns no row that carries the command for the seven prompts that refuse or ask about a command, and `run /speckit:complete for the rate limiter` and `/create:agent security-reviewer` still lead with their command. |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement |\n|----|-------------|\n| REQ-004 | `update the README typo in line 3` and `fix the typo in the README` return `sk-doc` with no command, and `write a readme for the doctor scripts folder` still returns `sk-doc` with `/create:readme`. The gate covers correction wording only: an edit that names no correction word keeps its command and is listed under Out of Scope. |\n| REQ-005 | A meaning-passed command row whose uncertainty is above the threshold does not pass, so `document the new skill and create a feature catalog for it` leads with `sk-doc`. |\n| REQ-006 | On a no-edit request no command row of class `add-only` or `mutates` passes, and a `read-only` command row still passes. |\n| REQ-007 | A weak problem cue with no passing skill hands off only at ranker score 10 or more, so the two app-problem prompts return no recommendation and the three weak-cue toolkit prompts in the probe keep their doctor command. |\n| REQ-008 | No code comment added by this phase names a spec path, a phase, a task, a finding or a requirement id. |\n\n> Acceptance criteria for these requirements live in `acceptance-criteria.md`,\n> which is the document that decides whether this packet may close.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n<!-- FILL: Write one measurable outcome per line. A command can prove it. GOOD: With 10 archives in `logs/archive`, `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh --keep 3` leaves 3. WEAK: The feature is successful. -->\n\n- **SC-001**: `node scratch/planning/probe-offers.mjs` prints 8 lines that hold `command=/` where it printed 26 before: `/speckit:complete` 1, `/create:readme` 2, `/create:agent` 2, `/create:manual-testing-playbook` 1 and `/doctor:` 2.\n- **SC-002**: The advisor suite reports 0 failed with more passed tests than `scratch/before.txt`, and the five floor lines and the eval line are unchanged.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n<!-- FILL: Name one dependency and one risk. Give each a concrete mitigation. GOOD: A script that reads `--keep` with no value could delete every archive. Mitigation: reject a missing value with exit 2 and test it. WEAK: There may be some risk. -->\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | The advisor daemon and its embedder answer the CLI probe | The after counts cannot be read | T014 marks itself `[B]` with the CLI error. The unit tests prove each gate without the daemon |\n| Risk | A lead list reads a real request as a refusal and a typed row loses its command | High: typed delivery is a pinned floor | Six request prompts are tested first, `don't forget to run` is excluded by name and T013 fails when typed delivery leaves 44 of 44 |\n| Risk | The weak-cue bar drops a tune row whose ranker score is between 6 and 10 | Med: the plain tune count is a floor | T013 compares the count. On a drop the task is `[B]` and no pattern is tuned to restore it |\n| Risk | The lists are tuned to the review's own probes | Med: that is the failure the reviews named | Each list holds general wording, the tests hold counter-examples and phase 023 scores sealed rows nobody saw |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:nfr -->\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"sed -n '1,220p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794669629726,"end":1794669629771}}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1794669631498,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"id":"prt_1daa5580a001DHEgRCB9XrJ7PJ","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1daa544ae001ARyniuWy4zDWII","type":"step-finish","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"0e9fe22fde7368b1900bad254a28d473a5ba43f2","cost":0,"tokens":{"input":3168,"output":76,"reasoning":238,"cache":{"read":162944,"write":0}}}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794669633383,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"id":"prt_1daa55f67001HYGSS8kP0bqLGq","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1daa55815001clhKhNXLJh7v91","type":"step-start","snapshot":"0e9fe22fde7368b1900bad254a28d473a5ba43f2"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794669650365,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1daa5a0fa001BnMB3aSMpVjjOD","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1daa55815001clhKhNXLJh7v91","type":"tool","id":"call_01_ektsefq2ozz78rrdmdm3lfu0","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"grep -n \"P024\\|P022\\|mention reader\\|question mark\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md | head -30; sed -n '1,160p' specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md"},"output":"3:description: \"The review of 2026-11-14 found that every Codex shell step reaches the transcript scorer with no command text, that two refusal wordings still get a command and three real requests lose theirs, that a question after a question mark still gets a start offer, that a command on the partner side counts as offered and that the shell-read rule counts a search and a heredoc line and misses a read after cd. This phase fixes each one, test first, and rescores the stored Codex sessions.\"\n8:  - \"refusal wording mention reader\"\n43:**Scope Boundary**: the Codex session reader with its test and its folder README, the mention reader in `command-attach.ts` with its test, the transcript scorer with its test and the routing-accuracy README. No corpus row, no committed baseline, no behaviour run, no model session, no `AGENTS.md` edit and no edit to another phase folder. The scorer file is being built by phases 022 and 023, so no task on it starts before phase 023 is Complete.\n46:- Phases 020 and 021 are Complete and committed, because lane A edits the mention reader phase 020 built (T001 checks).\n52:- A mention reader that reads `no need to run` and `stop using` as refusals, reads `why not use`, a later `run it` and a statement before a request as requests, and ends a sentence at a question mark.\n64:Codex runs its shell through a custom tool whose body is JavaScript, the session reader drops that body and the scorer therefore sees 58 shell steps with no command text in the before arm, so a Codex run can never show a load. The mention reader still hands a command to a reader who wrote `no need to run` or `stop using`, and withholds one from a reader who wrote `I have not run it yet, please start it`. A reader of the packet's numbers cannot trust a Codex row, and a person who refused a command still gets it.\n170:| P022, a bare ask word after a question mark | The sentence-start set of the bare lead holds `.`, `!` and a line break | Fix, reverses P022 as P024 (T008). A comma stays out, because a comma ends a clause and not a sentence, and no prompt reproduced it |\n191:- Read two more refusal wordings as refusals and three request wordings as requests in the mention reader, and end a sentence at a question mark.\n276:| Risk | A changed mention reader moves a row of the committed baseline | Med: the slice test fails | T019 compares the floors and names the moved row ids without a prompt. A recapture is the coordinator's decision, never a worker's |\n291:- **NFR-P01**: The mention reader stays one pass per named command, and the scorer stays one pass over a run's events.\n---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Phase 24: fable-review-remediation\"\ndescription: \"The review of 2026-11-14 found that every Codex shell step reaches the transcript scorer with no command text, that two refusal wordings still get a command and three real requests lose theirs, that a question after a question mark still gets a start offer, that a command on the partner side counts as offered and that the shell-read rule counts a search and a heredoc line and misses a read after cd. This phase fixes each one, test first, and rescores the stored Codex sessions.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"fable review remediation\"\n  - \"phase 24 fable review remediation\"\n  - \"codex shell steps without command text\"\n  - \"refusal wording mention reader\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Phase 24: fable-review-remediation\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n<!-- FILL: Fill every row: level, priority, status, date and branch. Use the real branch name. GOOD: Priority P1. Status Draft. Branch `feat/rotate-logs-keep`. WEAK: Priority TBD. Status maybe. -->\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 2 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Complete |\n| **Created** | 2026-11-14 |\n| **Branch** | `worktrees/352-command-surfacing-research` |\n| **Parent Spec** | ../spec.md |\n| **Phase** | 24 of 25 |\n| **Predecessor** | 023-untuned-outcome-evidence |\n| **Successor** | 025-release-notes-and-doc-sync |\n| **Handoff Criteria** | Every task in `tasks.md` is `[x]`, the advisor suite, the session reader tests and the history lookup tests report 0 failed, the mention probe prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`, `scratch/rescore-delta.txt` names the Codex start rate before and after, the five floors equal their before lines and strict validation prints `RESULT: PASSED` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n## Phase Context\n\nThis is **Phase 24** of the build that makes the skill advisor surface every tracked slash command with a run, start or ask policy on every supported CLI (`../spec.md`). The packet exists so an AI that works through skills stays free to choose the command path or the skill path and lands on the best correct workflow more often, never an improvised one. A read-only Fable 5.2 review at 11:40 on 2026-11-14 (`../review/fable-review-2026-11-14-1140/report.txt`) judged the packet on course and not ready to close. It left two P1 and seven P2 findings, and the Opus task checks of phases 020 and 021 carried four more items (`../scratch/carry-to-review.md`). The coordinator handled findings 2, 3 and 8, the `sed -i` part of finding 7 and the row-0 carry item. This phase takes the rest.\n\n**Scope Boundary**: the Codex session reader with its test and its folder README, the mention reader in `command-attach.ts` with its test, the transcript scorer with its test and the routing-accuracy README. No corpus row, no committed baseline, no behaviour run, no model session, no `AGENTS.md` edit and no edit to another phase folder. The scorer file is being built by phases 022 and 023, so no task on it starts before phase 023 is Complete.\n\n**Dependencies**:\n- Phases 020 and 021 are Complete and committed, because lane A edits the mention reader phase 020 built (T001 checks).\n- Phases 022 and 023 are Complete and committed before lane S starts, because all three phases edit `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (T003 checks).\n- The stored Codex sessions of the before and after arm are still readable under the Codex home folder (T002 reruns the probe).\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- A Codex reader that keeps the body of a custom tool call, and a scorer that reads the shell commands out of it.\n- A mention reader that reads `no need to run` and `stop using` as refusals, reads `why not use`, a later `run it` and a statement before a request as requests, and ends a sentence at a question mark.\n- A scorer that does not count a search or a heredoc line as a load, follows a `cd` inside one command and does not count a command on the partner side as offered.\n- `scratch/rescore-delta.txt` with the Codex start rate and load rate before and after, and one row in the parent goal log that states whether criterion 3's Codex number moved.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n<!-- FILL: State the problem in two sentences: what breaks, and for whom. GOOD: The rotate-logs script never deletes old archives, so a host that copies `logs/archive` fills its disk. WEAK: The script has issues with output. -->\n\n### Problem Statement\nCodex runs its shell through a custom tool whose body is JavaScript, the session reader drops that body and the scorer therefore sees 58 shell steps with no command text in the before arm, so a Codex run can never show a load. The mention reader still hands a command to a reader who wrote `no need to run` or `stop using`, and withholds one from a reader who wrote `I have not run it yet, please start it`. A reader of the packet's numbers cannot trust a Codex row, and a person who refused a command still gets it.\n\n### Purpose\nA Codex shell step reaches the scorer with its command text, a refusal loses its command and a real request keeps it, and the measure counts only a read as a load, so the stored runs and the brief both say what happened.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\n<!-- FILL: Run the command this change affects and paste the command and its verbatim output. Quote every number the spec states about current behavior from this block. Write `N/A:` and a reason when no command applies. GOOD: `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh` with 10 archives, then `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 10. WEAK: The script deletes old logs. -->\n```text\n# node scratch/planning/probe-codex-shell.mjs, 2026-11-14, over ../007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl.\n# Counts only. Body shape lines are left out here and kept in scratch/planning/probe-codex-shell.before.txt.\ncodex lines: 24\ncustom tool call name:exec: 58\ncustom tool calls: 58\ncustom tool calls with an input string: 58\nexec bodies the planned helper reads no command from: 8\nof those, read before the first write: 4\nowned rows: 16\npath now:none: 16\npath with the body read:command: 2\npath with the body read:none: 12\npath with the body read:skill: 2\nsessions read: 24\nsessions whose wrote fact changes: 0\nsessions with a shell read of a skill or command document: 4\nshell events: 58\nshell events with no command text: 58\nstarted now: 0\nstarted with the body read: 0\ntools called inside exec bodies: exec_command=65, mcp__codex_apps__github_fetch=1, web__run=4\n\n# The same probe over runs-post.jsonl (scratch/planning/probe-codex-shell.post.txt).\nshell events: 53\nshell events with no command text: 53\npath now:none: 16\npath with the body read:command: 1\npath with the body read:none: 13\npath with the body read:skill: 2\nstarted now: 0\nstarted with the body read: 0\n\n# node --import ./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs scratch/planning/probe-mention-reader.mts, last two lines.\nSHIPPED: 40 of 46 agree\nPLANNED: 46 of 46 agree\n\n# node ../020-command-offer-fit-guards/scratch/planning/probe-offers.mjs --top-only --file scratch/planning/review-prompts.json, row 0 of each prompt.\nPROMPT: no need to run /doctor:setup, the hooks are fine\n  row 0: command-doctor-setup 0.826/0.16 command=/doctor:setup policy=run owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: stop using /create:changelog for this, write the changelog entry by hand\n  row 0: sk-doc 0.8923/0.12 command=/create:changelog policy=ask owner=sk-doc ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: I have not run /speckit:plan yet, please start it for the login feature\n  row 0: system-spec-kit 0.82/0.22 command=- policy=- owner=- ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: I already ran /create:readme but the output was wrong, run it again for the hooks folder\n  row 0: sk-doc 0.9175/0.12 command=- policy=- owner=- ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: why not use /create:agent for this? go ahead and make a security reviewer agent\n  row 0: sk-doc 0.82/0.22 command=- policy=- owner=- ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: quick question? is /speckit:resume safe to run twice\n  row 0: system-spec-kit 0.8218/0.16 command=/speckit:resume policy=start owner=system-spec-kit ambiguous=false\n\n# node scratch/planning/probe-shell-read-rule.mjs, the hand-built events and both stored arms.\nrg over the owner entry document: skill\ngrep over the owner entry document: skill\nrg whose pattern is the document name: none\nheredoc body line that starts with a reader: skill\nheredoc body line that starts with head: skill\ncd into the skill folder, then cat: none\ncd into the mode folder, then sed: none\ncd elsewhere, then cat a bare name: none\ncat with the full path, the control: skill\nclaude: owned=32, loads resting on rg or grep alone=0, cd then a bare document name=0, heredoc body line with a reader verb=0\ncodex: owned=16, loads resting on rg or grep alone=0, cd then a bare document name=0, heredoc body line with a reader verb=0\ndevin: owned=32, loads resting on rg or grep alone=0, cd then a bare document name=0, heredoc body line with a reader verb=0\ndsh: owned=31, loads resting on rg or grep alone=0, cd then a bare document name=0, heredoc body line with a reader verb=0\nopencode: owned=32, loads resting on rg or grep alone=1, cd then a bare document name=0, heredoc body line with a reader verb=0\npi: owned=32, loads resting on rg or grep alone=1, cd then a bare document name=1, heredoc body line with a reader verb=1\n\n# rg -c \"offeredAs\" over score-command-transcripts.mjs prints nothing: the scorer never reads the field.\n\n# node --import ./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs scratch/planning/probe-skill-label.mts.\nneeds-mode hub, label sent as the hub: Advisor: live; use sk-doc (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\nneeds-mode hub, no label sent: Advisor: live; use sk-doc (needs a mode) 0.91/0.12 pass.\nsame head with and without the label: true\nfailing row 0, label taken from row 0: Advisor: live; use sk-git 0.82/0.20 pass.\nfailing row 0, label taken from the first passing row: Advisor: live; use sk-code 0.82/0.20 pass.\nCLI rows over 5 prompts: 10, below the bars: 0, row 0 below the bars: 0\n\n# node scratch/planning/probe-plugin-flake.mjs 20.\ntermination grace test: 20 passed, 0 failed of 20 runs, slowest process 251 ms\n\n# jq -c 'select(.id==\"sv-09\" or .id==\"sv-11\" or .id==\"sv-12\") | del(.prompt)' over command-prompts.jsonl.\n{\"id\":\"sv-09\",\"row_type\":\"slash-variant\",\"split\":\"none\",\"expected_command\":\"/speckit:resume\",\"expected_top\":null,\"expected_policy\":null,\"source\":\"authored-deepseek\"}\n{\"id\":\"sv-11\",\"row_type\":\"slash-variant\",\"split\":\"none\",\"expected_command\":\"/doctor:git\",\"expected_top\":null,\"expected_policy\":null,\"source\":\"authored-deepseek\"}\n{\"id\":\"sv-12\",\"row_type\":\"slash-variant\",\"split\":\"none\",\"expected_command\":\"/prompt:improve\",\"expected_top\":null,\"expected_policy\":null,\"source\":\"authored-deepseek\"}\n```\n<!-- /ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"The review of 2026-11-14 found that every Codex shell step reaches the transcript scorer with no command text, that two refusal wordings still get a command and three real requests lose theirs, that a question after a question mark still gets a start offer, that a command on the partner side counts as offered and that the shell-read rule counts a search and a heredoc line and misses a read after cd. This phase fixes each one, test first, and rescores the stored Codex sessions.\"\n8:  - \"refusal wording mention reader\"\n43:**Scope Boundary**: the Codex session reader with its test and its folder README, the mention reader in `command-attach.ts` with its test, the transcript scorer with its test and the routing-accuracy README. No corpus row, no committed baseline, no behaviour run, no model session, no `AGENTS.md` edit and no edit to another phase folder. The scorer file is being built by phases 022 and 023, so no task on it starts before phase 023 is Complete.\n46:- Phases 020 and 021 are Complete and committed, because lane A edits the mention reader phase 020 built (T001 checks).\n52:- A mention reader that reads `no need to run` and `stop using` as refusals, reads `why not use`, a later `run it` and a statement before a request as requests, and ends a sentence at a question mark.\n64:Codex runs its shell through a custom tool whose body is JavaScript, the session reader drops that body and the scorer therefore sees 58 shell steps with no command text in the before arm, so a Codex run can never show a load. The mention reader still hands a command to a reader who wrote `no need to run` or `stop using`, and withholds one from a reader who wrote `I have not run it yet, please start it`. A reader of the packet's numbers cannot trust a Codex row, and a person who refused a command still gets it.\n170:| P022, a bare ask word after a question mark | The sentence-start set of the bare lead holds `.`, `!` and a line break | Fix, reverses P022 as P024 (T008). A comma stays out, because a comma ends a clause and not a sentence, and no prompt reproduced it |\n191:- Read two more refusal wordings as refusals and three request wordings as requests in the mention reader, and end a sentence at a question mark.\n276:| Risk | A changed mention reader moves a row of the committed baseline | Med: the slice test fails | T019 compares the floors and names the moved row ids without a prompt. A recapture is the coordinator's decision, never a worker's |\n291:- **NFR-P01**: The mention reader stays one pass per named command, and the scorer stays one pass over a run's events.\n---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Phase 24: fable-review-remediation\"\ndescription: \"The review of 2026-11-14 found that every Codex shell step reaches the transcript scorer with no command text, that two refusal wordings still get a command and three real requests lose theirs, that a question after a question mark still gets a start offer, that a command on the partner side counts as offered and that the shell-read rule counts a search and a heredoc line and misses a read after cd. This phase fixes each one, test first, and rescores the stored Codex sessions.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"fable review remediation\"\n  - \"phase 24 fable review remediation\"\n  - \"codex shell steps without command text\"\n  - \"refusal wording mention reader\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.4 -->\n# Feature Specification: Phase 24: fable-review-remediation\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 2 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n<!-- FILL: Fill every row: level, priority, status, date and branch. Use the real branch name. GOOD: Priority P1. Status Draft. Branch `feat/rotate-logs-keep`. WEAK: Priority TBD. Status maybe. -->\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 2 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Complete |\n| **Created** | 2026-11-14 |\n| **Branch** | `worktrees/352-command-surfacing-research` |\n| **Parent Spec** | ../spec.md |\n| **Phase** | 24 of 25 |\n| **Predecessor** | 023-untuned-outcome-evidence |\n| **Successor** | 025-release-notes-and-doc-sync |\n| **Handoff Criteria** | Every task in `tasks.md` is `[x]`, the advisor suite, the session reader tests and the history lookup tests report 0 failed, the mention probe prints `SHIPPED: 46 of 46 agree`, `scratch/rescore-delta.txt` names the Codex start rate before and after, the five floors equal their before lines and strict validation prints `RESULT: PASSED` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n## Phase Context\n\nThis is **Phase 24** of the build that makes the skill advisor surface every tracked slash command with a run, start or ask policy on every supported CLI (`../spec.md`). The packet exists so an AI that works through skills stays free to choose the command path or the skill path and lands on the best correct workflow more often, never an improvised one. A read-only Fable 5.2 review at 11:40 on 2026-11-14 (`../review/fable-review-2026-11-14-1140/report.txt`) judged the packet on course and not ready to close. It left two P1 and seven P2 findings, and the Opus task checks of phases 020 and 021 carried four more items (`../scratch/carry-to-review.md`). The coordinator handled findings 2, 3 and 8, the `sed -i` part of finding 7 and the row-0 carry item. This phase takes the rest.\n\n**Scope Boundary**: the Codex session reader with its test and its folder README, the mention reader in `command-attach.ts` with its test, the transcript scorer with its test and the routing-accuracy README. No corpus row, no committed baseline, no behaviour run, no model session, no `AGENTS.md` edit and no edit to another phase folder. The scorer file is being built by phases 022 and 023, so no task on it starts before phase 023 is Complete.\n\n**Dependencies**:\n- Phases 020 and 021 are Complete and committed, because lane A edits the mention reader phase 020 built (T001 checks).\n- Phases 022 and 023 are Complete and committed before lane S starts, because all three phases edit `score-command-transcripts.mjs` (T003 checks).\n- The stored Codex sessions of the before and after arm are still readable under the Codex home folder (T002 reruns the probe).\n\n**Deliverables**:\n- A Codex reader that keeps the body of a custom tool call, and a scorer that reads the shell commands out of it.\n- A mention reader that reads `no need to run` and `stop using` as refusals, reads `why not use`, a later `run it` and a statement before a request as requests, and ends a sentence at a question mark.\n- A scorer that does not count a search or a heredoc line as a load, follows a `cd` inside one command and does not count a command on the partner side as offered.\n- `scratch/rescore-delta.txt` with the Codex start rate and load rate before and after, and one row in the parent goal log that states whether criterion 3's Codex number moved.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-context -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n<!-- FILL: State the problem in two sentences: what breaks, and for whom. GOOD: The rotate-logs script never deletes old archives, so a host that copies `logs/archive` fills its disk. WEAK: The script has issues with output. -->\n\n### Problem Statement\nCodex runs its shell through a custom tool whose body is JavaScript, the session reader drops that body and the scorer therefore sees 58 shell steps with no command text in the before arm, so a Codex run can never show a load. The mention reader still hands a command to a reader who wrote `no need to run` or `stop using`, and withholds one from a reader who wrote `I have not run it yet, please start it`. A reader of the packet's numbers cannot trust a Codex row, and a person who refused a command still gets it.\n\n### Purpose\nA Codex shell step reaches the scorer with its command text, a refusal loses its command and a real request keeps it, and the measure counts only a read as a load, so the stored runs and the brief both say what happened.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:measured-behavior -->\n### Measured Behavior\n<!-- FILL: Run the command this change affects and paste the command and its verbatim output. Quote every number the spec states about current behavior from this block. Write `N/A:` and a reason when no command applies. GOOD: `bash scripts/rotate-logs.sh` with 10 archives, then `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 10. WEAK: The script deletes old logs. -->\n```text\n# node scratch/planning/probe-codex-shell.mjs, 2026-11-14, over ../007-per-runtime-behaviour-proof/scratch/runs-pre.jsonl.\n# Counts only. Body shape lines are left out here and kept in scratch/planning/probe-codex-shell.before.txt.\ncodex lines: 24\ncustom tool call name:exec: 58\ncustom tool calls: 58\ncustom tool calls with an input string: 58\nexec bodies the planned helper reads no command from: 8\nof those, read before the first write: 4\nowned rows: 16\npath now:none: 16\npath with the body read:command: 2\npath with the body read:none: 12\npath with the body read:skill: 2\nsessions read: 24\nsessions whose wrote fact changes: 0\nsessions with a shell read of a skill or command document: 4\nshell events: 58\nshell events with no command text: 58\nstarted now: 0\nstarted with the body read: 0\ntools called inside exec bodies: exec_command=65, mcp__codex_apps__github_fetch=1, web__run=4\n\n# The same probe over runs-post.jsonl (scratch/planning/probe-codex-shell.post.txt).\nshell events: 53\nshell events with no command text: 53\npath now:none: 16\npath with the body read:command: 1\npath with the body read:none: 13\npath with the body read:skill: 2\nstarted now: 0\nstarted with the body read: 0\n\n# node --import ./.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/node_modules/tsx/dist/loader.mjs scratch/planning/probe-mention-reader.mts, last two lines.\nSHIPPED: 40 of 46 agree\nPLANNED: 46 of 46 agree\n\n# node ../020-command-offer-fit-guards/scratch/planning/probe-offers.mjs --top-only --file scratch/planning/review-prompts.json, row 0 of each prompt.\nPROMPT: no need to run /doctor:setup, the hooks are fine\n  row 0: command-doctor-setup 0.826/0.16 command=/doctor:setup policy=run owner=system-skilled-doctor ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: stop using /create:changelog for this, write the changelog entry by hand\n  row 0: sk-doc 0.8923/0.12 command=/create:changelog policy=ask owner=sk-doc ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: I have not run /speckit:plan yet, please start it for the login feature\n  row 0: system-spec-kit 0.82/0.22 command=- policy=- owner=- ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: I already ran /create:readme but the output was wrong, run it again for the hooks folder\n  row 0: sk-doc 0.9175/0.12 command=- policy=- owner=- ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: why not use /create:agent for this? go ahead and make a security reviewer agent\n  row 0: sk-doc 0.82/0.22 command=- policy=- owner=- ambiguous=false\nPROMPT: quick question? is /speckit:resume safe to run twice\n  row 0: system-spec-kit 0.8218/0.16 command=/speckit:resume policy=start owner=system-spec-kit ambiguous=false\n\n# node scratch/planning/probe-shell-read-rule.mjs, the hand-built events and both stored arms.\nrg over the owner entry documen