{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670170536,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1daad8f84001PHHhCbzhe2bF16","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1daad5da8001WEbs5JBjNdMcXu","type":"tool","id":"call_00_w4ehfrltwy07r5ajuyd56bru","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"{\n  \"sessionId\": \"fanout-scorer-attach-4-1794669272137-9v23rz\",\n  \"generation\": 1,\n  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n  \"openFindings\": [],\n  \"resolvedFindings\": [],\n  \"repeatedFindings\": [],\n  \"dimensionCoverage\": {\n    \"correctness\": false,\n    \"security\": false,\n    \"traceability\": false,\n    \"maintainability\": false\n  },\n  \"findingsBySeverity\": {\n    \"P0\": 0,\n    \"P1\": 0,\n    \"P2\": 0\n  },\n  \"openFindingsCount\": 0,\n  \"resolvedFindingsCount\": 0,\n  \"convergenceScore\": 0.0\n}\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-findings-registry.json"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-findings-registry.json","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-findings-registry.json"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"{\\n  \\\"sessionId\\\": \\\"fanout-scorer-attach-4-1794669272137-9v23rz\\\",\\n  \\\"generation\\\": 1,\\n  \\\"lineageMode\\\": \\\"new\\\",\\n  \\\"openFindings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"resolvedFindings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"repeatedFindings\\\": [],\\n  \\\"dimensionCoverage\\\": {\\n    \\\"correctness\\\": false,\\n    \\\"security\\\": false,\\n    \\\"traceability\\\": false,\\n    \\\"maintainability\\\": false\\n  },\\n  \\\"findingsBySeverity\\\": {\\n    \\\"P0\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"P1\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"P2\\\": 0\\n  },\\n  \\\"openFindingsCount\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"resolvedFindingsCount\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"convergenceScore\\\": 0.0\\n}\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-findings-registry.json\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670169988,"end":1794670170536}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670170546,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1daad9034001RQfSMPt1Oolp1D","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1daad5da8001WEbs5JBjNdMcXu","type":"tool","id":"call_01_wk4cdv6cqa8bopmmjc8pp007","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"---\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-4 lineage\ndescription: Runtime strategy tracking review progress for the scorer-attach fan-out lineage, fourth pass of command surfacing.\nversion: 1.11.14.0\n---\n\n# Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-4 lineage\n\n## 1. OVERVIEW\n\n### Purpose\n\nPersistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\n(P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\niteration before any review action.\n\n### Ownership\n\nMachine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human\ncommentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\n\n---\n\n## 2. TOPIC\n\nReview pass four of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\nin the `scorer-attach` area. Scope: the eleven changed paths listed in\n`review/review-scope-4.txt` whose area is `scorer-attach` — the attach module, the recommend\nhandler, the scorer modules that gate command rows, and their tests — plus shared docs that\ndescribe them. The change range is `0cdc9fa3ef..400c90e158` (HEAD at dispatch).\n\nThe operator focus is the pass-four brief: checks on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh;\na refusal, question or bare mention of a command still attaching or starting a mutating command;\nthe transcript scorer's load/followed/offer arithmetic; holdout hygiene; and docs that disagree\nwith code.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\n- [ ] correctness\n- [ ] security\n- [ ] traceability\n- [ ] maintainability\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n## 4. NON-GOALS\n\n- The renderer, hooks, plugin, session readers and doctor command docs are the\n  `render-hooks-plugin-4` and `doctor-docs-4` lineages' scope. This lineage reads them only as\n  context evidence.\n- The transcript scorer, command-offer harness, capture baseline and corpus files are the\n  `accuracy-runner-4` lineage's scope. The operator focus asks about their arithmetic; this\n  lineage records the boundary and does not raise code findings outside it.\n- Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\n  `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\n\n---\n\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold with no active P0.\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 4.\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\n\n---\n\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n\n---\n\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\n\n- Dimension: correctness\n- Focus area: the mention reader, the retired-command map and the small-edit gate in\n  `lib/command-attach.ts`, and the two new scorer gates in `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`.\n- Reason: the pass-four brief's highest-impact question is whether a refusal, question or\n  mention still attaches a command.\n- Required evidence: a direct `attachCommand` / `typedCommandForTop` probe and a compiled-route\n  probe for each prompt.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n\n---\n\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\n\n- Target pointers: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`,\n  `runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts`,\n  `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, and the six changed test files.\n- Behavior claims: phase 020 spec `REQ-003`, `REQ-004`, `REQ-006`, `REQ-007`; phase 024's mention\n  reader decisions P022 and P024; phase 021's head-row parity decision P015.\n- Reuse and conventions: the generated command tables are outputs of\n  `runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`; the `--check` run is fresh.\n  Review doctrine is `sk-code-review/references/review-core.md` §2.\n- Review risks and gaps: the local compiled dist is stale (system reminder). Tests read source\n  through vitest, so a source-level probe is valid, but a live runtime could still load dist.\n  No live per-runtime session is available; cross-runtime claims rest on the runtime-neutral\n  handler and the shared tests.\n- Out of scope: transcript scorer arithmetic, renderer output, holdout prompt text.\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No playbook surface in the changed files |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"---\\ntitle: Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-4 lineage\\ndescription: Runtime strategy tracking review progress for the scorer-attach fan-out lineage, fourth pass of command surfacing.\\nversion: 1.11.14.0\\n---\\n\\n# Deep Review Strategy - scorer-attach-4 lineage\\n\\n## 1. OVERVIEW\\n\\n### Purpose\\n\\nPersistent brain for this fan-out lineage. It records which dimensions remain, what was found\\n(P0/P1/P2), which review approaches worked or failed, and where to focus next. Read at every\\niteration before any review action.\\n\\n### Ownership\\n\\nMachine-managed metrics and coverage blocks are wrapped in explicit ownership markers. Human\\ncommentary and operator overrides live outside those markers.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. TOPIC\\n\\nReview pass four of `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build`\\nin the `scorer-attach` area. Scope: the eleven changed paths listed in\\n`review/review-scope-4.txt` whose area is `scorer-attach` — the attach module, the recommend\\nhandler, the scorer modules that gate command rows, and their tests — plus shared docs that\\ndescribe them. The change range is `0cdc9fa3ef..400c90e158` (HEAD at dispatch).\\n\\nThe operator focus is the pass-four brief: checks on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin and dsh;\\na refusal, question or bare mention of a command still attaching or starting a mutating command;\\nthe transcript scorer's load/followed/offer arithmetic; holdout hygiene; and docs that disagree\\nwith code.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n## 3. REVIEW DIMENSIONS (remaining)\\n- [ ] correctness\\n- [ ] security\\n- [ ] traceability\\n- [ ] maintainability\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:review-dimensions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. NON-GOALS\\n\\n- The renderer, hooks, plugin, session readers and doctor command docs are the\\n  `render-hooks-plugin-4` and `doctor-docs-4` lineages' scope. This lineage reads them only as\\n  context evidence.\\n- The transcript scorer, command-offer harness, capture baseline and corpus files are the\\n  `accuracy-runner-4` lineage's scope. The operator focus asks about their arithmetic; this\\n  lineage records the boundary and does not raise code findings outside it.\\n- Holdout prompt text is never read or printed. Corpus work is limited to counts and\\n  `jq 'del(.prompt)'` rows.\\n- No code changes: review is observation-only.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\\n\\n- Convergence: `newFindingsRatio` at or below the 0.10 threshold with no active P0.\\n- Cap: `maxIterations` 4.\\n- Stuck: two consecutive iterations with no new evidence (stuckThreshold 2).\\n- Any active P0 blocks PASS regardless of convergence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n## 6. COMPLETED DIMENSIONS\\n[None yet -- populated as iterations complete dimension reviews]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completed-dimensions -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n## 7. RUNNING FINDINGS\\n- **P0 (Critical):** 0 active\\n- **P1 (Major):** 0 active\\n- **P2 (Minor):** 0 active\\n- **Delta this iteration:** +0 P0, +0 P1, +0 P2\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:running-findings -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n## 10. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\\n\\n[Populated when a review approach has been tried from multiple angles without yielding new findings]\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n## 12. NEXT FOCUS\\n\\n- Dimension: correctness\\n- Focus area: the mention reader, the retired-command map and the small-edit gate in\\n  `lib/command-attach.ts`, and the two new scorer gates in `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`.\\n- Reason: the pass-four brief's highest-impact question is whether a refusal, question or\\n  mention still attaches a command.\\n- Required evidence: a direct `attachCommand` / `typedCommandForTop` probe and a compiled-route\\n  probe for each prompt.\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 13. KNOWN CONTEXT\\n\\n### Bounded Context Snapshot\\n\\n- Target pointers: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`,\\n  `runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts`,\\n  `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, and the six changed test files.\\n- Behavior claims: phase 020 spec `REQ-003`, `REQ-004`, `REQ-006`, `REQ-007`; phase 024's mention\\n  reader decisions P022 and P024; phase 021's head-row parity decision P015.\\n- Reuse and conventions: the generated command tables are outputs of\\n  `runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs`; the `--check` run is fresh.\\n  Review doctrine is `sk-code-review/references/review-core.md` §2.\\n- Review risks and gaps: the local compiled dist is stale (system reminder). Tests read source\\n  through vitest, so a source-level probe is valid, but a live runtime could still load dist.\\n  No live per-runtime session is available; cross-runtime claims rest on the runtime-neutral\\n  handler and the shared tests.\\n- Out of scope: transcript scorer arithmetic, renderer output, holdout prompt text.\\n\\n---\\n\\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n## 14. CROSS-REFERENCE STATUS\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Iteration | Notes |\\n|----------|-------|--------|-----------|-------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | pending | - | - |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | pending | - | - |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | - | No playbook surface in the changed files |\\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-reference-status -->\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670170164,"end":1794670170546}}}}
