{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670295303,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1daaf77b3001R27p7WlSby9tLb","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1daaf5ece0011o1pNHbNPCnAtG","type":"tool","id":"call_00_cbs3lf6rng7z8fobax3dd0mn","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]","newString":"## 8. WHAT WORKED\n\n- Reading the three guards as one ordering chain instead of three independent checks: the retired-name gap only appears because `typedCommandIn` rewrites before `commandOnlyMentioned` reads, and the coordinated-refusal gap only appears because the lead must sit directly before each occurrence (iteration 1).\n- Probing the handler's real attach path: `scoreAdvisorPrompt` put `sk-doc` and `system-deep-loop` first for the two refusal prompts, and `typedCommandForTop` returned the command for both, so the defect was proven at the public recommendation boundary rather than only at the helper (iteration 1).\n- Running the compiled-route front door for the same prompts: it returned `action: defer`, which narrowed the live path to the typed attach and kept the finding honest about its caller (iteration 1).\n- Running the six changed test files first: 191 passed, so the new tests are green and the gaps are uncovered inputs rather than a failing suite (iteration 1).\n\n---\n\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\n\n- Reading the mention reader as a complete refusal guard failed: its documented \"every occurrence has to carry a lead\" rule is what lets a coordinated refusal's second name through, so the reading produced finding `SA4-P1-002` instead of a clean pass (iteration 1).\n- Reading the small-edit gate's creation guard as a document-creation check failed: `make sure`, `add a` and `new` are ordinary correction clauses, and the gate stands down on all three, so the reading produced `SA4-P1-003` (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -90,15 +90,19 @@\n ---\n \n ## 8. WHAT WORKED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading the three guards as one ordering chain instead of three independent checks: the retired-name gap only appears because `typedCommandIn` rewrites before `commandOnlyMentioned` reads, and the coordinated-refusal gap only appears because the lead must sit directly before each occurrence (iteration 1).\n+- Probing the handler's real attach path: `scoreAdvisorPrompt` put `sk-doc` and `system-deep-loop` first for the two refusal prompts, and `typedCommandForTop` returned the command for both, so the defect was proven at the public recommendation boundary rather than only at the helper (iteration 1).\n+- Running the compiled-route front door for the same prompts: it returned `action: defer`, which narrowed the live path to the typed attach and kept the finding honest about its caller (iteration 1).\n+- Running the six changed test files first: 191 passed, so the new tests are green and the gaps are uncovered inputs rather than a failing suite (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n ## 9. WHAT FAILED\n \n-[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\n+- Reading the mention reader as a complete refusal guard failed: its documented \"every occurrence has to carry a lead\" rule is what lets a coordinated refusal's second name through, so the reading produced finding `SA4-P1-002` instead of a clean pass (iteration 1).\n+- Reading the small-edit gate's creation guard as a document-creation check failed: `make sure`, `add a` and `new` are ordinary correction clauses, and the gate stands down on all three, so the reading produced `SA4-P1-003` (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n","status":"modified","additions":6,"deletions":2}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md\", \"oldString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n[First iteration -- populated after iteration 1 completes]\", \"newString\": \"## 8. WHAT WORKED\\n\\n- Reading the three guards as one ordering chain instead of three independent checks: the retired-name gap only appears because `typedCommandIn` rewrites before `commandOnlyMentioned` reads, and the coordinated-refusal gap only appears because the lead must sit directly before each occurrence (iteration 1).\\n- Probing the handler's real attach path: `scoreAdvisorPrompt` put `sk-doc` and `system-deep-loop` first for the two refusal prompts, and `typedCommandForTop` returned the command for both, so the defect was proven at the public recommendation boundary rather than only at the helper (iteration 1).\\n- Running the compiled-route front door for the same prompts: it returned `action: defer`, which narrowed the live path to the typed attach and kept the finding honest about its caller (iteration 1).\\n- Running the six changed test files first: 191 passed, so the new tests are green and the gaps are uncovered inputs rather than a failing suite (iteration 1).\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. WHAT FAILED\\n\\n- Reading the mention reader as a complete refusal guard failed: its documented \\\"every occurrence has to carry a lead\\\" rule is what lets a coordinated refusal's second name through, so the reading produced finding `SA4-P1-002` instead of a clean pass (iteration 1).\\n- Reading the small-edit gate's creation guard as a document-creation check failed: `make sure`, `add a` and `new` are ordinary correction clauses, and the gate stands down on all three, so the reading produced `SA4-P1-003` (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670294963,"end":1794670295303}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670295338,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1daaf78bd001M6nGNRkyAEBqfx","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1daaf5ece0011o1pNHbNPCnAtG","type":"tool","id":"call_01_mt4zmcifrk0484swrqcuqno7","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md","oldString":"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated]","newString":"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n\n- **The compiled route attaches the refused command.** Ruled out for `do not run /create:skill` and `do not run /deep:review or /deep:research`: `compiled-route.cjs` returns `action: defer`, so the typed attach is the live path (iteration 1, evidence: probe output and `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:704`).\n- **The retired-name rewrite is itself wrong.** Ruled out: the changed test pins `/create:skill` → `/create:sk-skill`, and the phase decision chose that mapping; only the guard ordering is defective (iteration 1).\n- **`commandOnlyMentioned` reads a longer command as its shorter prefix.** Ruled out by the `(?![a-z0-9_-])` boundary and the `/create:sk-skill-parent` test (iteration 1)."},"output":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md","patch":"Index: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n+++ specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md\n@@ -114,9 +114,11 @@\n ---\n \n ## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n \n-[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\n+- **The compiled route attaches the refused command.** Ruled out for `do not run /create:skill` and `do not run /deep:review or /deep:research`: `compiled-route.cjs` returns `action: defer`, so the typed attach is the live path (iteration 1, evidence: probe output and `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:704`).\n+- **The retired-name rewrite is itself wrong.** Ruled out: the changed test pins `/create:skill` → `/create:sk-skill`, and the phase decision chose that mapping; only the guard ordering is defective (iteration 1).\n+- **`commandOnlyMentioned` reads a longer command as its shorter prefix.** Ruled out by the `(?![a-z0-9_-])` boundary and the `/create:sk-skill-parent` test (iteration 1).\n \n ---\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md\", \"oldString\": \"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n[Review angles that were investigated and definitively eliminated]\", \"newString\": \"## 11. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\\n\\n- **The compiled route attaches the refused command.** Ruled out for `do not run /create:skill` and `do not run /deep:review or /deep:research`: `compiled-route.cjs` returns `action: defer`, so the typed attach is the live path (iteration 1, evidence: probe output and `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:704`).\\n- **The retired-name rewrite is itself wrong.** Ruled out: the changed test pins `/create:skill` → `/create:sk-skill`, and the phase decision chose that mapping; only the guard ordering is defective (iteration 1).\\n- **`commandOnlyMentioned` reads a longer command as its shorter prefix.** Ruled out by the `(?![a-z0-9_-])` boundary and the `/create:sk-skill-parent` test (iteration 1).\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670295229,"end":1794670295338}}}}
