{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670416402,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab1503b001WhHGnY4rF9Udnn","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1dab0d8850015GD8wP6J53CJlv","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ude4jbt13d75nrelh4gz4z09","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Iteration 002\n\n## Dispatcher\n\n- Run: `fanout-scorer-attach-4-1794669272137-9v23rz` (lineage `scorer-attach-4`, pass four, area `scorer-attach`)\n- Mode: review; executor: in-process (no nested dispatch)\n- Dimension: security\n- Review focus addressed: the operator focus asks whether a question or a bare mention of a command can still attach or start a mutating command. This iteration takes the question/mention half against the scorer path, then checks holdout hygiene across the changed files and the changed test that reads the corpus. The transcript scorer's load/followed/offer arithmetic and the six live runtime surfaces are outside this lineage's scope and are named below. Budget profile: `verify` (11-13 calls), used 11.\n- Prior state: iteration 1 recorded three P1 refusal/correction guard gaps; they remain active.\n\n## Files Reviewed\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:356-432` (ask leads, bare lead, mention reader)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1140-1231,1588-1618` (handoff, mention withholding, no-edit gate, call order)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:311-364,429-488` (`publicRecommendation` command copy, compiled-route attach)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts:1-160` (corpus read and new weak-cue cases)\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:135-230` (ask/mention tables)\n- Probe: `lineage/probes/probe-scorer.vitest.ts` (doctor question and statement rows)\n- Executed: `vitest run --cache=false` on the six changed test files → 191 passed, exit 0 (reused from iteration 1; no source changed between runs).\n\n## Findings - New\n\n### P0 Findings\n\nNone.\n\n### P1 Findings\n\nNone new this iteration. The three active P1 findings from iteration 1 remain active and keep this iteration's verdict at CONDITIONAL.\n\n### P2 Findings\n\n1. **A question or statement that names a doctor command with the noun `command` still passes that command row** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209` -- `withholdMentionedCommands` withholds a passing command row only when `commandOnlyMentioned` recognizes the naming. The bare-ask lead is `(?:is|does|can|will|would) ` (`command-attach.ts:389`) and the ask leads require the name to follow the lead directly, so `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` has `the ... command` between the ask word and the name. The same is true of the statement `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README`. In both probes the `command-doctor-update` row passed, and `publicRecommendation` copies `command: '/doctor:update'` and `policy: 'ask'` from `commandRowFor` (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:358-362`). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209]\n   Finding class: mention_reader_gap\n   Scope proof: the changed mention reader and the changed scorer gate are in the declared scope; `publicRecommendation` is the handler's only command-copy path, and the probe uses the real projection and scorer.\n   Affected surface hints: doctor command rows, question/statement phrasings with the noun `command`, `/doctor:update` ask policy, hook brief third row.\n   Case: `scoreAdvisorPrompt('Is the /doctor:update command safe?')` passes `command-doctor-update` as the third row; after `publicRecommendation` it carries `/doctor:update` with policy `ask`. `scoreAdvisorPrompt('The /doctor:update command is documented in the README')` passes the same row. The command is `ask`, so it asks before it writes; that keeps this P2 rather than P1.\n   Claim adjudication:\n   ```json\n   {\"type\":\"claim\",\"claim\":\"A question or statement that puts the noun 'command' between the ask word and the command name is not recognized by the mention reader, so the command row stays passing.\",\"evidenceRefs\":[\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:389\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209\",\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:358\"],\"counterevidenceSought\":\"Probed the direct form 'what does /doctor:update do?' and the row was withheld, so the gap is the inserted noun, not the doctor row itself. Read the ask lead list: it allows 'the command' only after 'what does/what is/...', not after the bare ask words.\",\"alternativeExplanation\":\"The question is a yes/no safety question, not a request; a command offer would still ask before writing, so the impact is an unfit offer rather than a silent write.\",\"finalSeverity\":\"P2\",\"confidence\":0.9,\"downgradeTrigger\":\"Raise to P1 if a mutating command with policy run reaches this phrasing, or if the hooks render the third row in every runtime.\"}\n   ```\n\n## Traceability Checks\n\n- `spec_code` -- partial. The phase 020 purpose says a command the prompt only asks about is not offered; the direct `what does` form passes, but the `is the X command` form does not. The three P1s from iteration 1 remain the larger spec mismatch.\n- `checklist_evidence` -- pending. No checklist claim is in this iteration's focus; deferred to iteration 3.\n- `feature_catalog_code` -- pending; iteration 3.\n- `agent_cross_runtime` -- partial. The scorer and handler have no runtime branch. The third-row rendering question is a renderer/plugin concern owned by `render-hooks-plugin-4`; this lineage records the scorer row, not the rendered brief.\n- `skill_agent` -- notApplicable; no agent-definition change in this area.\n- `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable.\n\n## Integration Evidence\n\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1611` calls `withholdMentionedCommands` after `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` and before the passing set is computed, so a command row that survives this gate reaches both the CLI and the hooks.\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:318` looks up `commandRowFor(recommendation.skill)`; `:358-362` copies `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` onto the public row. The doctor row therefore carries `/doctor:update` rather than only a skill id.\n- Holdout hygiene: the changed source files contain no `command-prompts.jsonl` or `holdout-prompts.jsonl` read. The two changed tests that read the corpus (`advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts:155-166` and `doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts:125-137`) select a known tune id and assert `split === 'tune'` before using the prompt; neither prints a prompt. No tune, fix or report path reads a holdout row.\n- Transcript scorer: `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `command-offer.mjs` and `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` are the `accuracy-runner-4` lineage's files and are not in this lineage's scope. The operator focus's Codex-body, rg/grep, heredoc, cd, partner-side, paired-arm and Wilson-range checks belong there; this iteration records the boundary instead of raising a cross-area finding.\n- Runtime map: the handler's command copy is shared by every runtime; the renderer's child downgrade (read-only visibility) is `render-hooks-plugin-4`'s surface. No changed file in this lineage branches on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin or dsh.\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- **Policy limits the question case.** `/doctor:update` is `ask`, so even a surviving row asks before it writes. The finding is an unfit offer, not an unconfirmed write; a `run` policy on a mutating doctor command would raise the severity.\n- **The row is third in the list.** The probe's passing rows are `system-skilled-doctor`, `mcp-code-mode`, `command-doctor-update`; the handler's default topK is 3, so the command is the last visible row. The hook brief's row count is renderer-owned; the scorer row exists either way.\n- **The statement case may be a deliberate mention.** \"The /doctor:update command is documented in the README\" is a statement, not a request. The phase purpose names a command the prompt \"only mentions\" as an unfit offer, so it is recorded with the question case; a reviewer can split it if the statement class is judged out of scope.\n- **The changed corpus-reading tests are tune-only by id.** Both assert `split === 'tune'`; no holdout row id is used, and no prompt text is printed.\n\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\n\n- `fusion.ts:1216-1231` -- the no-edit gate withholds `add-only` and `mutates` command rows and keeps a `read-only` row; the changed test pins all three classes and passes.\n- `fusion.ts:1200-1211` -- a command row named directly after `what does`/`explain`/`ran` is withheld; the doctor direct-question probe lost the row as intended.\n- `command-attach.ts:472` -- the hub attach path withholds every command on a no-edit prompt, including a read-only one; this is stricter than the scorer gate but cannot offer a writing command.\n- `advisor-recommend.ts:358-362` -- a command row with no `CommandRow` entry adds no `command` field; an inherited name such as `constructor` cannot resolve through `commandRowFor`'s own-key check (`command-attach.ts:193-195`).\n- Holdout hygiene: no holdout prompt text was read or printed; corpus reads in changed tests are tune-id selected and split-asserted.\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- **The doctor command row can be offered on a direct `what does` question.** Ruled out by the probe: `what does /doctor:update do?` passes only `system-skilled-doctor`; the command row is withheld.\n- **A read-only command is withheld by the scorer on a no-edit request.** Ruled out: `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit` returns the `command-doctor-env` row unchanged and the changed test asserts it.\n- **Holdout rows are read by a changed source path.** Ruled out: no changed source file references either corpus file; the only corpus readers are tests that select tune ids and assert the split.\n- **The question case can silently write.** Ruled out for this command: `commandRowFor('command-doctor-update')?.policy` is `ask` (generated row, `command-attach.ts:178`), so the command asks before it acts.\n\n## Next Focus\n\n- Dimension: traceability\n- Focus area: the shared docs that describe the changed attach/handler/scorer behaviour -- `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` and `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md` -- plus the phase 020 requirement that fixes the weak-cue bar.\n- Reason: iteration 1 found the code-level attach gaps; the docs and the phase requirement are the places where the packet's own claims can disagree with the changed code.\n- Rotation status: correctness and security complete (CONDITIONAL), traceability next.\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: security was productive (one P2); no blocked approach.\n- Required evidence: line-level comparison of each doc claim with the changed code, and the phase 020 `REQ-007` text against `DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE`.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-002.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-002.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-002.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Iteration 002\\n\\n## Dispatcher\\n\\n- Run: `fanout-scorer-attach-4-1794669272137-9v23rz` (lineage `scorer-attach-4`, pass four, area `scorer-attach`)\\n- Mode: review; executor: in-process (no nested dispatch)\\n- Dimension: security\\n- Review focus addressed: the operator focus asks whether a question or a bare mention of a command can still attach or start a mutating command. This iteration takes the question/mention half against the scorer path, then checks holdout hygiene across the changed files and the changed test that reads the corpus. The transcript scorer's load/followed/offer arithmetic and the six live runtime surfaces are outside this lineage's scope and are named below. Budget profile: `verify` (11-13 calls), used 11.\\n- Prior state: iteration 1 recorded three P1 refusal/correction guard gaps; they remain active.\\n\\n## Files Reviewed\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:356-432` (ask leads, bare lead, mention reader)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1140-1231,1588-1618` (handoff, mention withholding, no-edit gate, call order)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:311-364,429-488` (`publicRecommendation` command copy, compiled-route attach)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts:1-160` (corpus read and new weak-cue cases)\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:135-230` (ask/mention tables)\\n- Probe: `lineage/probes/probe-scorer.vitest.ts` (doctor question and statement rows)\\n- Executed: `vitest run --cache=false` on the six changed test files → 191 passed, exit 0 (reused from iteration 1; no source changed between runs).\\n\\n## Findings - New\\n\\n### P0 Findings\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n### P1 Findings\\n\\nNone new this iteration. The three active P1 findings from iteration 1 remain active and keep this iteration's verdict at CONDITIONAL.\\n\\n### P2 Findings\\n\\n1. **A question or statement that names a doctor command with the noun `command` still passes that command row** -- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209` -- `withholdMentionedCommands` withholds a passing command row only when `commandOnlyMentioned` recognizes the naming. The bare-ask lead is `(?:is|does|can|will|would) ` (`command-attach.ts:389`) and the ask leads require the name to follow the lead directly, so `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` has `the ... command` between the ask word and the name. The same is true of the statement `The /doctor:update command is documented in the README`. In both probes the `command-doctor-update` row passed, and `publicRecommendation` copies `command: '/doctor:update'` and `policy: 'ask'` from `commandRowFor` (`handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:358-362`). [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209]\\n   Finding class: mention_reader_gap\\n   Scope proof: the changed mention reader and the changed scorer gate are in the declared scope; `publicRecommendation` is the handler's only command-copy path, and the probe uses the real projection and scorer.\\n   Affected surface hints: doctor command rows, question/statement phrasings with the noun `command`, `/doctor:update` ask policy, hook brief third row.\\n   Case: `scoreAdvisorPrompt('Is the /doctor:update command safe?')` passes `command-doctor-update` as the third row; after `publicRecommendation` it carries `/doctor:update` with policy `ask`. `scoreAdvisorPrompt('The /doctor:update command is documented in the README')` passes the same row. The command is `ask`, so it asks before it writes; that keeps this P2 rather than P1.\\n   Claim adjudication:\\n   ```json\\n   {\\\"type\\\":\\\"claim\\\",\\\"claim\\\":\\\"A question or statement that puts the noun 'command' between the ask word and the command name is not recognized by the mention reader, so the command row stays passing.\\\",\\\"evidenceRefs\\\":[\\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:389\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209\\\",\\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:358\\\"],\\\"counterevidenceSought\\\":\\\"Probed the direct form 'what does /doctor:update do?' and the row was withheld, so the gap is the inserted noun, not the doctor row itself. Read the ask lead list: it allows 'the command' only after 'what does/what is/...', not after the bare ask words.\\\",\\\"alternativeExplanation\\\":\\\"The question is a yes/no safety question, not a request; a command offer would still ask before writing, so the impact is an unfit offer rather than a silent write.\\\",\\\"finalSeverity\\\":\\\"P2\\\",\\\"confidence\\\":0.9,\\\"downgradeTrigger\\\":\\\"Raise to P1 if a mutating command with policy run reaches this phrasing, or if the hooks render the third row in every runtime.\\\"}\\n   ```\\n\\n## Traceability Checks\\n\\n- `spec_code` -- partial. The phase 020 purpose says a command the prompt only asks about is not offered; the direct `what does` form passes, but the `is the X command` form does not. The three P1s from iteration 1 remain the larger spec mismatch.\\n- `checklist_evidence` -- pending. No checklist claim is in this iteration's focus; deferred to iteration 3.\\n- `feature_catalog_code` -- pending; iteration 3.\\n- `agent_cross_runtime` -- partial. The scorer and handler have no runtime branch. The third-row rendering question is a renderer/plugin concern owned by `render-hooks-plugin-4`; this lineage records the scorer row, not the rendered brief.\\n- `skill_agent` -- notApplicable; no agent-definition change in this area.\\n- `playbook_capability` -- notApplicable.\\n\\n## Integration Evidence\\n\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1611` calls `withholdMentionedCommands` after `applyDoctorHelperHandoff` and before the passing set is computed, so a command row that survives this gate reaches both the CLI and the hooks.\\n- `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:318` looks up `commandRowFor(recommendation.skill)`; `:358-362` copies `command`, `policy` and `ownerSkillId` onto the public row. The doctor row therefore carries `/doctor:update` rather than only a skill id.\\n- Holdout hygiene: the changed source files contain no `command-prompts.jsonl` or `holdout-prompts.jsonl` read. The two changed tests that read the corpus (`advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts:155-166` and `doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts:125-137`) select a known tune id and assert `split === 'tune'` before using the prompt; neither prints a prompt. No tune, fix or report path reads a holdout row.\\n- Transcript scorer: `score-command-transcripts.mjs`, `command-offer.mjs` and `command-transcript-score.vitest.ts` are the `accuracy-runner-4` lineage's files and are not in this lineage's scope. The operator focus's Codex-body, rg/grep, heredoc, cd, partner-side, paired-arm and Wilson-range checks belong there; this iteration records the boundary instead of raising a cross-area finding.\\n- Runtime map: the handler's command copy is shared by every runtime; the renderer's child downgrade (read-only visibility) is `render-hooks-plugin-4`'s surface. No changed file in this lineage branches on claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin or dsh.\\n\\n## Edge Cases\\n\\n- **Policy limits the question case.** `/doctor:update` is `ask`, so even a surviving row asks before it writes. The finding is an unfit offer, not an unconfirmed write; a `run` policy on a mutating doctor command would raise the severity.\\n- **The row is third in the list.** The probe's passing rows are `system-skilled-doctor`, `mcp-code-mode`, `command-doctor-update`; the handler's default topK is 3, so the command is the last visible row. The hook brief's row count is renderer-owned; the scorer row exists either way.\\n- **The statement case may be a deliberate mention.** \\\"The /doctor:update command is documented in the README\\\" is a statement, not a request. The phase purpose names a command the prompt \\\"only mentions\\\" as an unfit offer, so it is recorded with the question case; a reviewer can split it if the statement class is judged out of scope.\\n- **The changed corpus-reading tests are tune-only by id.** Both assert `split === 'tune'`; no holdout row id is used, and no prompt text is printed.\\n\\n## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces\\n\\n- `fusion.ts:1216-1231` -- the no-edit gate withholds `add-only` and `mutates` command rows and keeps a `read-only` row; the changed test pins all three classes and passes.\\n- `fusion.ts:1200-1211` -- a command row named directly after `what does`/`explain`/`ran` is withheld; the doctor direct-question probe lost the row as intended.\\n- `command-attach.ts:472` -- the hub attach path withholds every command on a no-edit prompt, including a read-only one; this is stricter than the scorer gate but cannot offer a writing command.\\n- `advisor-recommend.ts:358-362` -- a command row with no `CommandRow` entry adds no `command` field; an inherited name such as `constructor` cannot resolve through `commandRowFor`'s own-key check (`command-attach.ts:193-195`).\\n- Holdout hygiene: no holdout prompt text was read or printed; corpus reads in changed tests are tune-id selected and split-asserted.\\n\\n## Ruled Out\\n\\n- **The doctor command row can be offered on a direct `what does` question.** Ruled out by the probe: `what does /doctor:update do?` passes only `system-skilled-doctor`; the command row is withheld.\\n- **A read-only command is withheld by the scorer on a no-edit request.** Ruled out: `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit` returns the `command-doctor-env` row unchanged and the changed test asserts it.\\n- **Holdout rows are read by a changed source path.** Ruled out: no changed source file references either corpus file; the only corpus readers are tests that select tune ids and assert the split.\\n- **The question case can silently write.** Ruled out for this command: `commandRowFor('command-doctor-update')?.policy` is `ask` (generated row, `command-attach.ts:178`), so the command asks before it acts.\\n\\n## Next Focus\\n\\n- Dimension: traceability\\n- Focus area: the shared docs that describe the changed attach/handler/scorer behaviour -- `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md` and `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md` -- plus the phase 020 requirement that fixes the weak-cue bar.\\n- Reason: iteration 1 found the code-level attach gaps; the docs and the phase requirement are the places where the packet's own claims can disagree with the changed code.\\n- Rotation status: correctness and security complete (CONDITIONAL), traceability next.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: security was productive (one P2); no blocked approach.\\n- Required evidence: line-level comparison of each doc claim with the changed code, and the phase 020 `REQ-007` text against `DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE`.\\n\\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/iterations/iteration-002.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670415931,"end":1794670416402}}}}
