e|es|ing)|author(?:ing)?|draft(?:ing)?|scaffold(?:ing)?|generat(?:e|es|ing)|mak(?:e|es|ing)|new|build(?:ing)?|set up|add an?|need an?)\\b/`; (3) add `'broken links'` and `'dead links'` to `SMALL_EDIT_WORDING`. Change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `rg -c 'SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS' $CA` prints 2 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, Opus check FAIL (3 of 14 false positives left), superseded in part by T022 and T024.\n80:- [x] T022 Withhold a creation command only on a correction verb, and exempt the changelog and goal commands (`CA`, `CAG`). After T021, before T020. Added after the Opus check of T021 found that changelog, goal and noun-led requests still lose their command, decided without the operator (D1). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a small edit')`, add `it.each([['sk-create-changelog', 'changelog for v2.1, it fixes the broken link checker and spelling errors'], ['sk-create-changelog', 'log the spelling fixes in the changelog'], ['sk-create-readme', 'document the cli in a readme, each flag gets a one line description'], ['sk-create-readme', 'readme for the spelling package'], ['sk-create-agent', 'an agent that fixes typos']])('keeps the creation command for %s on %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE(mode), prompt)` to equal `MODE_COMMANDS['sk-doc'][mode]`, and `it('keeps the goal command when the goal is about fixes')` expecting the sk-doc mode whose command is `/create:goal` to return `/create:goal` for `set a goal to fix all the typos in the docs`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the new cases fail and every older case pass. Then in `CA`: (1) add `'/create:changelog'` and `'/create:goal'` to `SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS` and extend its comment with one sentence saying a changelog or a goal describes 