command. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the new cases fail. Then in `CA`: replace `SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS` and its comment with `const SMALL_EDIT_GATED_COMMANDS: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set(['/create:readme', '/create:feature-catalog', '/create:manual-testing-playbook', '/create:repo-rule', '/create:benchmark']);` and a comment saying these commands write a document that is later corrected in place, so a correction request names an edit to it rather than a new one, and in `attachCommand` replace the condition `commands[workflowMode].startsWith('/create:') && !SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS.has(commands[workflowMode])` with `SMALL_EDIT_GATED_COMMANDS.has(commands[workflowMode])`. Keep `SMALL_EDIT_REQUEST`, `CREATION_REQUEST` and `CORRECTION_VERB` as they are. Change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `rg -c 'SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS' $CA` prints nothing, `rg -c 'SMALL_EDIT_GATED_COMMANDS' $CA` prints 2 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS): `Tests  93 passed (93)`, `TC` exit 0, 41 of 41 listed prompts as expected, one realistic miss (repo rule) fixed in T026.\n82:- [x] T026 Leave the repo-rule and benchmark commands out of the small-edit gate (`CA`, `CAG`). After T024, before T020. Added after the Opus check of T024 (PASS) found that a repo rule or a benchmark names its purpose the way an agent does, so `I want a repo rule that says fix typos in the same commit` lost `/create:repo-rule`. Decided without the operator (D1). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a small edit')`, add `it.each(['I want a repo rule that says fix typos in the same commit', 'repo rule: always fix typos in the same commit'])('keeps the repo-rule command on %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE(mode), prompt)` to be `/create:repo-