equests. Decided without the operator (D1). Test first: in `CAG`, in the `it.each` T020 added that expects `false`, add `['the next step is /speckit:implement\\nany questions?', '/speckit:implement']`, and add `it.each([['is /speckit:resume safe to run twice', '/speckit:resume'], ['does /doctor:git change files or just report problems', '/doctor:git'], ['can /prompt:improve make a vague request easier to follow', '/prompt:improve'], ['ok. is /speckit:plan enough here', '/speckit:plan']])('reads %s as a question about %s', ...)` expecting `commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)` to be `true`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the five new cases fail. Then in `CA`'s `commandOnlyMentioned`: fold the text so line breaks survive (`.replace(/[^\\S\\n]+/g, ' ').replace(/ *\\n\\s*/g, '\\n')` in place of the current whitespace collapse), end a sentence at `.`, `!` or `\\n`, and accept the bare lead `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` when a `?` follows the command before the sentence end OR when the lead starts the prompt or directly follows a sentence end. Change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: Opus check PASS 2026-11-14: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  104 passed (104)`, `tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` with `tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  23 passed (23)`, `TC` exit 0, comment grep exit 1. Accepted limit, decided without the operator: `?` and `,` do not end a sentence, so `quick question? is /speckit:resume safe to run twice` and `ok, is /speckit:plan enough here` read as requests. Both follow the sentence-end set this task names.\n88:- [x] T008 Add the gate that stops a mentioned command's own row (`FU`, `CMA`). Start after T003 is verified. This task adds the function `withholdMentionedCommands` and nothing else. T017 and T018 change the two functions that use the reader. Test first: in `CMA`, add `describe('withholdMentionedCommands')` with a passing command row `command-speckit-complete` and a passing skill row `system-spec-kit`, built with the row helper the neighbouring cases use. Expect `withholdMentionedCommands(rows, 'do not run /speckit:complete yet, just explain what it does')` to return the command row with `passes_threshold` `false` and the skill row unchanged, expect the same call with `run /speckit:complete for the rate limiter` to return both rows unchanged, expect the same call with `is /speckit:complete overkill for a two line fix?` to return the command row with `passes_threshold` `false`, and expect a passing row `command-doctor-env` with the prompt `do not run /doctor:env on this machine` to stop passing, which proves a command with a subcommand is matched by its base. Run `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` and see it fail on the missing export. Then in `FU`, add `commandOnlyMentioned` and `commandRowFor` to the import from `'../command-attach.js'`, and add `export function withholdMentionedCommands(ranked: readonly AdvisorScoredRecommendation[], prompt: string): AdvisorScoredRecommendation[]` directly above `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`. It maps each passing `kind === 'command'` row whose `commandRowFor(row.skill)?.command.split(' ')[0]` satisfies `commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)` to `{ ...row, passes_threshold: false }` and returns every other row as it is. Give it a comment saying a command row passes on its typed name, so a prompt that names the command to refuse it would otherwise pass that row. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c \"^export function withholdMentionedCommands\" $FU` prints 1 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). First run `4 failed | 20 passed (24)` on the missing export, then `Tests  24 passed (24)`, the export