he retired alias `/create:skill` is not read as one, because the typed name resolves to `/create:sk-skill` first. It predates this phase.\n92:- [x] T023 Keep a writing command the prompt types and asks for on a no-edit request (`FU`, `CMA`). After T009, before T010. Added after the Opus check of T009 found that a scope limit such as `do not touch the code` withheld a command the user typed and asked for, decided without the operator (D1). Test first: in `CMA`, inside `describe('withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit')`, add `it('keeps a writing command the prompt types and asks for')` with the same passing rows the neighbouring case builds, expecting `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit(rows, 'run /speckit:complete for the rate limiter, do not change the public api')` to leave `command-speckit-complete` passing, and `it('still withholds a writing command the prompt only names')` expecting the same call with `do not run /speckit:complete, and do not change anything` to leave it not passing. Run `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` and see the first new case fail. Then in `FU`'s `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit`, inside the per-row check and before a row is un-passed, compute `const base = commandRowFor(recommendation.skill)?.command.split(' ')[0];` and return the row unchanged when `base !== undefined && typedCommandIn(promptLower) === base && !commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, base)`, importing `typedCommandIn` from `../command-attach.js` when it is not already imported. Add a one-line comment saying a command the reader typed and asked for is the request, and the no-edit words limit its scope. Use the variable names the function already has. Change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/scorer/doctor-ordering.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). Through the real `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, the three typed-and-asked prompts keep `command-speckit-save`, `command-speckit-complete` and `command-doctor-speckit` passing, and the two true no-edit prompts pass no writing command. Accepted limit (D1): a no-edit prompt that types two commands and refuses the longer one still withholds the one it asks for, because the typed-command reader returns only the longest name.\n93:- [x] T010 Stop a weak cue from lowering the hand-off bar (`FU`, `DHC`). Test first: in `DHC`, with the scoring helper the existing cases use and no passing skill, add `it.each(['the environment variable for the database url is missing in production', 'the install step in our dockerfile is broken, the overlay filesystem is stale'])('hands off no doctor command for the app problem %s', ...)` expecting no passing row whose id starts `command-doctor-`, and `it.each([['AGENTS.md is missing the shipped sections', 'command-doctor-agents-md-check'], ['the runtime mirrors are out of sync with .skilled', 'command-doctor-runtime-mirrors']])('still hands off %s', ...)` expecting that id to pass. When the second id differs from the probe line `first=/doctor:runtime-mirrors`, take the id `runnableDoctorBridgeId` returns for it. Run `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` and see the two app-problem cases pass `command-doctor-env` and `command-doctor-overlay-status`. Then in `FU`'s `applyDoctorHelperHandoff`, replace `if (match && cue === null && match.score < DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE) return [...ranked];` with `if (match && cue !== 'strong' && match.score < DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE) return [...ranked];` and put above it a comment saying a weak cue is a bare word ordinary work also uses, so it earns no lower bar than a prompt with no cue. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. When a slice test fails because a tune row lost its doctor command, mark the task `[B]` with the row id and restore the line. Evidence: DeepSeek worker marked it blocked as its line instructs: treating a weak cue like no cue dropped tune row `doctor-b-helper-handoff-01` (9.51) and the runtime-mirrors control never reached the bar. The fusion line was restored, its three test cases stayed and T025 resolved both.\n95:- [x] T025 Give a weak doctor cue its own hand-off bar between the strong-cue bar and the no-cue bar (`FU`, `DH`, `DHC`). After T010, before T011. Added after T010 blocked as its line instructs: treating a weak cue like no cue (bar `DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE`) dropped the committed tune row `doctor-b-helper-handoff-01` (weak cue, `/doctor:agents-md check` at 9.51), and the runtime-mirrors control never reaches the bar because two skills pass first. Decided without the operator (D1): the planning probe scores weak-cue app problems at 8.361 and 6.529 and weak-cue toolkit problems at 9.51, 11.428, 14.255 and 15.398, so a weak-cue bar of 9 separates them. Test first: in `DHC`, in the `it.each` T010 added for `still hands off %s`, replace the row `['the runtime mirrors are out of sync with .skilled', <its id>]` with `['the symlink to the skilled checkout is broken', <the id runnableDoctorBridgeId returns for /doctor:symlink link>]`, keeping the AGENTS.md row. Run `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` and see the two app-problem cases fail. If the symlink row also fails before the code change for a reason other than the bar, mark the task `[B]` with the printed line. Then in `DH`, directly below `export const DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE = 10;`, add `export const DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE = 9;` with a comment saying a weak cue is a bare word ordinary work also uses, so it needs a stronger ranker match than a strong cue, though less than no cue. In `FU`, add `DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE` to the import list that already holds `DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE`, then in `applyDoctorHelperHandoff`, directly after the line `if (match && cue === null && match.score < DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE) return [...ranked];` add `if (match && cue === 'weak' && match.score < DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE) return [...ranked];`. Leave the no-cue line as it is. Change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `rg -c 'DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE' $FU` prints 2, `rg -c 'DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE' $DH` prints 1 and `TC` exits 0. When a slice test fails because a tune row lost its doctor command, mark the task `[B]` with the row id and remove the added line. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). `doctor-handoff-command` 16 passed, `doctor-helper-handoff` 16, `doctor-routing-slice` 2 (the tune row keeps `/doctor:agents-md check`), `TC` exit 0. A probe shows the two app problems hand off nothing at 8.361 and 6.529, and the symlink control resolves to `command-doctor-helper` because `/doctor:symlink link` is an ask route. Limit: no unit case sits between 9 and 10, so only the slice tune row pins the weak-cue bar.\n97:- [x] T011 State the weak-cue rule in the hand-off module header (`DH`). After T010. In the numbered comment block at the top of the file, the sentence sits on two comment lines: the line that ends `leads. With no skill passing, a strong ranker match stands in for the` and the next line `//      cue.`. Replace the words `With no skill passing, a strong ranker match stands in for the` and the `cue.` on the next line with `With no skill passing, a weak cue or no cue needs a strong ranker match,` and a next comment line `//      and only a strong cue hands off on the lower score.`, keeping the `leads.` that starts the first line and the comment indentation. Verify: `rg -c \"only a strong cue hands off on the lower score\" $DH` prints 1, `rg -c \"stands in for the cue\" $DH` prints nothing and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, checked by the coordinator. The two comment lines carry the new sentence, `rg -c \"only a strong cue hands off on the lower score\" $DH` printed 1, `rg -c \"stands in for the cue\" $DH` printed nothing, `TC` exit 0. The sentence stays true with the weak-cue bar of 9 that T025 added, because a weak cue still needs more than the strong-cue bar.\n98:- [x] T027 Correct the weak-cue comment in the hand-off test (`DHC`). After T011. Added after the Opus check of T025 found the comment above the app-problem `it.each` still says a weak cue earns no lower bar than a prompt with no cue, which is false since the weak-cue bar is 9 and the no-cue bar is 10. Replace that comment with `// A bare word that ordinary work also uses is a weak cue, so it needs a stronger ranker match than a strong cue.` keeping the indentation, and change nothing else. Verify: `rg -c 'earns no lower bar' $ADV/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` prints nothing, `rg -c 'needs a stronger ranker match than a strong cue' $ADV/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` prints 1 and `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. Evidence: coordinator check 2026-11-14: `rg -c 'earns no lower bar'` printed nothing (exit 1), `rg -c 'needs a stronger ranker match than a strong cue'` printed 1, `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  16 passed (16)`.\n105:<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3 and 10. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n107:- [x] T012 [C] Rebuild and run every suite (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, `TC`, `VALL` and `REAL`, and write each command with its result lines into `after.txt`. Verify: the build and `TC` exit 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed with more passed tests than `$SP/before.txt`, and the `REAL` lines are written beside their `before.txt` lines with the difference stated as a count, or as `embedder not live`. A lower real count does not block this task. When the `combined` count of the real sealed plain line is lower than its before line, write `DROP: real plain holdout <before> to <after>`, then find the cause in the working tree and write it: change the T010 line back to `cue === null`, rebuild, run `REAL` and write `cause: T010` when the count returns. When it does not return, put the T010 line back, remove T007's `&& recommendation.uncertainty <= uncertaintyThreshold`, rebuild, run `REAL` and write `cause: T007` when the count returns and `cause: unknown` otherwise. Put every line back, rebuild, and see `G diff --stat -- $FU` print the same line it printed before the check. `rg -c -e '^DROP: ' $SP/after.txt` and `rg -c -e '^cause: (T007|T010|unknown)$' $SP/after.txt` print the same count, or both print nothing. Evidence: `after.txt`: build exit 0, `TC` exit 0. First `VALL` failed 2 cases of `tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` only (sv-09, sv-11, sv-12 no longer offered, the intended change), slice baseline recaptured (decision P020), rerun `Test Files  184 passed (184)`, `Tests  1919 passed | 6 skipped`, 81 more than 1838. `REAL` plain holdout 5 to 4, `DROP: real plain holdout 5 to 4`, `cause: T007` (removing the weak-cue bar left 4, removing the uncertainty bar returned 5), every line restored, rebuilt, `G diff --stat -- $FU` unchanged. `rg -c` of DROP and cause both print 1.\n187:- [x] CHK-022 [P0] Each of T003 to T010 and T017 recorded a failing first run for the reason its line names. Evidence: each task evidence line names its failing first run, and each Opus check confirmed the test-first order from the worker log.\n188:- [x] CHK-023 [P1] The six request prompts and the five controls keep their command (T003, T014). Evidence: REQUEST6 and CONTROL5 return `false` in `CAG` (104 passed), and `/speckit:complete` stays on its request line in `repro-after.txt` (T014).\n197:- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Finding classes: A-8, B-9 first half and B-3 are `class-of-bug` (every path that attaches a command), A-4 and A-6 are `cross-consumer` (the scorer against the hooks, the phrase path against the hand-off) and A-5 is `algorithmic`. Evidence: the plan addendum classes the findings as written here, and T003 to T005, T018 gate every attach path.\n200:- [x] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The mention reader has adversarial cases: a longer command name, two commands, a curly apostrophe, `don't forget to run`, a refusal in a later clause, a refusal word before a comma, `never mind`, a yes or no question and `can you run` (T003). Evidence: `CAG` holds the longer name, two commands, curly apostrophe, `don't forget to run`, later-clause refusal, refusal before a comma, `never mind`, yes or no question and `can you run` cases, 104 passed (T003).\n201:- [x] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix: three attach paths by two readings (refused, asked about) by one request control, covered by T003 to T005, T008, T017 and T018. Evidence: the three attach paths by refused and asked-about readings and one request control are covered in `CAG` and `TCO`, all passing.\n211:- [x] CHK-030 [P0] The command name is escaped before it enters a pattern (T003). Evidence: `commandOnlyMentioned` passes the command through `escapePhrase` before `new RegExp` (`CA` line 401).\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"3:description: \"Ordered worker-sized tasks that withhold a command where none fits: a mention reader in the attach module, a small-edit gate, an uncertainty bar on the meaning pass, a no-edit gate on commands that write and a weak-cue bar on the doctor hand-off, each with a test written first.\"\n54:Worker lanes. Lane A owns `CA` and `CAG`. Lane B owns `FU`, `CMA`, `DHC` and `TCO`. Lane C owns `DH`. Lane A runs T003 to T006 in order. Lane B runs T007, T008, T017, T018, T009 and T010 in that order and starts T008 only after T003 is verified, because T008 imports the function T003 adds. Lane C runs T011 after T010. `[P]` marks only the first task of lane A and of lane B, which may start side by side. Every other task waits for the task before it in its lane.\n74:- [x] T003 [P] Add the mention reader `commandOnlyMentioned` (`CA`, `CAG`). Before any edit run `node $PL/probe-mention-leads.mjs | tail -1` and see `RESULT: 24 of 24 agree`, which proves the pattern sources below on every case this task names, and run `node $PL/probe-mention-leads-loose.mjs` and see four lines that start `loose reading returns true`, which is the reading this task must not write. Test first: in `CAG`, add `describe('a command the prompt only mentions')` with `it.each(REFUSE8)('reads %s as a mention of %s', ...)` expecting `commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)` to be `true`, `it.each(QUESTION2)('reads the question %s as a mention of %s', ...)` expecting `true`, `it.each(REQUEST6)('reads %s as a request for %s', ...)` expecting `false`, `it.each(CONTROL5)('reads %s as a request for %s beside a refusal word', ...)` expecting `false`, `it('reads each command of a two-command prompt on its own')` expecting `commandOnlyMentioned('use /speckit:plan, not /speckit:complete', '/speckit:complete')` to be `true`, `it('reads a curly apostrophe as a straight one')` expecting `commandOnlyMentioned('don’t run /speckit:save', '/speckit:save')` to be `true`, and `it('does not read a longer command name as the shorter one')` expecting `commandOnlyMentioned('do not run /create:sk-skill-parent', '/create:sk-skill')` to be `false`. Import `commandOnlyMentioned` beside `isNoEditRequest`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the file fail on the missing export. Then in `CA`, below `isNoEditRequest`, add two constants, two exported lists and the function. Copy the four pattern values character for character from `$PL/probe-mention-leads.mjs`, where they are named `USE`, `GAP`, `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS` and `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS`, and name the first two `COMMAND_USE_VERB` and `COMMAND_GAP_WORDS`. `COMMAND_USE_VERB` is the string `(?:run|start|use|invoke|launch|execute|call|trigger|open|rerun|re-run|kick off)`. `COMMAND_GAP_WORDS` is the string `(?:[a-z']+ ){0,2}`: a gap word is one or more of the letters a to z and the apostrophe followed by one space, so a gap never crosses a comma, a digit, a slash or any other punctuation. Do not write `\\S+` or `\\w+` for a gap word. `COMMAND_DECLINE_LEADS` holds two pattern sources. The first is `(?:do not|don't|dont|never|not|won't|wont|no longer|cannot|can't) `, then the lookahead `(?!(?:forget|hesitate|fail|mind)\\b)`, then `COMMAND_GAP_WORDS`, then `COMMAND_USE_VERB`, then one space, then `COMMAND_GAP_WORDS`. The second is the bare lead `(?:skip|skipping|without|instead of|rather than|avoid|not) ` followed by at most two gap words of which none is a use verb, written `(?:(?!USE\\b)[a-z']+ ){0,2}` with `COMMAND_USE_VERB` in the place of `USE`. `COMMAND_ASK_LEADS` holds three pattern sources. The first is `(?:what does|what is|what's|what would|what will|what did|how does|how did|why does|why did|explain|describe|tell me what|tell me how|tell me about|tell me why|difference between|differ from|differs from|different from|undo what|ran|already ran|was running) (?:the )?(?:command )?`. The second is `(?:should i|should we|do i need to|when would i) `, then `COMMAND_USE_VERB`, then ` (?:the )?(?:command )?`. The third is `(?:is|does|can|will|would) `, which matches only when the command follows it directly. `commandOnlyMentioned(prompt: string, command: string): boolean` lower-cases the prompt, folds `‘` and `’` to `'`, collapses whitespace runs to one space, lower-cases the command, escapes it with `escapePhrase` and returns whether, for one lead of the two lists, the pattern `(?:^|[^a-z0-9_/])` then the lead then the escaped command then `(?![a-z0-9_-])` matches the text. Give each list a comment saying a command the reader refuses or asks about is named without being asked for, that a lead must sit directly before the command so a later clause cannot refuse an earlier request, and that a gap holds plain words only so a refusal before a comma cannot swallow the request after it. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `TC` exits 0, `rg -c \"^import\" $CA` prints nothing and `rg -c -F \"[a-z']+ ){0,2}\" $CA` prints at least 1. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). The new cases failed first with `commandOnlyMentioned is not a function` (24 failed), then `Tests  62 passed (62)`, `TC` exit 0, `rg -c \"^import\"` printed nothing and the gap pattern count printed 2. The decline and ask lists equal the probe's by value, `probe-mention-leads.mjs` printed `RESULT: 24 of 24 agree`. The worker also exported the two shared constants, which changes no behaviour.\n75:- [x] T004 Withhold a mentioned command on the typed path (`CA`, `CAG`). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('typed command boundaries')`, add `it('delivers no typed command the prompt refuses')` expecting `typedCommandForTop('system-spec-kit', 'do not run /speckit:complete yet, just explain what it does')` to be `undefined`, and `it('still delivers a typed command the prompt asks for')` expecting `typedCommandForTop('system-spec-kit', 'run /speckit:complete for the rate limiter')?.command` to be `'/speckit:complete'`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the first case return an object. Then in `CA`'s `typedCommandForTop`, after the line that returns `undefined` for an untracked command, add `if (commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)) return undefined;`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). One line added after the untracked-command return, the refusal case returned an object at the old logic (`old= /speckit:complete new= undefined`), then `Tests  64 passed (64)`, `tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` 10 passed, `TC` exit 0. Two misses the verifier found in the T003 lists are fixed in T020.\n76:- [x] T005 Withhold a mentioned command on the hub attach path (`CA`, `CAG`). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('a command the prompt only mentions')`, add `it.each(['what does /create:readme do?', 'skip /create:readme, just append one line to the existing README'])('offers no hub command for %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), prompt)` to be `undefined`, `it('offers no deep-loop command the prompt refuses')` expecting `attachCommand('system-deep-loop', SINGLE(mode), 'please do not start /deep:research, I only want a two line summary of the readme')` to be `undefined`, where `mode` is the key of `MODE_COMMANDS['system-deep-loop']` whose value is `/deep:research`, and `it('still offers the hub command a plain request routes to')` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), 'write a readme for the doctor scripts folder')` to be `'/create:readme'`. Run the file and see the three refusal cases return a command. Then in `CA`'s `attachCommand`, after the two own-key lookups and before the deep-loop block, add `if (commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, commands[workflowMode])) return undefined;` with a comment saying a route that picked the mode because the prompt named its command must not offer a command the reader refused or asked about. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). The guard sits after the second own-key lookup and before the deep-loop block, a helper probe showed all three refusal prompts would have returned a command without it, then `Tests  68 passed (68)`, `tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` 10 passed, `TC` exit 0. A prompt that refuses and later asks for the same command is fixed in T020.\n77:- [x] T006 Withhold a creation command from a small in-place edit (`CA`, `CAG`). Test first: in `CAG`, add `describe('command attach on a small edit')` with `it.each(['update the README typo in line 3', 'fix the typo in the README', 'correct the spelling in the hooks readme', 'fix the broken link in the install guide readme'])('offers no creation command for %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), prompt)` to be `undefined`, `it.each(['write a readme for the doctor scripts folder', 'create a readme for the payments module, check it for typos when done'])('still offers the creation command for %s', ...)` expecting `'/create:readme'`, and `it('leaves a command outside the create namespace alone')` expecting `attachCommand('system-deep-loop', SINGLE(mode), 'do a thorough deep review of the typo handling')` to be `'/deep:review'`, where `mode` is the key whose value is `/deep:review`. Run the file and see the four small-edit cases return `/create:readme`. Then in `CA`, below `DEPTH_WORDING`, add `export const SMALL_EDIT_WORDING: readonly string[]` holding `typo`, `typos`, `spelling`, `misspelled`, `misspelling`, `grammar`, `punctuation`, `wording`, `broken link`, `dead link`, `one line` and `single line`, with a comment saying a creation workflow scaffolds, reviews and validates a whole document, which is the wrong size for a correction inside one. Build `SMALL_EDIT_REQUEST` from it as `DEPTH_REQUEST` is built, with `line \\\\d+` as one more alternative, and `CREATION_REQUEST` as `/\\b(?:create|write|author|draft|scaffold|generate|make|new)\\b/`. In `attachCommand`, after the mention gate, add `if (commands[workflowMode].startsWith('/create:') && SMALL_EDIT_REQUEST.test(prompt.toLowerCase()) && !CREATION_REQUEST.test(prompt.toLowerCase())) return undefined;`. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, verified as part of the chain. The small-edit gate took five tasks: T006 built it, three Opus checks failed it on creation requests that lost their command (T021 and T022 patched it), T024 inverted it at the retry bound to a list of gated commands and T026 left the repo-rule and benchmark commands out. Final state: `/create:readme`, `/create:feature-catalog` and `/create:manual-testing-playbook` are gated, the T024 check ran 41 listed prompts and 16 of its own with one realistic miss, which T026 fixed.\n79:- [x] T021 Narrow the small-edit gate to whole-document creation commands and widen its creation verbs (`CA`, `CAG`). After T006, before T020. Added after the Opus check of T006 found realistic creation requests that lose their command, decided without the operator (D1). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a small edit')`, add `it.each([['sk-doc', 'sk-create-agent', 'build an agent that fixes typos in our docs'], ['sk-doc', 'sk-create-readme', 'writing a readme for the grammar module'], ['sk-doc', 'sk-create-readme', 'add a readme for the spelling package'], ['sk-doc', 'sk-create-changelog', 'add a changelog entry for the typo fixes in the cli help']])('still offers the creation command on %s %s for %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand(skill, SINGLE(mode), prompt)` to be the value of that mode in the command table the existing kept cases read (use the same lookup they use, and when a mode key named here does not exist in that table, take the key whose command is `/create:agent`, `/create:readme` or `/create:changelog` and say so in the report), and `it('leaves the wording commands outside the gate')` expecting the mode whose command is `/create:with-human-voice` to return that command for `humanize the wording in the onboarding guide`, and `it.each(['fix the broken links in the install guide readme', 'fix the dead links in the hooks readme'])('offers no creation command for %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE('sk-create-readme'), prompt)` to be `undefined`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the new cases fail. Then in `CA`: (1) add, below `CREATION_REQUEST`, `const SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set(['/create:with-human-voice', '/create:diff']);` with a comment saying these two commands exist to work on wording that is already there, so a correction word fits them; in `attachCommand` change the gate condition `commands[workflowMode].startsWith('/create:')` to `commands[workflowMode].startsWith('/create:') && !SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS.has(commands[workflowMode])`; (2) replace the `CREATION_REQUEST` pattern with `/\\b(?:creat(?:e|es|ing)|writ(?:e|es|ing)|author(?:ing)?|draft(?:ing)?|scaffold(?:ing)?|generat(?:e|es|ing)|mak(?:e|es|ing)|new|build(?:ing)?|set up|add an?|need an?)\\b/`; (3) add `'broken links'` and `'dead links'` to `SMALL_EDIT_WORDING`. Change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `rg -c 'SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS' $CA` prints 2 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, Opus check FAIL (3 of 14 false positives left), superseded in part by T022 and T024.\n80:- [x] T022 Withhold a creation command only on a correction verb, and exempt the changelog and goal commands (`CA`, `CAG`). After T021, before T020. Added after the Opus check of T021 found that changelog, goal and noun-led requests still lose their command, decided without the operator (D1). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a small edit')`, add `it.each([['sk-create-changelog', 'changelog for v2.1, it fixes the broken link checker and spelling errors'], ['sk-create-changelog', 'log the spelling fixes in the changelog'], ['sk-create-readme', 'document the cli in a readme, each flag gets a one line description'], ['sk-create-readme', 'readme for the spelling package'], ['sk-create-agent', 'an agent that fixes typos']])('keeps the creation command for %s on %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE(mode), prompt)` to equal `MODE_COMMANDS['sk-doc'][mode]`, and `it('keeps the goal command when the goal is about fixes')` expecting the sk-doc mode whose command is `/create:goal` to return `/create:goal` for `set a goal to fix all the typos in the docs`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the new cases fail and every older case pass. Then in `CA`: (1) add `'/create:changelog'` and `'/create:goal'` to `SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS` and extend its comment with one sentence saying a changelog or a goal describes fixes, so a correction word is its content; (2) below `CREATION_REQUEST` add `const CORRECTION_VERB = /\\b(?:fix|correct|update|edit|change|tweak|repair)\\b/;` with a one-line comment saying a small edit names the correction to make, and in `attachCommand` add `&& CORRECTION_VERB.test(prompt.toLowerCase())` to the small-edit gate condition. Change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `rg -c 'CORRECTION_VERB' $CA` prints 2 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, Opus check FAIL (agent, skill and command requests whose purpose names a correction lost their command), the exemption list it extended was replaced in T024, its `CORRECTION_VERB` stays.\n81:- [x] T024 Gate only the document commands a small edit corrects in place (`CA`, `CAG`). After T022, before T020. Added after the third Opus check of the small-edit gate found that a request for an agent, skill or command whose purpose names a correction (`an agent to fix typos`) lost its command. Three fixes of one symptom reached the retry bound, so the design is inverted once, decided without the operator (D1): if this check also finds a common miss, the gate is removed instead. Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a small edit')`, add `it.each([['sk-create-agent', 'an agent to fix typos'], ['sk-create-agent', 'give me an agent to fix broken links in the docs'], ['sk-create-agent', 'I want an agent to correct spelling in pull requests']])('keeps the creation command for %s on %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE(mode), prompt)` to equal `MODE_COMMANDS['sk-doc'][mode]`, plus one case each for the sk-doc modes whose commands are `/create:sk-skill` (`a skill to correct spelling in markdown`) and `/create:command` (`I'd like a command to fix dead links`), found by value in `MODE_COMMANDS['sk-doc']` and expecting that command. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the new cases fail. Then in `CA`: replace `SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS` and its comment with `const SMALL_EDIT_GATED_COMMANDS: ReadonlySet<string> = new Set(['/create:readme', '/create:feature-catalog', '/create:manual-testing-playbook', '/create:repo-rule', '/create:benchmark']);` and a comment saying these commands write a document that is later corrected in place, so a correction request names an edit to it rather than a new one, and in `attachCommand` replace the condition `commands[workflowMode].startsWith('/create:') && !SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS.has(commands[workflowMode])` with `SMALL_EDIT_GATED_COMMANDS.has(commands[workflowMode])`. Keep `SMALL_EDIT_REQUEST`, `CREATION_REQUEST` and `CORRECTION_VERB` as they are. Change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `rg -c 'SMALL_EDIT_EXEMPT_COMMANDS' $CA` prints nothing, `rg -c 'SMALL_EDIT_GATED_COMMANDS' $CA` prints 2 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS): `Tests  93 passed (93)`, `TC` exit 0, 41 of 41 listed prompts as expected, one realistic miss (repo rule) fixed in T026.\n82:- [x] T026 Leave the repo-rule and benchmark commands out of the small-edit gate (`CA`, `CAG`). After T024, before T020. Added after the Opus check of T024 (PASS) found that a repo rule or a benchmark names its purpose the way an agent does, so `I want a repo rule that says fix typos in the same commit` lost `/create:repo-rule`. Decided without the operator (D1). Test first: in `CAG`, inside `describe('command attach on a small edit')`, add `it.each(['I want a repo rule that says fix typos in the same commit', 'repo rule: always fix typos in the same commit'])('keeps the repo-rule command on %s', ...)` expecting `attachCommand('sk-doc', SINGLE(mode), prompt)` to be `/create:repo-rule`, where `mode` is the key of `MODE_COMMANDS['sk-doc']` whose value is `/create:repo-rule`, and `it('keeps the benchmark command on benchmark how fast we fix typos')` the same way for `/create:benchmark`. When either command is absent from `MODE_COMMANDS['sk-doc']`, take the table that holds it and say so. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the new cases fail. Then in `CA`, remove `'/create:repo-rule'` and `'/create:benchmark'` from `SMALL_EDIT_GATED_COMMANDS`, leaving the other three, and change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `rg -c \"'/create:repo-rule'\" $CA` prints nothing and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, checked by the coordinator. The gated set holds the three document commands, `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  96 passed (96)`, `command-attach` 10 and `command-brief-golden` 13 passed, `TC` exit 0. Deviation: the `rg` check prints 2