ead from the split constant, and `TC` exits 0. Evidence so far: DeepSeek worker, Opus check FAIL on the line-break sentence end, all 13 named prompts correct, `Tests  99 passed (99)`, `TC` exit 0. Finished by T028. Evidence: rejected once by the Opus check, then fixed by T028. The Opus check of T020 with T028 (2026-11-14) printed `Tests  104 passed (104)` for `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `TC` exit 0, and a probe of REFUSE8, REQUEST6, QUESTION2, CONTROL5 and the T020 cases gave 32 of 32 right results.\n84:- [x] T028 End a sentence at a line break, and read a bare ask lead that opens a sentence as a question (`CA`, `CAG`). After T020. Added after the Opus check of T020 (FAIL) found that whitespace folding turns a line break into a space, so a `?` on a later line still counts, and that chat questions without `?` (`is /speckit:resume safe to run twice`, rows sv-09, sv-11 and sv-12) now read as requests. Decided without the operator (D1). Test first: in `CAG`, in the `it.each` T020 added that expects `false`, add `['the next step is /speckit:implement\\nany questions?', '/speckit:implement']`, and add `it.each([['is /speckit:resume safe to run twice', '/speckit:resume'], ['does /doctor:git change files or just report problems', '/doctor:git'], ['can /prompt:improve make a vague request easier to follow', '/prompt:improve'], ['ok. is /speckit:plan enough here', '/speckit:plan']])('reads %s as a question about %s', ...)` expecting `commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)` to be `true`. Run `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` and see the five new cases fail. Then in `CA`'s `commandOnlyMentioned`: fold the text so line breaks survive (`.replace(/[^\\S\\n]+/g, ' ').replace(/ *\\n\\s*/g, '\\n')` in place of the current whitespace collapse), end a sentence at `.`, `!` or `\\n`, and accept the bare lead `COMMAND_BARE_ASK_LEAD` when a `?` follows the command before the sentence end OR when the lead starts the prompt or directly follows a sentence end. Change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: Opus check PASS 2026-11-14: `VX tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  104 passed (104)`, `tests/command-attach.vitest.ts` with `tests/command-brief-golden.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  23 passed (23)`, `TC` exit 0, comment grep exit 1. Accepted limit, decided without the operator: `?` and `,` do not end a sentence, so `quick question? is /speckit:resume safe to run twice` and `ok, is /speckit:plan enough here` read as requests. Both follow the sentence-end set this task names.\n88:- [x] T008 Add the gate that stops a mentioned command's own row (`FU`, `CMA`). Start after T003 is verified. This task adds the function `withholdMentionedCommands` and nothing else. T017 and T018 change the two functions that use the reader. Test first: in `CMA`, add `describe('withholdMentionedCommands')` with a passing command row `command-speckit-complete` and a passing skill row `system-spec-kit`, built with the row helper the neighbouring cases use. Expect `withholdMentionedCommands(rows, 'do not run /speckit:complete yet, just explain what it does')` to return the command row with `passes_threshold` `false` and the skill row unchanged, expect the same call with `run /speckit:complete for the rate limiter` to return both rows unchanged, expect the same call with `is /speckit:complete overkill for a two line fix?` to return the command row with `passes_threshold` `false`, and expect a passing row `command-doctor-env` with the prompt `do not run /doctor:env on this machine` to stop passing, which proves a command with a subcommand is matched by its base. Run `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` and see it fail on the missing export. Then in `FU`, add `commandOnlyMentioned` and `commandRowFor` to the import from `'../command-attach.js'`, and add `export function withholdMentionedCommands(ranked: readonly AdvisorScoredRecommendation[], prompt: string): AdvisorScoredRecommendation[]` directly above `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`. It maps each passing `kind === 'command'` row whose `commandRowFor(row.skill)?.command.split(' ')[0]` satisfies `commandOnlyMentioned(prompt, command)` to `{ ...row, passes_threshold: false }` and returns every other row as it is. Give it a comment saying a command row passes on its typed name, so a prompt that names the command to refuse it would otherwise pass that row. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c \"^export function withholdMentionedCommands\" $FU` prints 1 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). First run `4 failed | 20 passed (24)` on the missing export, then `Tests  24 passed (24)`, the export count printed 1, `TC` exit 0. Accepted limit, decided without the operator (D1): rows match on the base name, so refusing one subcommand of a family (`/doctor:ci toggle`) also withholds a sibling the same prompt asks for. A prompt that explains and then asks for one command is fixed in T020.\n89:- [x] T017 Leave a refused typed command's owner where it ranked (`FU`, `TCO`). After T008. This task changes the function `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst` and nothing else. Test first: in `TCO`, inside `describe('a typed command without a scorer row leads through its owner')`, add `it('keeps the order when the prompt refuses the typed command')` with `const ranked = [recommendation('sk-code'), recommendation('sk-doc'), recommendation('sk-prompt')];` expecting `rankedSkills(ranked, 'do not run /create:goal')` to equal `['sk-code', 'sk-doc', 'sk-prompt']`. Run `VX tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` and see the case fail with `['sk-doc', 'sk-code', 'sk-prompt']`, the order the planning probe printed. Then in `FU`'s `rankTypedCommandOwnerFirst`, directly after the line `if (command === undefined || !Object.hasOwn(TRACKED_COMMANDS, command)) return [...ranked];`, add `if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];` with a comment saying a command the reader refused must not pull its owner to the front. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed, `rg -c -F 'if (commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, command)) return [...ranked];' $FU` prints 1 and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). The guard sits after the tracked-command line, `tests/scorer/typed-command-owner.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  5 passed (5)`, the guard count printed 1, `TC` exit 0. A probe kept the order on refusals in upper case, with a curly apostrophe and with a mode suffix, and still pulled the owner forward on a real request. Accepted limit, decided without the operator (D1): a refusal of the retired alias `/create:skill` is not read as one, because the typed name resolves to `/create:sk-skill` first. It predates this phase.\n92:- [x] T023 Keep a writing command the prompt types and asks for on a no-edit request (`FU`, `CMA`). After T009, before T010. Added after the Opus check of T009 found that a scope limit such as `do not touch the code` withheld a command the user typed and asked for, decided without the operator (D1). Test first: in `CMA`, inside `describe('withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit')`, add `it('keeps a writing command the prompt types and asks for')` with the same passing rows the neighbouring case builds, expecting `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit(rows, 'run /speckit:complete for the rate limiter, do not change the public api')` to leave `command-speckit-complete` passing, and `it('still withholds a writing command the prompt only names')` expecting the same call with `do not run /speckit:complete, and do not change anything` to leave it not passing. Run `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` and see the first new case fail. Then in `FU`'s `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit`, inside the per-row check and before a row is un-passed, compute `const base = commandRowFor(recommendation.skill)?.command.split(' ')[0];` and return the row unchanged when `base !== undefined && typedCommandIn(promptLower) === base && !commandOnlyMentioned(promptLower, base)`, importing `typedCommandIn` from `../command-attach.js` when it is not already imported. Add a one-line comment saying a command the reader typed and asked for is the request, and the no-edit words limit its scope. Use the variable names the function already has. Change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/scorer/doctor-ordering.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` report 0 failed and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). Through the real `scoreAdvisorPrompt`, the three typed-and-asked prompts keep `command-speckit-save`, `command-speckit-complete` and `command-doctor-speckit` passing, and the two true no-edit prompts pass no writing command. Accepted limit (D1): a no-edit prompt that types two commands and refuses the longer one still withholds the one it asks for, because the typed-command reader returns only the longest name.\n93:- [x] T010 Stop a weak cue from lowering the hand-off bar (`FU`, `DHC`). Test first: in `DHC`, with the scoring helper the existing cases use and no passing skill, add `it.each(['the environment variable for the database url is missing in production', 'the install step in our dockerfile is broken, the overlay filesystem is stale'])('hands off no doctor command for the app problem %s', ...)` expecting no passing row whose id starts `command-doctor-`, and `it.each([['AGENTS.md is missing the shipped sections', 'command-doctor-agents-md-check'], ['the runtime mirrors are out of sync with .skilled', 'command-doctor-runtime-mirrors']])('still hands off %s', ...)` expecting that id to pass