ue bar of 9 separates them. Test first: in `DHC`, in the `it.each` T010 added for `still hands off %s`, replace the row `['the runtime mirrors are out of sync with .skilled', <its id>]` with `['the symlink to the skilled checkout is broken', <the id runnableDoctorBridgeId returns for /doctor:symlink link>]`, keeping the AGENTS.md row. Run `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` and see the two app-problem cases fail. If the symlink row also fails before the code change for a reason other than the bar, mark the task `[B]` with the printed line. Then in `DH`, directly below `export const DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE = 10;`, add `export const DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE = 9;` with a comment saying a weak cue is a bare word ordinary work also uses, so it needs a stronger ranker match than a strong cue, though less than no cue. In `FU`, add `DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE` to the import list that already holds `DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE`, then in `applyDoctorHelperHandoff`, directly after the line `if (match && cue === null && match.score < DOCTOR_HELPER_UNCUED_MIN_SCORE) return [...ranked];` add `if (match && cue === 'weak' && match.score < DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE) return [...ranked];`. Leave the no-cue line as it is. Change nothing else. Verify: the first run fails as described, then `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/doctor-helper-handoff.vitest.ts`, `VX tests/doctor-routing-slice.vitest.ts` and `VX tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` report 0 failed, `rg -c 'DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE' $FU` prints 2, `rg -c 'DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE' $DH` prints 1 and `TC` exits 0. When a slice test fails because a tune row lost its doctor command, mark the task `[B]` with the row id and remove the added line. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, then an Opus verifier (PASS). `doctor-handoff-command` 16 passed, `doctor-helper-handoff` 16, `doctor-routing-slice` 2 (the tune row keeps `/doctor:agents-md check`), `TC` exit 0. A probe shows the two app problems hand off nothing at 8.361 and 6.529, and the symlink control resolves to `command-doctor-helper` because `/doctor:symlink link` is an ask route. Limit: no unit case sits between 9 and 10, so only the slice tune row pins the weak-cue bar.\n97:- [x] T011 State the weak-cue rule in the hand-off module header (`DH`). After T010. In the numbered comment block at the top of the file, the sentence sits on two comment lines: the line that ends `leads. With no skill passing, a strong ranker match stands in for the` and the next line `//      cue.`. Replace the words `With no skill passing, a strong ranker match stands in for the` and the `cue.` on the next line with `With no skill passing, a weak cue or no cue needs a strong ranker match,` and a next comment line `//      and only a strong cue hands off on the lower score.`, keeping the `leads.` that starts the first line and the comment indentation. Verify: `rg -c \"only a strong cue hands off on the lower score\" $DH` prints 1, `rg -c \"stands in for the cue\" $DH` prints nothing and `TC` exits 0. Evidence: DeepSeek worker, checked by the coordinator. The two comment lines carry the new sentence, `rg -c \"only a strong cue hands off on the lower score\" $DH` printed 1, `rg -c \"stands in for the cue\" $DH` printed nothing, `TC` exit 0. The sentence stays true with the weak-cue bar of 9 that T025 added, because a weak cue still needs more than the strong-cue bar.\n98:- [x] T027 Correct the weak-cue comment in the hand-off test (`DHC`). After T011. Added after the Opus check of T025 found the comment above the app-problem `it.each` still says a weak cue earns no lower bar than a prompt with no cue, which is false since the weak-cue bar is 9 and the no-cue bar is 10. Replace that comment with `// A bare word that ordinary work also uses is a weak cue, so it needs a stronger ranker match than a strong cue.` keeping the indentation, and change nothing else. Verify: `rg -c 'earns no lower bar' $ADV/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` prints nothing, `rg -c 'needs a stronger ranker match than a strong cue' $ADV/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` prints 1 and `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` reports 0 failed. Evidence: coordinator check 2026-11-14: `rg -c 'earns no lower bar'` printed nothing (exit 1), `rg -c 'needs a stronger ranker match than a strong cue'` printed 1, `VX tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` printed `Tests  16 passed (16)`.\n105:<!-- FILL: Write one verification task per requirement. Each one runs a command. GOOD: T003 Run both invocations. Verify: `ls logs/archive | wc -l` prints 3 and 10. WEAK: T003 Test everything. -->\n107:- [x] T012 [C] Rebuild and run every suite (`$SP/after.txt`). Run `npm run build` in `ADV`, `TC`, `VALL` and `REAL`, and write each command with its result lines into `after.txt`. Verify: the build and `TC` exit 0, `VALL` reports 0 failed with more passed tests than `$SP/before.txt`, and the `REAL` lines are written beside their `before.txt` lines with the difference stated as a count, or as `embedder not live`. A lower real count does not block this task. When the `combined` count of the real sealed plain line is lower than its before line, write `DROP: real plain holdout <before> to <after>`, then find the cause in the working tree and write it: change the T010 line back to `cue === null`, rebuild, run `REAL` and write `cause: T010` when the count returns. When it does not return, put the T010 line back, remove T007's `&& recommendation.uncertainty <= uncertaintyThreshold`, rebuild, run `REAL` and write `cause: T007` when the count returns and `cause: unknown` otherwise. Put every line back, rebuild, and see `G diff --stat -- $FU` print the same line it printed before the check. `rg -c -e '^DROP: ' $SP/after.txt` and `rg -c -e '^cause: (T007|T010|unknown)$' $SP/after.txt` print the same count, or both print nothing. Evidence: `after.txt`: build exit 0, `TC` exit 0. First `VALL` failed 2 cases of `tests/command-routing-slice.vitest.ts` only (sv-09, sv-11, sv-12 no longer offered, the intended change), slice baseline recaptured (decision P020), rerun `Test Files  184 passed (184)`, `Tests  1919 passed | 6 skipped`, 81 more than 1838. `REAL` plain holdout 5 to 4, `DROP: real plain holdout 5 to 4`, `cause: T007` (removing the weak-cue bar left 4, removing the uncertainty bar returned 5), every line restored, rebuilt, `G diff --stat -- $FU` unchanged. `rg -c` of DROP and cause both print 1.\n187:- [x] CHK-022 [P0] Each of T003 to T010 and T017 recorded a failing first run for the reason its line names. Evidence: each task evidence line names its failing first run, and each Opus check confirmed the test-first order from the worker log.\n188:- [x] CHK-023 [P1] The six request prompts and the five controls keep their command (T003, T014). Evidence: REQUEST6 and CONTROL5 return `false` in `CAG` (104 passed), and `/speckit:complete` stays on its request line in `repro-after.txt` (T014).\n197:- [x] CHK-FIX-001 [P0] Finding classes: A-8, B-9 first half and B-3 are `class-of-bug` (every path that attaches a command), A-4 and A-6 are `cross-consumer` (the scorer against the hooks, the phrase path against the hand-off) and A-5 is `algorithmic`. Evidence: the plan addendum classes the findings as written here, and T003 to T005, T018 gate every attach path.\n200:- [x] CHK-FIX-004 [P1] The mention reader has adversarial cases: a longer command name, two commands, a curly apostrophe, `don't forget to run`, a refusal in a later clause, a refusal word before a comma, `never mind`, a yes or no question and `can you run` (T003). Evidence: `CAG` holds the longer name, two commands, curly apostrophe, `don't forget to run`, later-clause refusal, refusal before a comma, `never mind`, yes or no question and `can you run` cases, 104 passed (T003).\n201:- [x] CHK-FIX-005 [P1] Matrix: three attach paths by two readings (refused, asked about) by one request control, covered by T003 to T005, T008, T017 and T018. Evidence: the three attach paths by refused and asked-about readings and one request control are covered in `CAG` and `TCO`, all passing.\n211:- [x] CHK-030 [P0] The command name is escaped before it enters a pattern (T003). Evidence: `commandOnlyMentioned` passes the command through `escapePhrase` before `new RegExp` (`CA` line 401).\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"REQ-003\\\\|REQ-004\\\\|REQ-006\\\\|REQ-007\\\\|commandOnlyMentioned\\\\|small-edit\\\\|weak cue\\\\|T003\\\\|T006\\\\|T010\\\\|T011\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/tasks.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670492524,"end":1794670492650}}}}
