{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1794670549344,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"id":"prt_1dab35960001laTFImOkyoWKoV","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1dab347da0010x39oV92lrKIFk","type":"step-start","snapshot":"379199085cdc82d9f8106f5a17032d5bc116bcdd"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670564415,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab393510010XPXCsVB3bHWvB","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1dab347da0010x39oV92lrKIFk","type":"tool","id":"call_00_mnlc9ihuq8l6x8xn7640qlx6","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md | sed -n '33,41p'; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md | sed -n '60,68p'; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts | sed -n '168,200p'"},"output":"    33\tWhen a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n    34\t\n    35\tThe request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that defaults to true. When a caller passes `false` the handler skips `enrichCompiledRoutes()` on both the fresh and the cached return (the two `input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false` checks in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`), so no `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess starts and no recommendation carries `compiledRoute` or `command`. The prompt hooks pass `true` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238`), because the `command` field is derived from the compiled route. The OpenCode plugin does not pass the option and keeps receiving `compiledRoute`. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:23`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:57`).\n    36\t\n    37\tThe request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n    38\t\n    39\tA hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row. `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered, so one command never takes two slots.\n    40\t\n    41\t### Recommendation Contract (`kind`, `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId`)\n    60\t\n    61\t### Validation And Tests\n    62\t\n    63\t| File | Type | Role |\n    64\t|---|---|---|\n    65\t| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Vitest | 17 cases: cosine bar, margin, stand-in refusal, eligibility and ranking rule |\n    66\t| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Generated bridge file matches the deriver |\n    67\t\n    68\t---\n   168\t    const command = '/create:agent';\n   169\t    const mode = Object.entries(MODE_COMMANDS['sk-doc']).find(([, value]) => value === command)?.[0];\n   170\t    expect(mode, 'sk-doc declares a mode for /create:agent').toBeTruthy();\n   171\t    mockedChild.execFileSync.mockReturnValue(JSON.stringify({\n   172\t      action: 'route',\n   173\t      hubId: 'sk-doc',\n   174\t      selectionKind: 'single',\n   175\t      targets: [{ workflowMode: mode }],\n   176\t    }));\n   177\t\n   178\t    const topOnly = responseData(await handleAdvisorRecommend({\n   179\t      prompt: corpusRow.prompt,\n   180\t      options: { includeCompiledRoute: true, compiledRouteTopOnly: true },\n   181\t    })).data?.recommendations ?? [];\n   182\t    expect(topOnly[0]?.skillId).toBe('sk-doc');\n   183\t    expect(topOnly[0]?.command).toBe(command);\n   184\t    expect(topOnly.slice(1).map((row) => row.skillId)).toContain('create:agent');\n   185\t\n   186\t    const everyRow = responseData(await handleAdvisorRecommend({\n   187\t      prompt: corpusRow.prompt,\n   188\t      options: { includeCompiledRoute: true },\n   189\t    })).data?.recommendations ?? [];\n   190\t    expect(everyRow[0]?.skillId).toBe('sk-doc');\n   191\t    expect(everyRow[0]?.command).toBe(command);\n   192\t    expect(everyRow[0]?.command).toBe(topOnly[0]?.command);\n   193\t  });\n   194\t\n   195\t  it('marks a hub that needs a mode without marking a hub that has none', async () => {\n   196\t    mockedChild.execFileSync.mockReturnValue(JSON.stringify({\n   197\t      action: 'defer',\n   198\t      hubId: 'sk-doc',\n   199\t      selectionKind: null,\n   200\t      targets: [],\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"    33\tWhen a recommendation gets a `compiledRoute`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` also asks `attachCommand()` in `lib/command-attach.ts` for a slash command and sets the optional `command` field when one comes back (the `command` field of `AdvisorRecommendationSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`, `z.string().min(1).optional()`). `attachCommand()` names a command only for a `route` decision with `selectionKind: 'single'` and exactly one target, and only when the generated `MODE_COMMANDS` table maps that hub and `workflowMode` to a command. A bundle, a multi-target route or a mode with no command leaves `command` off. For `system-deep-loop` the prompt must type the same command or hold a phrase from `DEPTH_WORDING`, so a prompt that only names a topic such as research or review gets no deep-loop command. A prompt that matches `NO_EDIT_REQUEST` gets no command from any hub, because a reader who rules out a change is never handed work that writes.\n    34\t\n    35\tThe request option `options.includeCompiledRoute` is an optional boolean that defaults to true. When a caller passes `false` the handler skips `enrichCompiledRoutes()` on both the fresh and the cached return (the two `input.options?.includeCompiledRoute === false` checks in `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`), so no `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess starts and no recommendation carries `compiledRoute` or `command`. The prompt hooks pass `true` (`hooks/lib/skill-advisor-cli-fallback.ts:238`), because the `command` field is derived from the compiled route. The OpenCode plugin does not pass the option and keeps receiving `compiledRoute`. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:23`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:57`).\n    36\t\n    37\tThe request option `options.compiledRouteTopOnly` is an optional boolean that defaults to false. When a caller passes `true`, `enrichCompiledRoutes()` runs the route lookup for the first recommendation only and returns every later one unchanged, so only the top pick can carry `compiledRoute` or `command`. Each lookup is a `compiled-route.cjs` subprocess, so this saves one subprocess for each further eligible hub. The prompt hooks pass `true` with `includeCompiledRoute: true`, because the brief leads with the top pick. The option is declared in the zod schema (the `options` of `AdvisorRecommendInputSchema` in `schemas/advisor-tool-schemas.ts`), the tool descriptor (`tools/advisor-recommend.ts:24`) and the CLI manifest (`skill-advisor-cli-manifest.ts:58`).\n    38\t\n    39\tA hub also leaves `command` off when the same command already ranks in the result through its own command row. `enrichCompiledRoutes()` takes the `command` fields present in the result as the commands already offered, so one command never takes two slots.\n    40\t\n    41\t### Recommendation Contract (`kind`, `command`, `policy`, `ownerSkillId`)\n    60\t\n    61\t### Validation And Tests\n    62\t\n    63\t| File | Type | Role |\n    64\t|---|---|---|\n    65\t| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts` | Vitest | 17 cases: cosine bar, margin, stand-in refusal, eligibility and ranking rule |\n    66\t| `.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-bridges-drift-guard.vitest.ts` | Vitest | Generated bridge file matches the deriver |\n    67\t\n    68\t---\n   168\t    const command = '/create:agent';\n   169\t    const mode = Object.entries(MODE_COMMANDS['sk-doc']).find(([, value]) => value === command)?.[0];\n   170\t    expect(mode, 'sk-doc declares a mode for /create:agent').toBeTruthy();\n   171\t    mockedChild.execFileSync.mockReturnValue(JSON.stringify({\n   172\t      action: 'route',\n   173\t      hubId: 'sk-doc',\n   174\t      selectionKind: 'single',\n   175\t      targets: [{ workflowMode: mode }],\n   176\t    }));\n   177\t\n   178\t    const topOnly = responseData(await handleAdvisorRecommend({\n   179\t      prompt: corpusRow.prompt,\n   180\t      options: { includeCompiledRoute: true, compiledRouteTopOnly: true },\n   181\t    })).data?.recommendations ?? [];\n   182\t    expect(topOnly[0]?.skillId).toBe('sk-doc');\n   183\t    expect(topOnly[0]?.command).toBe(command);\n   184\t    expect(topOnly.slice(1).map((row) => row.skillId)).toContain('create:agent');\n   185\t\n   186\t    const everyRow = responseData(await handleAdvisorRecommend({\n   187\t      prompt: corpusRow.prompt,\n   188\t      options: { includeCompiledRoute: true },\n   189\t    })).data?.recommendations ?? [];\n   190\t    expect(everyRow[0]?.skillId).toBe('sk-doc');\n   191\t    expect(everyRow[0]?.command).toBe(command);\n   192\t    expect(everyRow[0]?.command).toBe(topOnly[0]?.command);\n   193\t  });\n   194\t\n   195\t  it('marks a hub that needs a mode without marking a hub that has none', async () => {\n   196\t    mockedChild.execFileSync.mockReturnValue(JSON.stringify({\n   197\t      action: 'defer',\n   198\t      hubId: 'sk-doc',\n   199\t      selectionKind: null,\n   200\t      targets: [],\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md | sed -n '33,41p'; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md | sed -n '60,68p'; nl -ba .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/handlers/advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option.vitest.ts | sed -n '168,200p'\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670564177,"end":1794670564415}}}}
