r rules out a change gets its skill and no unfit command, while every typed and plain request that gets its command today keeps it.\n122:| A-5, the two prompts with only a doctor row | A weak cue with no passing skill needs only the ranker score 6 | A weak cue needs the score 10 that a prompt with no cue needs (T010, T011) |\n158:| `ADV/tests/scorer/doctor-handoff-command.vitest.ts` | Modify | Cases for the weak cue |\n181:| REQ-004 | `update the README typo in line 3` and `fix the typo in the README` return `sk-doc` with no command, and `write a readme for the doctor scripts folder` still returns `sk-doc` with `/create:readme`. The gate covers correction wording only: an edit that names no correction word keeps its command and is listed under Out of Scope. |\n184:| REQ-007 | A weak problem cue with no passing skill hands off only at ranker score 10 or more, so the two app-problem prompts return no recommendation and the three weak-cue toolkit prompts in the probe keep their doctor command. |\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"REQ-007\\\\|REQ-004\\\\|weak cue\\\" specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md | head -10\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670572752,"end":1794670572798}}}}
