rrectness and security complete (CONDITIONAL), traceability next. - Blocked/productive carry-forward: security was productive (one P2); no blocked approach. - Required evidence: line-level comparison of each doc claim with the changed code, and the phase 020 `REQ-007` text against `DOCTOR_HELPER_WEAK_CUE_MIN_SCORE`. Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\", \"newString\": \"- Dimension: maintainability\\n- Focus area: the changed test tables as the regression fence for the three residual behaviors — the\\n  coordinated refusal, the retired-alias refusal and the generic creation word — plus the\\n  case-count and doc-sync cost of the same change.\\n- Reason: iteration 3 established which findings are active and which are advisories; iteration 4\\n  checks whether the tests can fail for the residual reasons and whether the changed test surface\\n  stays maintainable.\\n- Rotation status: correctness, security and traceability complete (CONDITIONAL, one active P1);\\n  maintainability last.\\n- Blocked/productive carry-forward: traceability was productive (three P2s, two severity\\n  corrections); no blocked approach.\\n- Required evidence: add each residual prompt to the existing table mentally and show which\\n  assertion would fail today; confirm the test file's table size and the doc count.\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670634234,"end":1794670634632}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670634662,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab4a63c001xSp6k1Mv4Ipn59","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1dab49324001nFRMpNZ8W8xyKU","type":"tool","id":"call_01_w6cr5oquy2tv37mviwb6tfa6","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \"WHAT WORKED\" -A30 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md | head -40"},"output":"92:## 8. WHAT WORKED\n93-\n94-- Reading the three guards as one ordering chain instead of three independent checks: the retired-name gap only appears because `typedCommandIn` rewrites before `commandOnlyMentioned` reads, and the coordinated-refusal gap only appears because the lead must sit directly before each occurrence (iteration 1).\n95-- Probing the handler's real attach path: `scoreAdvisorPrompt` put `sk-doc` and `system-deep-loop` first for the two refusal prompts, and `typedCommandForTop` returned the command for both, so the defect was proven at the public recommendation boundary rather than only at the helper (iteration 1).\n96-- Running the compiled-route front door for the same prompts: it returned `action: defer`, which narrowed the live path to the typed attach and kept the finding honest about its caller (iteration 1).\n97-- Running the six changed test files first: 191 passed, so the new tests are green and the gaps are uncovered inputs rather than a failing suite (iteration 1).\n98-- Comparing the direct `what does /doctor:update do?` case with the `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` case: the first lost its command row and the second kept it, which isolated the missing `the ... command` gap in the bare-ask lead instead of blaming the doctor row (iteration 2).\n99-- Reading `publicRecommendation` before judging the probe: `scoreAdvisorPrompt` reports `command: null` on a command row, but the handler copies the generated row's command at `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:358-362`, so the public offer is real (iteration 2).\n100-\n101----\n102-\n103-## 9. WHAT FAILED\n104-\n105-- Reading the mention reader as a complete refusal guard failed: its documented \"every occurrence has to carry a lead\" rule is what lets a coordinated refusal's second name through, so the reading produced finding `SA4-P1-002` instead of a clean pass (iteration 1).\n106-- Reading the small-edit gate's creation guard as a document-creation check failed: `make sure`, `add a` and `new` are ordinary correction clauses, and the gate stands down on all three, so the reading produced `SA4-P1-003` (iteration 1).\n107-- Reading the mention reader as covering every question form failed: the `Is the X command safe?` shape puts the noun between the ask word and the name, so the command row survived; it became `SA4-P2-001` rather than a clean security pass (iteration 2).\n108-\n109----\n110-\n111-<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n112-## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n113-### **`commandOnlyMentioned` can read a longer command as the shorter one.** Ruled out by `(?![a-z0-9_-])` and the changed test for `/create:sk-skill-parent`; the guard returns false for the shorter name. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n114-- What was tried: **`commandOnlyMentioned` can read a longer command as the shorter one.** Ruled out by `(?![a-z0-9_-])` and the changed test for `/create:sk-skill-parent`; the guard returns false for the shorter name.\n115-- Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n116-- Do NOT retry: **`commandOnlyMentioned` can read a longer command as the shorter one.** Ruled out by `(?![a-z0-9_-])` and the changed test for `/create:sk-skill-parent`; the guard returns false for the shorter name.\n117-\n118-### **A read-only command is withheld by the scorer on a no-edit request.** Ruled out: `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit` returns the `command-doctor-env` row unchanged and the changed test asserts it. -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n119-- What was tried: **A read-only command is withheld by the scorer on a no-edit request.** Ruled out: `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit` returns the `command-doctor-env` row unchanged and the changed test asserts it.\n120-- Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n121-- Do NOT retry: **A read-only command is withheld by the scorer on a no-edit request.** Ruled out: `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit` returns the `command-doctor-env` row unchanged and the changed test asserts it.\n122-\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"92:## 8. WHAT WORKED\n93-\n94-- Reading the three guards as one ordering chain instead of three independent checks: the retired-name gap only appears because `typedCommandIn` rewrites before `commandOnlyMentioned` reads, and the coordinated-refusal gap only appears because the lead must sit directly before each occurrence (iteration 1).\n95-- Probing the handler's real attach path: `scoreAdvisorPrompt` put `sk-doc` and `system-deep-loop` first for the two refusal prompts, and `typedCommandForTop` returned the command for both, so the defect was proven at the public recommendation boundary rather than only at the helper (iteration 1).\n96-- Running the compiled-route front door for the same prompts: it returned `action: defer`, which narrowed the live path to the typed attach and kept the finding honest about its caller (iteration 1).\n97-- Running the six changed test files first: 191 passed, so the new tests are green and the gaps are uncovered inputs rather than a failing suite (iteration 1).\n98-- Comparing the direct `what does /doctor:update do?` case with the `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` case: the first lost its command row and the second kept it, which isolated the missing `the ... command` gap in the bare-ask lead instead of blaming the doctor row (iteration 2).\n99-- Reading `publicRecommendation` before judging the probe: `scoreAdvisorPrompt` reports `command: null` on a command row, but the handler copies the generated row's command at `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts:358-362`, so the public offer is real (iteration 2).\n100-\n101----\n102-\n103-## 9. WHAT FAILED\n104-\n105-- Reading the mention reader as a complete refusal guard failed: its documented \"every occurrence has to carry a lead\" rule is what lets a coordinated refusal's second name through, so the reading produced finding `SA4-P1-002` instead of a clean pass (iteration 1).\n106-- Reading the small-edit gate's creation guard as a document-creation check failed: `make sure`, `add a` and `new` are ordinary correction clauses, and the gate stands down on all three, so the reading produced `SA4-P1-003` (iteration 1).\n107-- Reading the mention reader as covering every question form failed: the `Is the X command safe?` shape puts the noun between the ask word and the name, so the command row survived; it became `SA4-P2-001` rather than a clean security pass (iteration 2).\n108-\n109----\n110-\n111-<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n112-## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n113-### **`commandOnlyMentioned` can read a longer command as the shorter one.** Ruled out by `(?![a-z0-9_-])` and the changed test for `/create:sk-skill-parent`; the guard returns false for the shorter name. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n114-- What was tried: **`commandOnlyMentioned` can read a longer command as the shorter one.** Ruled out by `(?![a-z0-9_-])` and the changed test for `/create:sk-skill-parent`; the guard returns false for the shorter name.\n115-- Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n116-- Do NOT retry: **`commandOnlyMentioned` can read a longer command as the shorter one.** Ruled out by `(?![a-z0-9_-])` and the changed test for `/create:sk-skill-parent`; the guard returns false for the shorter name.\n117-\n118-### **A read-only command is withheld by the scorer on a no-edit request.** Ruled out: `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit` returns the `command-doctor-env` row unchanged and the changed test asserts it. -- BLOCKED (iteration 2, 1 attempts)\n119-- What was tried: **A read-only command is withheld by the scorer on a no-edit request.** Ruled out: `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit` returns the `command-doctor-env` row unchanged and the changed test asserts it.\n120-- Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n121-- Do NOT retry: **A read-only command is withheld by the scorer on a no-edit request.** Ruled out: `withholdWritingCommandsOnNoEdit` returns the `command-doctor-env` row unchanged and the changed test asserts it.\n122-\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && grep -n \\\"WHAT WORKED\\\" -A30 specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/deep-review-strategy.md | head -40\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670634556,"end":1794670634662}}}}
