-handoff.ts:54\"],\n      \"counterevidenceSought\": \"The code matches the accepted T025 decision and the tune row at 9.51; the stale side is the requirement text, not the constant.\",\n      \"alternativeExplanation\": \"The requirement may intentionally describe the no-cue bar; it says 'weak problem cue', and the code has a separate weak constant.\",\n      \"finalSeverity\": \"P2\",\n      \"confidence\": \"high\",\n      \"downgradeTrigger\": \"Withdraw if REQ-007 is amended to 9 before the packet closes.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"severityTransitions\": [\n    {\"id\": \"SA4-P1-001\", \"from\": \"P1\", \"to\": \"P2\", \"reason\": \"Phase 020 T017 records the retired-alias refusal as an accepted limit.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"SA4-P1-003\", \"from\": \"P1\", \"to\": \"P2\", \"reason\": \"AC-004 scopes the small-edit gate to the two exact prompts and the three document commands; the variants are a breadth tradeoff.\"}\n  ],\n  \"traceabilityChecks\": {\n    \"spec_code\": {\"level\": \"core\", \"status\": \"partial\", \"notes\": \"REQ-003/004 exact prompts pass; REQ-007 says 10 while AC-007 and the code use 9; coordinated refusal is uncovered (SA4-P1-002).\"},\n    \"checklist_evidence\": {\"level\": \"core\", \"status\": \"partial\", \"notes\": \"AC-002/003/004/006/007 are Met with evidence; AC-007 records 9 while REQ-007 says 10; CHK-FIX-004's two-command case is a request.\"},\n    \"feature_catalog_code\": {\"level\": \"overlay\", \"status\": \"partial\", \"notes\": \"advisor-recommend.md:39 stale; command-meaning-matching.md:65 stale count; doctor routing text still true.\"},\n    \"skill_agent\": {\"level\": \"overlay\", \"status\": \"notApplicable\", \"notes\": \"No agent definition changed in this area.\"},\n    \"agent_cross_runtime\": {\"level\": \"overlay\", \"status\": \"partial\", \"notes\": \"No runtime branch; live per-runtime proof belongs to the phase 007 arm.\"},\n    \"playbook_capability\": {\"level\": \"overlay\", \"status\": \"notApplicable\", \"notes\