{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794670921579,"sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","part":{"partID":"prt_1dab904ad001H3tACRj1tTvMfe","sessionID":"ses_e255ff46fffexTncZnylD3HfiJ","messageID":"msg_1dab87aed0015Yvf8xJLux7caU","type":"tool","id":"call_00_y2pauab7ryju9z4zimiog8ul","tool":"write","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Four (scorer-attach lineage)\n\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\n- Pass: the fourth review pass. It runs after the pass-three fixes (`0cdc9fa3ef`) and the phase 020/021/024 code in `198e6d1a9d..400c90e158`.\n- Lineage: `scorer-attach-4`, area `scorer-attach`, run `fanout-scorer-attach-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, executor `cli-opencode` `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max.\n- Reviewed scope: the eleven paths in `review/review-scope-4.txt` whose area is `scorer-attach` — `lib/command-attach.ts`, `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `lib/scorer/projection.ts`, `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, and six changed test files — plus the shared feature docs that describe them.\n- Inputs to this synthesis: the four iteration narratives, the four delta files, the lineage registry (8 active findings), the strategy and the dashboard.\n- Cross-area boundary: renderer/hooks/plugin/session-reader files belong to `render-hooks-plugin-4`; the transcript scorer and capture harness belong to `accuracy-runner-4`; doctor command docs belong to `doctor-docs-4`. This lineage names those surfaces but raises no code finding outside its area.\n- Iteration cap: 4 of 4. Convergence was not declared because one active P1 remains; the loop stopped at the cap.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\n\n- **Verdict: CONDITIONAL.** No P0, one P1 and seven P2 findings are active.\n- **hasAdvisories: false.** The advisory flag is reserved for a PASS that carries P2s; this verdict is conditional on the P1.\n- **Active counts:** P0 0, P1 1, P2 7.\n- **The active P1:** a coordinated refusal such as `do not run /deep:review or /deep:research` still delivers `/deep:research` through the typed-command path. The command is `ask`, so it asks before it writes; the refusal is still overridden, which is the defect.\n- **Accepted limits kept as P2:** the retired-alias refusal (`do not run /create:skill`) and the generic creation word in a correction (`fix the typo in the readme and make sure ...`). Phase 020 T017 records the first as an accepted limit; AC-004 scopes the small-edit gate to the two exact README prompts and the three document commands.\n- **Documentation and requirement drift:** `advisor-recommend.md:39` says a hub suppresses a command its own row already offers, but the changed head-row rule keeps both; `command-meaning-matching.md:65` reports 17 cases where the file now has 28; `REQ-007` says a weak cue needs ranker score 10 while the accepted T025 decision, `AC-007` and the code use 9.\n- **One test-fence gap:** the changed tables do not pin the coordinated refusal, the retired-alias refusal, the generic creation word or the `Is the X command` question. The suite stays green while all four are live.\n- **Mutating-command safety:** no finding lets a command write without its asking step. The worst outcome is an unfit offer of an `ask` or `start` command, which then asks before it writes. That is why the refusal finding is P1, not P0.\n- **Cross-runtime:** the changed attach, scorer and handler modules carry no runtime branch. The six runtimes reach the same handler; the renderer's third-row behavior is a sibling lineage's surface. No live per-runtime session was available in this lineage.\n- **Holdout:** no changed source file reads `command-prompts.jsonl` or `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. The two changed tests that read the corpus select a tune id and assert `split === 'tune'` before using the prompt; no prompt text is printed.\n- **Release readiness:** `in-progress`. The cap was reached with one active P1 and no convergence event.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Planning Trigger\n\nThe verdict requires remediation. One P1 is a must-fix refusal gap; seven P2s cover accepted limits, documentation and test coverage. The Planning Packet groups them into four file-disjoint workstreams.\n\n```json Planning Packet\n{\n  \"triggered\": true,\n  \"triggerReason\": \"One active P1 is a refusal that still attaches a command; seven P2s cover accepted limits, doc/spec drift and test coverage.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"CONDITIONAL\",\n  \"hasAdvisories\": false,\n  \"counts\": { \"p0\": 0, \"p1\": 1, \"p2\": 7, \"active\": 8, \"iterations\": 4 },\n  \"activeFindings\": [\n    { \"id\": \"SA4-P1-002\", \"severity\": \"P1\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414\", \"origin\": \"introduced\", \"workGroup\": \"WG1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"SA4-P1-001\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED-ADJUSTED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240\", \"origin\": \"pre-existing\", \"workGroup\": \"WG1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"SA4-P1-003\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED-ADJUSTED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:487\", \"origin\": \"introduced\", \"workGroup\": \"WG1\" },\n    { \"id\": \"SA4-P2-001\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209\", \"origin\": \"introduced\", \"workGroup\": \"WG2\" },\n    { \"id\": \"SA4-P2-002\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:39\", \"origin\": \"introduced\", \"workGroup\": \"WG3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"SA4-P2-003\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:65\", \"origin\": \"introduced\", \"workGroup\": \"WG3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"SA4-P2-004\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts:54\", \"origin\": \"introduced\", \"workGroup\": \"WG3\" },\n    { \"id\": \"SA4-P2-005\", \"severity\": \"P2\", \"verdict\": \"CONFIRMED\", \"location\": \".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39\", \"origin\": \"introduced\", \"workGroup\": \"WG4\" }\n  ],\n  \"findingClasses\": [\"guard_gap\", \"mention_reader_gap\", \"doc_code_drift\", \"spec_code_drift\", \"test_coverage_gap\"],\n  \"affectedSurfacesSeed\": [\n    \"typed-command attach\",\n    \"mention reader\",\n    \"doctor command row\",\n    \"feature-catalog docs\",\n    \"phase 020 requirement text\",\n    \"command-attach test tables\"\n  ],\n  \"fixCompletenessRequired\": true\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\n\n| ID | Sev | Dimension | Location | Evidence | Impact | Disposition |\n|----|-----|-----------|----------|----------|--------|-------------|\n| SA4-P1-002 | P1 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414` | `commandOnlyMentioned` requires a separate lead before every occurrence; `do not run A or B` leaves B unled. `typedCommandForTop` returns `/deep:research`; the top row is `system-deep-loop`. | A refusal still attaches an ask-policy command. | Fix in WG1. |\n| SA4-P1-001 | P2 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240` | `typedCommandIn` rewrites `/create:skill` before the mention guard reads the live name. Probe returns `/create:sk-skill` with `start`. | Documented accepted limit (T017); the code still has the gap. | Keep advisory; revisit only if the alias semantics change. |\n| SA4-P1-003 | P2 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:487` | `CREATION_REQUEST` includes `make`, `new`, `add an`, `need an`; the gate stands down and returns `/create:readme` for correction prompts. | Accepted breadth tradeoff per AC-004/T024/T026. | Keep advisory; the test gap is WG4. |\n| SA4-P2-001 | P2 | security | `runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209` | `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` and the statement form pass `command-doctor-update`; the bare-ask lead does not allow the noun `command`. | An ask-policy doctor command is offered on a question. | Fix in WG2. |\n| SA4-P2-002 | P2 | traceability | `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:39` | The doc says a hub suppresses a command its own row offers; the changed head-row rule keeps both and the changed test asserts it. | Docs disagree with code. | Fix in WG3. |\n| SA4-P2-003 | P2 | traceability | `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:65` | The doc says 17 cases; the file has 28 `it(` declarations. | Stale test inventory. | Fix in WG3. |\n| SA4-P2-004 | P2 | traceability | `runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts:54` | `REQ-007` says 10; `AC-007` and T025 accept 9; the code uses 9. | A scoring case between 9 and 10 contradicts the requirement text. | Fix the requirement text in WG3. |\n| SA4-P2-005 | P2 | maintainability | `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39` | None of the four residual prompts has a table row; each would fail at the assertion line today. | The suite stays green while the residuals are live. | Fix in WG4. |\n\n### Finding class / scope proof / affected surfaces\n\n- `SA4-P1-002` -- `guard_gap`; both files in scope, the compiled route for the exact prompt returns `defer`, and the typed path is the live caller. Affected: typed-command attach, multi-command refusals, deep-loop ask policies.\n- `SA4-P1-001` -- `guard_gap`; mapping and guard are in `command-attach.ts`, the handler copies the returned command. Affected: retired-command map, `/create:sk-skill` start policy.\n- `SA4-P1-003` -- `guard_gap`; the gate and its regex are in `command-attach.ts`, and the compiled route selects `sk-create-readme` for each case. Affected: small-edit gate, `/create:readme` start policy.\n- `SA4-P2-001` -- `mention_reader_gap`; the reader and the withholding gate are in scope, and `publicRecommendation` copies the command. Affected: doctor command rows, question/statement phrasings.\n- `SA4-P2-002`..`SA4-P2-004` -- `doc_code_drift`/`spec_code_drift`; the docs and the phase requirement describe the changed files. Affected: operator docs, acceptance evidence, handoff threshold text.\n- `SA4-P2-005` -- `test_coverage_gap`; the changed test file and the functions it fences are in scope. Affected: `REFUSE8`, the small-edit table, `QUESTION2`, `CHK-FIX-004`.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\n\n1. **WG1 -- Attach refusal guard (safety lane).** Files: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. Fix `SA4-P1-002` by letting a refusal lead cover a coordinated command list (`do not run A or B`), without turning `use A, not B` into a refusal of the requested A. Keep `SA4-P1-001` and `SA4-P1-003` as documented advisories unless the packet reopens the alias or the creation guard.\n2. **WG2 -- Doctor question mention.** Files: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`. Extend the bare-ask lead or the ask list to allow `the` and `command` between the ask word and the name; add the two probes to `QUESTION2` and the `withholdMentionedCommands` table.\n3. **WG3 -- Doc and requirement sync.** Files: `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md`, `020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md`/`acceptance-criteria.md`. Correct the head-row sentence, update the test inventory, and make `REQ-007` say 9 (or record the discrepancy as the accepted T025 decision).\n4. **WG4 -- Test fence.** Files: `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`. Add the four rows; rename `REFUSE8` if the count changes. The rows make the accepted limits and the remaining gaps visible instead of green-by-omission.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Spec Seed\n\n- State the refusal contract for a coordinated command list: one lead may cover `A or B`, while a later clause that asks for a command still wins.\n- State the alias-refusal behavior: `/create:skill` refusal maps to the live command and is an accepted limit until the alias is retired.\n- Narrow the creation-request guard to a document-object phrase, or record `make sure`/`add a`/`new` as accepted breadth tradeoffs.\n- State the weak-cue bar as one number in `REQ-007`, `AC-007` and the mechanism table.\n- Add a doc-sync task to every change that alters a head-row rule or a test inventory.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Plan Seed\n\n- T1: Add the coordinated-refusal regression test first; watch it fail; then adjust `commandOnlyMentioned` and re-run the full `command-attach-guards` suite.\n- T2: Add the `Is the X command` row to `QUESTION2`; watch it fail; adjust the bare-ask lead; re-run `command-attach-guards` and `command-meaning-anchor`.\n- T3: Update the two feature docs and the phase 020 requirement; run `derive-command-bridges.cjs --check` to confirm no generated drift.\n- T4: Add the four test rows from `SA4-P2-005`; keep the accepted limits marked with a comment that names the packet decision, not a spec path.\n- T5: Re-run the advisor suite, the five floors and the slice tests; confirm the change does not move a tune or holdout row.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Traceability Status\n\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | REQ-003/004 exact prompts pass; REQ-007 says 10 against AC-007's 9; coordinated refusal is an uncovered class. |\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | AC-002/003/004/006/007 are Met with evidence; CHK-FIX-004's \"two commands\" case is a request, not a coordinated refusal. |\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition changed in this area. |\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | No runtime branch in the changed modules; live proof belongs to the phase 007 arm. |\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | Two shared docs disagree with the changed code; doctor routing text remains true. |\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook surface changed. |\n\n`AC_COVERAGE`: exempt. The target root has no `checklist.md`, no `acceptance-criteria.md` and no `implementation-summary.md`; the phase 020 child docs carry their own acceptance evidence.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Deferred Items\n\n- **Transcript scorer arithmetic** (Codex exec bodies, rg/grep, heredocs, cd, partner-side commands, paired arms, Wilson ranges): owned by `accuracy-runner-4`; this lineage records the boundary and does not raise a finding.\n- **Live per-runtime proof** (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh): the changed modules are runtime-neutral; the phase 007 arm owns live sessions.\n- **Renderer third-row behavior**: whether the hook brief displays the doctor command row is `render-hooks-plugin-4`'s surface; the scorer row exists regardless.\n- **Stale local dist**: the system reminder reports a stale compiled dist. The review reads source through vitest; a live runtime may load dist until `npm run build` runs in the advisor package.\n- **Accepted limits**: the retired-alias refusal and the generic creation word remain advisories. Reopen only if the packet chooses a narrower alias or creation contract.\n\n---\n\n## Dimension Expansion Map\n\n- Completed pivots: 0.\n- Failed pivots: 0.\n- Audited overrides: 0.\n- Swept: none; the four dimensions each ran once.\n- Pivot lineage: none.\n- Remaining frontier: the transcript scorer and the live runtimes are sibling areas, not a frontier of this lineage.\n\n---\n\n## Search Ledger\n\n- `requiredBugClasses`: guard_gap, boundary_parsing, state_transition, doc_code_drift, mention_reader_gap, no_edit_policy, holdout_leak, runtime_branch, spec_code_drift, checklist_evidence, test_coverage_gap, vacuous_assertion.\n- `covered`: guard_gap, mention_reader_gap, no_edit_policy, doc_code_drift, spec_code_drift, test_coverage_gap.\n- `ruledOut`: boundary_parsing, holdout_leak, runtime_branch, vacuous_assertion, checklist_evidence_gap.\n- `deferred`: state_transition (no-edit/read-only path split; no compiled-hub read-only route proved), the transcript-scorer arithmetic (sibling area).\n- `searchDebt`: 3 (the deferred no-edit path split, the two sibling-area items). `hasSearchDebt: true`.\n- `graphCoverageMode`: `graphless_fallback`; the coverage graph seed was skipped because `upsert.cjs` writes outside the lineage boundary.\n- `ruledOutCandidates`: the compiled route attaching the refused command; the retired-name rewrite itself; a longer command reading as its prefix; the generated projection being hand-edited; the weak-cue code being wrong; the changed assertions being vacuous.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Audit Appendix\n\n### Convergence summary\n\n| Iteration | Dimension | Ratio | P0/P1/P2 | Verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | correctness | 1.00 | 0/3/0 | CONDITIONAL |\n| 2 | security | 1.00 | 0/0/1 | CONDITIONAL |\n| 3 | traceability | 1.00 | 0/0/3 | CONDITIONAL |\n| 4 | maintainability | 1.00 | 0/0/1 | CONDITIONAL |\n\nNo convergence event was recorded. The cap of 4 was reached with one active P1. `convergenceScore` is 0.0 in the reducer; `hasSearchDebt` is true.\n\n### Coverage summary\n\n- Dimensions covered: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability (4 of 4).\n- Changed test files executed: 6; 191 tests passed, exit 0.\n- Probe files: `lineage/probes/probe-scorer.vitest.ts` and `lineage/probes/vitest.config.ts` (read-only source probes; no writes outside the lineage).\n- Compiled-route front door: run for the refusal, correction and deep-loop prompts; the refusal prompts returned `defer`, the correction prompts returned a single `sk-create-readme` route.\n- Deriver: `derive-command-bridges.cjs --check` returned `status: fresh`, `changed: []`.\n\n### Ruled-out claims\n\n- The compiled route attaches the refused command (defer for both refusal prompts).\n- The retired-name rewrite is wrong (the mapping is the pinned behavior; the guard ordering is the gap).\n- A longer command reads as its shorter prefix (boundary test passes).\n- The small-edit gate withholds a genuine creation request (the two controls pass).\n- The generated projection was hand-edited (deriver fresh).\n- The weak-cue code should be 10 (T025/AC-007 accept 9; the spec text is stale).\n- A changed assertion is vacuous (each changed case passes its table row into the function).\n- A changed path reads or prints a holdout row (tune-id selection plus split assertion).\n\n### Sources reviewed\n\n- `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`.\n- Six changed test files: `command-attach-guards`, `command-meaning-anchor`, `doctor-helper-handoff`, `advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option`, `doctor-handoff-command`, `typed-command-owner`.\n- Shared docs: `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md`, `scripts/command-bridges/README.md`.\n- Packet docs: `020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `tasks.md`; `024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md`; `review/review-scope-4.txt`; `review/review-brief-4.txt`.\n- Review doctrine: `sk-code-review/references/review-core.md` §2.\n\n### Write discipline\n\n- Every file written by this lineage is under `review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/`: four iteration narratives, four deltas, the strategy, the config, the registry, the dashboard, the report, the probe files and the temporary record builders.\n- No review target, config, generated table, command, skill, agent, renderer or sibling lineage file was modified.\n- The state log was written only by `append-mode-event.cjs`; the reducer refreshed the registry, dashboard and strategy after each iteration.\n- No nested CLI, sub-agent or Task dispatch was used. No `generate-context.js`, `validate.sh`, git write or out-of-lineage command was run.\n","path":"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md"},"output":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md","title":"write","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Created file successfully: specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"content\": \"# Review Report: Command Surfacing Build, Pass Four (scorer-attach lineage)\\n\\n- Review target: `specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build` (spec-folder)\\n- Pass: the fourth review pass. It runs after the pass-three fixes (`0cdc9fa3ef`) and the phase 020/021/024 code in `198e6d1a9d..400c90e158`.\\n- Lineage: `scorer-attach-4`, area `scorer-attach`, run `fanout-scorer-attach-4-1794669272137-9v23rz`, executor `cli-opencode` `opencode-go/deepseek-v4.1-flash` at reasoning effort max.\\n- Reviewed scope: the eleven paths in `review/review-scope-4.txt` whose area is `scorer-attach` — `lib/command-attach.ts`, `lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `lib/scorer/projection.ts`, `handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`, and six changed test files — plus the shared feature docs that describe them.\\n- Inputs to this synthesis: the four iteration narratives, the four delta files, the lineage registry (8 active findings), the strategy and the dashboard.\\n- Cross-area boundary: renderer/hooks/plugin/session-reader files belong to `render-hooks-plugin-4`; the transcript scorer and capture harness belong to `accuracy-runner-4`; doctor command docs belong to `doctor-docs-4`. This lineage names those surfaces but raises no code finding outside its area.\\n- Iteration cap: 4 of 4. Convergence was not declared because one active P1 remains; the loop stopped at the cap.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Executive Summary\\n\\n- **Verdict: CONDITIONAL.** No P0, one P1 and seven P2 findings are active.\\n- **hasAdvisories: false.** The advisory flag is reserved for a PASS that carries P2s; this verdict is conditional on the P1.\\n- **Active counts:** P0 0, P1 1, P2 7.\\n- **The active P1:** a coordinated refusal such as `do not run /deep:review or /deep:research` still delivers `/deep:research` through the typed-command path. The command is `ask`, so it asks before it writes; the refusal is still overridden, which is the defect.\\n- **Accepted limits kept as P2:** the retired-alias refusal (`do not run /create:skill`) and the generic creation word in a correction (`fix the typo in the readme and make sure ...`). Phase 020 T017 records the first as an accepted limit; AC-004 scopes the small-edit gate to the two exact README prompts and the three document commands.\\n- **Documentation and requirement drift:** `advisor-recommend.md:39` says a hub suppresses a command its own row already offers, but the changed head-row rule keeps both; `command-meaning-matching.md:65` reports 17 cases where the file now has 28; `REQ-007` says a weak cue needs ranker score 10 while the accepted T025 decision, `AC-007` and the code use 9.\\n- **One test-fence gap:** the changed tables do not pin the coordinated refusal, the retired-alias refusal, the generic creation word or the `Is the X command` question. The suite stays green while all four are live.\\n- **Mutating-command safety:** no finding lets a command write without its asking step. The worst outcome is an unfit offer of an `ask` or `start` command, which then asks before it writes. That is why the refusal finding is P1, not P0.\\n- **Cross-runtime:** the changed attach, scorer and handler modules carry no runtime branch. The six runtimes reach the same handler; the renderer's third-row behavior is a sibling lineage's surface. No live per-runtime session was available in this lineage.\\n- **Holdout:** no changed source file reads `command-prompts.jsonl` or `holdout-prompts.jsonl`. The two changed tests that read the corpus select a tune id and assert `split === 'tune'` before using the prompt; no prompt text is printed.\\n- **Release readiness:** `in-progress`. The cap was reached with one active P1 and no convergence event.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 2. Planning Trigger\\n\\nThe verdict requires remediation. One P1 is a must-fix refusal gap; seven P2s cover accepted limits, documentation and test coverage. The Planning Packet groups them into four file-disjoint workstreams.\\n\\n```json Planning Packet\\n{\\n  \\\"triggered\\\": true,\\n  \\\"triggerReason\\\": \\\"One active P1 is a refusal that still attaches a command; seven P2s cover accepted limits, doc/spec drift and test coverage.\\\",\\n  \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONDITIONAL\\\",\\n  \\\"hasAdvisories\\\": false,\\n  \\\"counts\\\": { \\\"p0\\\": 0, \\\"p1\\\": 1, \\\"p2\\\": 7, \\\"active\\\": 8, \\\"iterations\\\": 4 },\\n  \\\"activeFindings\\\": [\\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"SA4-P1-002\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P1\\\", \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONFIRMED\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"introduced\\\", \\\"workGroup\\\": \\\"WG1\\\" },\\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"SA4-P1-001\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONFIRMED-ADJUSTED\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"pre-existing\\\", \\\"workGroup\\\": \\\"WG1\\\" },\\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"SA4-P1-003\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONFIRMED-ADJUSTED\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:487\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"introduced\\\", \\\"workGroup\\\": \\\"WG1\\\" },\\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"SA4-P2-001\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONFIRMED\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"introduced\\\", \\\"workGroup\\\": \\\"WG2\\\" },\\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"SA4-P2-002\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONFIRMED\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:39\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"introduced\\\", \\\"workGroup\\\": \\\"WG3\\\" },\\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"SA4-P2-003\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONFIRMED\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:65\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"introduced\\\", \\\"workGroup\\\": \\\"WG3\\\" },\\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"SA4-P2-004\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONFIRMED\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts:54\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"introduced\\\", \\\"workGroup\\\": \\\"WG3\\\" },\\n    { \\\"id\\\": \\\"SA4-P2-005\\\", \\\"severity\\\": \\\"P2\\\", \\\"verdict\\\": \\\"CONFIRMED\\\", \\\"location\\\": \\\".skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39\\\", \\\"origin\\\": \\\"introduced\\\", \\\"workGroup\\\": \\\"WG4\\\" }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"findingClasses\\\": [\\\"guard_gap\\\", \\\"mention_reader_gap\\\", \\\"doc_code_drift\\\", \\\"spec_code_drift\\\", \\\"test_coverage_gap\\\"],\\n  \\\"affectedSurfacesSeed\\\": [\\n    \\\"typed-command attach\\\",\\n    \\\"mention reader\\\",\\n    \\\"doctor command row\\\",\\n    \\\"feature-catalog docs\\\",\\n    \\\"phase 020 requirement text\\\",\\n    \\\"command-attach test tables\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"fixCompletenessRequired\\\": true\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 3. Active Finding Registry\\n\\n| ID | Sev | Dimension | Location | Evidence | Impact | Disposition |\\n|----|-----|-----------|----------|----------|--------|-------------|\\n| SA4-P1-002 | P1 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:414` | `commandOnlyMentioned` requires a separate lead before every occurrence; `do not run A or B` leaves B unled. `typedCommandForTop` returns `/deep:research`; the top row is `system-deep-loop`. | A refusal still attaches an ask-policy command. | Fix in WG1. |\\n| SA4-P1-001 | P2 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:240` | `typedCommandIn` rewrites `/create:skill` before the mention guard reads the live name. Probe returns `/create:sk-skill` with `start`. | Documented accepted limit (T017); the code still has the gap. | Keep advisory; revisit only if the alias semantics change. |\\n| SA4-P1-003 | P2 | correctness | `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts:487` | `CREATION_REQUEST` includes `make`, `new`, `add an`, `need an`; the gate stands down and returns `/create:readme` for correction prompts. | Accepted breadth tradeoff per AC-004/T024/T026. | Keep advisory; the test gap is WG4. |\\n| SA4-P2-001 | P2 | security | `runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts:1209` | `Is the /doctor:update command safe?` and the statement form pass `command-doctor-update`; the bare-ask lead does not allow the noun `command`. | An ask-policy doctor command is offered on a question. | Fix in WG2. |\\n| SA4-P2-002 | P2 | traceability | `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md:39` | The doc says a hub suppresses a command its own row offers; the changed head-row rule keeps both and the changed test asserts it. | Docs disagree with code. | Fix in WG3. |\\n| SA4-P2-003 | P2 | traceability | `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md:65` | The doc says 17 cases; the file has 28 `it(` declarations. | Stale test inventory. | Fix in WG3. |\\n| SA4-P2-004 | P2 | traceability | `runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts:54` | `REQ-007` says 10; `AC-007` and T025 accept 9; the code uses 9. | A scoring case between 9 and 10 contradicts the requirement text. | Fix the requirement text in WG3. |\\n| SA4-P2-005 | P2 | maintainability | `tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts:39` | None of the four residual prompts has a table row; each would fail at the assertion line today. | The suite stays green while the residuals are live. | Fix in WG4. |\\n\\n### Finding class / scope proof / affected surfaces\\n\\n- `SA4-P1-002` -- `guard_gap`; both files in scope, the compiled route for the exact prompt returns `defer`, and the typed path is the live caller. Affected: typed-command attach, multi-command refusals, deep-loop ask policies.\\n- `SA4-P1-001` -- `guard_gap`; mapping and guard are in `command-attach.ts`, the handler copies the returned command. Affected: retired-command map, `/create:sk-skill` start policy.\\n- `SA4-P1-003` -- `guard_gap`; the gate and its regex are in `command-attach.ts`, and the compiled route selects `sk-create-readme` for each case. Affected: small-edit gate, `/create:readme` start policy.\\n- `SA4-P2-001` -- `mention_reader_gap`; the reader and the withholding gate are in scope, and `publicRecommendation` copies the command. Affected: doctor command rows, question/statement phrasings.\\n- `SA4-P2-002`..`SA4-P2-004` -- `doc_code_drift`/`spec_code_drift`; the docs and the phase requirement describe the changed files. Affected: operator docs, acceptance evidence, handoff threshold text.\\n- `SA4-P2-005` -- `test_coverage_gap`; the changed test file and the functions it fences are in scope. Affected: `REFUSE8`, the small-edit table, `QUESTION2`, `CHK-FIX-004`.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 4. Remediation Workstreams\\n\\n1. **WG1 -- Attach refusal guard (safety lane).** Files: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`. Fix `SA4-P1-002` by letting a refusal lead cover a coordinated command list (`do not run A or B`), without turning `use A, not B` into a refusal of the requested A. Keep `SA4-P1-001` and `SA4-P1-003` as documented advisories unless the packet reopens the alias or the creation guard.\\n2. **WG2 -- Doctor question mention.** Files: `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`. Extend the bare-ask lead or the ask list to allow `the` and `command` between the ask word and the name; add the two probes to `QUESTION2` and the `withholdMentionedCommands` table.\\n3. **WG3 -- Doc and requirement sync.** Files: `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md`, `020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md`/`acceptance-criteria.md`. Correct the head-row sentence, update the test inventory, and make `REQ-007` say 9 (or record the discrepancy as the accepted T025 decision).\\n4. **WG4 -- Test fence.** Files: `runtime/tests/command-attach-guards.vitest.ts`, `runtime/tests/command-meaning-anchor.vitest.ts`. Add the four rows; rename `REFUSE8` if the count changes. The rows make the accepted limits and the remaining gaps visible instead of green-by-omission.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 5. Spec Seed\\n\\n- State the refusal contract for a coordinated command list: one lead may cover `A or B`, while a later clause that asks for a command still wins.\\n- State the alias-refusal behavior: `/create:skill` refusal maps to the live command and is an accepted limit until the alias is retired.\\n- Narrow the creation-request guard to a document-object phrase, or record `make sure`/`add a`/`new` as accepted breadth tradeoffs.\\n- State the weak-cue bar as one number in `REQ-007`, `AC-007` and the mechanism table.\\n- Add a doc-sync task to every change that alters a head-row rule or a test inventory.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 6. Plan Seed\\n\\n- T1: Add the coordinated-refusal regression test first; watch it fail; then adjust `commandOnlyMentioned` and re-run the full `command-attach-guards` suite.\\n- T2: Add the `Is the X command` row to `QUESTION2`; watch it fail; adjust the bare-ask lead; re-run `command-attach-guards` and `command-meaning-anchor`.\\n- T3: Update the two feature docs and the phase 020 requirement; run `derive-command-bridges.cjs --check` to confirm no generated drift.\\n- T4: Add the four test rows from `SA4-P2-005`; keep the accepted limits marked with a comment that names the packet decision, not a spec path.\\n- T5: Re-run the advisor suite, the five floors and the slice tests; confirm the change does not move a tune or holdout row.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 7. Traceability Status\\n\\n| Protocol | Level | Status | Evidence |\\n|----------|-------|--------|----------|\\n| `spec_code` | core | partial | REQ-003/004 exact prompts pass; REQ-007 says 10 against AC-007's 9; coordinated refusal is an uncovered class. |\\n| `checklist_evidence` | core | partial | AC-002/003/004/006/007 are Met with evidence; CHK-FIX-004's \\\"two commands\\\" case is a request, not a coordinated refusal. |\\n| `skill_agent` | overlay | notApplicable | No agent definition changed in this area. |\\n| `agent_cross_runtime` | overlay | partial | No runtime branch in the changed modules; live proof belongs to the phase 007 arm. |\\n| `feature_catalog_code` | overlay | partial | Two shared docs disagree with the changed code; doctor routing text remains true. |\\n| `playbook_capability` | overlay | notApplicable | No playbook surface changed. |\\n\\n`AC_COVERAGE`: exempt. The target root has no `checklist.md`, no `acceptance-criteria.md` and no `implementation-summary.md`; the phase 020 child docs carry their own acceptance evidence.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 8. Deferred Items\\n\\n- **Transcript scorer arithmetic** (Codex exec bodies, rg/grep, heredocs, cd, partner-side commands, paired arms, Wilson ranges): owned by `accuracy-runner-4`; this lineage records the boundary and does not raise a finding.\\n- **Live per-runtime proof** (claude, codex, opencode, pi, devin, dsh): the changed modules are runtime-neutral; the phase 007 arm owns live sessions.\\n- **Renderer third-row behavior**: whether the hook brief displays the doctor command row is `render-hooks-plugin-4`'s surface; the scorer row exists regardless.\\n- **Stale local dist**: the system reminder reports a stale compiled dist. The review reads source through vitest; a live runtime may load dist until `npm run build` runs in the advisor package.\\n- **Accepted limits**: the retired-alias refusal and the generic creation word remain advisories. Reopen only if the packet chooses a narrower alias or creation contract.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Dimension Expansion Map\\n\\n- Completed pivots: 0.\\n- Failed pivots: 0.\\n- Audited overrides: 0.\\n- Swept: none; the four dimensions each ran once.\\n- Pivot lineage: none.\\n- Remaining frontier: the transcript scorer and the live runtimes are sibling areas, not a frontier of this lineage.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Search Ledger\\n\\n- `requiredBugClasses`: guard_gap, boundary_parsing, state_transition, doc_code_drift, mention_reader_gap, no_edit_policy, holdout_leak, runtime_branch, spec_code_drift, checklist_evidence, test_coverage_gap, vacuous_assertion.\\n- `covered`: guard_gap, mention_reader_gap, no_edit_policy, doc_code_drift, spec_code_drift, test_coverage_gap.\\n- `ruledOut`: boundary_parsing, holdout_leak, runtime_branch, vacuous_assertion, checklist_evidence_gap.\\n- `deferred`: state_transition (no-edit/read-only path split; no compiled-hub read-only route proved), the transcript-scorer arithmetic (sibling area).\\n- `searchDebt`: 3 (the deferred no-edit path split, the two sibling-area items). `hasSearchDebt: true`.\\n- `graphCoverageMode`: `graphless_fallback`; the coverage graph seed was skipped because `upsert.cjs` writes outside the lineage boundary.\\n- `ruledOutCandidates`: the compiled route attaching the refused command; the retired-name rewrite itself; a longer command reading as its prefix; the generated projection being hand-edited; the weak-cue code being wrong; the changed assertions being vacuous.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 9. Audit Appendix\\n\\n### Convergence summary\\n\\n| Iteration | Dimension | Ratio | P0/P1/P2 | Verdict |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| 1 | correctness | 1.00 | 0/3/0 | CONDITIONAL |\\n| 2 | security | 1.00 | 0/0/1 | CONDITIONAL |\\n| 3 | traceability | 1.00 | 0/0/3 | CONDITIONAL |\\n| 4 | maintainability | 1.00 | 0/0/1 | CONDITIONAL |\\n\\nNo convergence event was recorded. The cap of 4 was reached with one active P1. `convergenceScore` is 0.0 in the reducer; `hasSearchDebt` is true.\\n\\n### Coverage summary\\n\\n- Dimensions covered: correctness, security, traceability, maintainability (4 of 4).\\n- Changed test files executed: 6; 191 tests passed, exit 0.\\n- Probe files: `lineage/probes/probe-scorer.vitest.ts` and `lineage/probes/vitest.config.ts` (read-only source probes; no writes outside the lineage).\\n- Compiled-route front door: run for the refusal, correction and deep-loop prompts; the refusal prompts returned `defer`, the correction prompts returned a single `sk-create-readme` route.\\n- Deriver: `derive-command-bridges.cjs --check` returned `status: fresh`, `changed: []`.\\n\\n### Ruled-out claims\\n\\n- The compiled route attaches the refused command (defer for both refusal prompts).\\n- The retired-name rewrite is wrong (the mapping is the pinned behavior; the guard ordering is the gap).\\n- A longer command reads as its shorter prefix (boundary test passes).\\n- The small-edit gate withholds a genuine creation request (the two controls pass).\\n- The generated projection was hand-edited (deriver fresh).\\n- The weak-cue code should be 10 (T025/AC-007 accept 9; the spec text is stale).\\n- A changed assertion is vacuous (each changed case passes its table row into the function).\\n- A changed path reads or prints a holdout row (tune-id selection plus split assertion).\\n\\n### Sources reviewed\\n\\n- `runtime/lib/command-attach.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/fusion.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/doctor-helper-handoff.ts`, `runtime/lib/scorer/projection.ts`, `runtime/handlers/advisor-recommend.ts`.\\n- Six changed test files: `command-attach-guards`, `command-meaning-anchor`, `doctor-helper-handoff`, `advisor-recommend-compiled-route-option`, `doctor-handoff-command`, `typed-command-owner`.\\n- Shared docs: `feature-catalog/cli-surface/advisor-recommend.md`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/command-meaning-matching.md`, `feature-catalog/scorer-fusion/doctor-command-routing.md`, `scripts/command-bridges/README.md`.\\n- Packet docs: `020-command-offer-fit-guards/spec.md`, `acceptance-criteria.md`, `tasks.md`; `024-fable-review-remediation/spec.md`; `review/review-scope-4.txt`; `review/review-brief-4.txt`.\\n- Review doctrine: `sk-code-review/references/review-core.md` §2.\\n\\n### Write discipline\\n\\n- Every file written by this lineage is under `review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/`: four iteration narratives, four deltas, the strategy, the config, the registry, the dashboard, the report, the probe files and the temporary record builders.\\n- No review target, config, generated table, command, skill, agent, renderer or sibling lineage file was modified.\\n- The state log was written only by `append-mode-event.cjs`; the reducer refreshed the registry, dashboard and strategy after each iteration.\\n- No nested CLI, sub-agent or Task dispatch was used. No `generate-context.js`, `validate.sh`, git write or out-of-lineage command was run.\\n\", \"path\": \"specs/system-skill-advisor/routing-and-scoring/008-command-surfacing-build/review/lineages/scorer-attach-4/review-report.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794670920877,"end":1794670921579}}}}
